10679|MRAM|2026-05-11|live|HIGH|115.2|29.68|strong||||1.20|07:00|MRAM stock gapped up over 45% in overnight trading into Monday amid AI-linked momentum in semiconductors, with no fresh company-specific news but strong retail sentiment on Stocktwits turning extremely bullish. The move builds on a more than 100% rise since April 29 quarterly results showing 13% revenue growth to $14.9 million and $0.11 adjusted EPS beating estimates, plus a $40 million defense co|||Everspin Technologies announced a $40M defense/mil-aero MRAM contract (April 30), coupled with Q1 2026 earnings that beat expectations: revenue of $14.87M vs. $13.14M YoY, and a reduced net loss of $296K. The company is also expanding its U.S. manufacturing base and analyst fair value has been raised to $18.00 (vs. prior $12.50 and street target $14.00), indicating significant upside recognition. This combination of a major contract win, earnings beat, and analyst upgrades qualifies as a strong catalyst.|
10680|BW|2026-05-11|live|HIGH|96.0|26.07|strong||||1.00|07:00|BW stock gapped up today ahead of its Q1 2026 earnings report due after market close, with investors betting on potential beats despite bearish analyst outlooks citing ongoing class action lawsuits and legal uncertainty. Recent contract wins like the $35 million power plant maintenance award in February and $13 million boiler cleaning deal in January provided underlying support, but no fresh headl|||The news items are vague and lack concrete catalysts. While BW won a $21M coal-to-gas contract and has a $2.8B backlog, these are not new earnings beats or guidance raises with specific numbers. The earnings announcement headline mentions Q1 results are coming but provides no actual reported EPS, revenue, or guidance figures—only generic forward-looking commentary. The class action lawsuit news is actually negative sentiment. Without verified earnings numbers, specific guidance raises, or a transformative deal announcement, this gap-up lacks a genuine, verifiable catalyst.|
10681|WYFI|2026-05-11|live|MODERATE|51.6|12.99|strong||||1.00|07:00|Bit Digital Inc. (BTBT) holds 27 million WhiteFiber (WYFI) shares valued at around $322.1 million, representing major crypto-linked exposure on its balance sheet. This positioning drove BTBT up 5.59% on May 6 amid Ethereum treasury hype and staking yields, creating torque for WYFI as traders pile into related plays when alt-coins rally. No direct WYFI-specific news, but BTBT's grind from $1.35 to |||WYFI gapped up on a BTIG analyst initiation with a Buy rating and $20 price target (April 10), combined with positive coverage highlighting the company's colocation and cloud services business growth potential. This represents an analyst upgrade cluster on a previously under-covered AI infrastructure/data center play, which qualifies as a strong catalyst for a tech stock in a favorable sector.|
10682|BZH|2026-05-11|live|HIGH|84.0|19.93|strong||||1.00|07:20|No specific news or catalyst found for BZH gapping up today. Recent peer context from Legacy Housing (LEGH) Q1 2026 earnings shows BZH down 1-4% alongside homebuilders like CVCO, HOV, LGIH, DFH amid broader housing softness, with LEGH holding steadier at -0.09%. BZH lacks direct positive triggers in available data.|||Beazer Homes (BZH) reported Q2 2026 earnings with a significant +95.83% EPS beat against expectations, despite a modest -8.61% revenue miss. The company delivered results "right around expectations" on key operating metrics and highlighted strong liquidity with strategic shifts toward to-be-built sales positioning for future growth. This combination of a substantial earnings beat with operational confidence and forward-looking strategy improvements qualifies as a strong catalyst in a cyclical housing stock.|
10683|MNDY|2026-05-11|live|HIGH|100.8|19.16|strong||||1.20|07:20|No gap up catalyst identified for MNDY. Latest news is a class action lawsuit reminder from Rosen Law Firm with a May 11 lead plaintiff deadline for buyers between September 17, 2025, and February 6, 2026, which typically pressures stocks lower. Broader market shows overbought S&P 500 and Nasdaq RSI above 70, extreme greed sentiment, and narrow breadth driven by five tech giants (GOOGL, NVDA, AMZN|||The news items provided are vague, generic, and lack specific catalyst details. The headline "HubSpot and monday.com Shares Are Soaring, What You Need To Know" mentions a gap-up but provides no concrete reason—no specific earnings numbers, guidance figures, dates, or verifiable announcement. The other articles are retrospective commentary and opinion pieces ("Is MNDY a good stock to buy?") rather than actual news catalysts. Without specific earnings beats, guidance raises, or named contracts, this appears to be sector momentum (other software peers reporting strong results) rather than a company-specific catalyst for MNDY itself.|
10684|DRTS|2026-05-11|live|MODERATE|50.4|10.46|strong||||1.20|07:35|DRTS stock gapped up over 1% in overnight trading due to anticipation of interim data from the first three patients in Alpha Tau Medical's U.S. Regain study for Alpha DaRT radiation therapy in recurrent glioblastoma brain cancer. The company is hosting a conference call today to discuss the results. Alpha DaRT uses implanted radium-224 sources for targeted tumor radiation, and the therapy has FDA |||Alpha Tau Medical received Japan regulatory approval for its Alpha DaRT technology and H.C. Wainwright upgraded its price target from $9 to $12 with a Buy rating, citing the approval and upcoming 2026 clinical data readouts. Additionally, the company announced a rolling FDA PMA submission and interim data from the Regain study, representing meaningful regulatory and clinical progress in a clinical-stage biotech. While not a massive earnings beat (company has minimal revenue), the analyst upgrade cluster combined with concrete regulatory approvals (Japan) and FDA advancement constitute a solid catalyst for a biotech stock.|
10844|BZH|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|34.79|mna|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 34.8% gap, 14.3x rvol||The catalyst is an all-cash acquisition proposal from Dream Finders Homes to buy all of Beazer at $25.75/share — a textbook M&A buyout, not an EP momentum setup. The gap is entirely the buyout premium and price will be anchored/capped at the offer, leaving no follow-through trade. Grade mna; the authoritative M&A filter governs.|Dream Finders Homes has submitted an unsolicited proposal to acquire all outstanding shares of Beazer Homes (BZH) in an all-cash transaction at $25.75 per share. This is a classic M&A acquisition scenario — the gap-up is driven entirely by the buyout premium, and the share price will be anchored/capped at the deal offer price of $25.75. There is no momentum trade available; this is a hard skip as an EP candidate.|[Benzinga 2026-05-11] Dream Finders Homes Submits Proposal To Beazer Homes Board To Acquire All Outstanding Shares Of Beazer In All-Cash Transaction At $25.75/Shr.
10845|MRAM|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|33.76|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 33.8% gap, 44.2x rvol||The only grounded item is a generic Benzinga "$100 invested 5 years ago" retrospective — boilerplate filler with zero concrete company-specific catalyst (no earnings, contract, guidance, or upgrade). A 34% gap alone is just the market's vote, never sufficient for HIGH without a real material reason. Sharing a broad semiconductor sector with AI data-center cohorts does not constitute joining their actual story, so no theme/narrative axis fires.|The only available news item is a Benzinga retrospective article asking how much a $100 investment in Everspin Technologies 5 years ago would be worth today — this is a generic, non-event article with no specific catalyst (no earnings numbers, no guidance, no contract, no upgrade). There is no concrete, verifiable company-specific catalyst in the provided news to explain the gap-up. This type of filler article frequently appears without driving any real event, and the gap-up cannot be attributed to a material fundamental development based on the available information.|[Benzinga 2026-05-01] Here's How Much $100 Invested In Everspin Technologies 5 Years Ago Would Be Worth Today.
10846|HTCO|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|66.0|20.21|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 20.2% gap, 4.1x rvol||The only "catalyst" is a corporate governance restructuring that boosts insider Class B voting power, balloons authorized share capital, and pre-authorizes a reverse split up to 1,000:1 — dilution/control measures, not value-creating events, with no earnings, contract, or M&A. The debt repayment is mildly positive but immaterial, and the catalyst joins no active narrative cohort (the AI/data-center themes are unrelated to ocean shipping). A gap on a boilerplate small-cap PR with no concrete fundamental driver is routine, so I demote off the HIGH floor.|The catalyst here is a corporate governance restructuring announcement — Class B voting rights were boosted from 20 to 100 votes per share, authorized share capital was massively expanded (from ~$1.25M to ~$5.275M), and the board was granted authority to do a reverse split up to 1,000:1. There is no earnings beat, no revenue/EPS figures, no new contract, no FDA decision, and no M&A deal. These governance changes primarily consolidate insider control and expand the share count, which is not a value-creating catalyst. The debt repayment news (Streeterville Capital) is mildly positive but immaterial relative to the overall picture. No concrete, verifiable catalyst explains a legitimate gap-up here — this reads as a low-quality press release from a small-cap (~$50M) stock with no fundamental driver.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-11, items ] EX-99.1 3 ea029005001ex99-1.htm PRESS RELEASE DATED MAY 11, 2026 Exhibit 99.1 High-Trend International Group Class A Shareholders Approve Major Corporate Governance Enhancements NEW YORK, May 11, 2026 /PRNewswire/ &ndash; High-Trend International Group (NASDAQ: HTCO) (&#8220;HTCO&#8221; or the &#8220;Company&#8221;), global ocean transportation company, today announced that the Company&#8217;s Class A shareholders approved a series of transformative corporate governance measures at an Extraordinary General Meeting held on May 7, 2026. The approved resolutions include a significant enhancement of voting rights attached to the Company&#8217;s Class B ordinary shares, a substantial increase in authorized share capital and the authorization of potential future share consolidations. Key Shareholder Approvals: Enhanced Class B Voting Rights: Class A shareholders approved a special resolution to increase the voting rights attached to each Class B ordinary share from twenty votes to one hundred votes on all matters subject to a vote at general meetings of the Company. Increased Authorized Share Capital: Class A shareholders approved an expansion of the Company&#8217;s authorized share capital from US$1,250,000 to US$5,275,250, increasing the number of authorized Class A ordinary shares from 489,900,000 to 2,000,000,000 and Class B ordinary shares from 10,100,000 to 110,100,000. Share Consolidation Authorization: Shareholders granted the Company&#8217;s Board of Directors discretionary authority to consolidate the Company&#8217;s issued and outstanding Class A ordinary shares at any time during a period of up to two years, provided that the accumulative consolidation ratio shall not exceed 1,000:1. The Board of Directors will retain full discretion on whether to implement any such consolidation, as well as the exact ratio and effective date. Amended Memorandum and Articles of Association: Shareholders approved the adoption of the Fourth Amended and Restated Memorandum and Articles of Association, which reflect the above changes and additionally established that certain major corporate actions will be subject to the prior written consent of the Majority of the holders Class B ordinary shares. &#8220;These shareholder approvals represent a pivotal milestone in High-Trend International Group&#8217;s corporate evolution,&#8221; said Mr. Christopher Nixon Cox, Chairman of the Company. &#8220;The enhanced governance framework and expanded capital structure provide the Company with greater strategic flexibility to pursue growth initiatives, strengthen our balance sheet, and create long-term value for all stakeholders. We remain committed to executing our vision as a leading global ocean technology company.&#8221; About High-Trend International Group High-Trend International Group is a global ocean transportation company with core businesses in international shipping. Forward-Looking Statements This press release contains forwar
10847|MNDY|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|18.65|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 18.6% gap, 5.5x rvol||Real, material catalyst: a clean Q1 beat (rev +24%, EPS $1.15 vs $0.93 est) plus a raised FY guide and record large-ARR net adds, with an AI Work Platform launch adding a strategic narrative layer. The 18.6% gap is well-supported by concrete company-specific results rather than sector drift or a squeeze. The guidance raise is only modest (~$14M on a $4.1B cap), so the AI-agent narrative keeps this solidly strong but short of game_changer.|monday.com reported Q1 2026 results with revenue of $351.3M (+24% YoY), beating estimates of $339.2M by ~$12M, and non-GAAP EPS of $1.15 vs. the $0.93 estimate — a massive ~24% EPS beat. The company also raised full-year 2026 revenue guidance to $1.466B–$1.474B (from $1.452B–$1.462B), topping the $1.458B consensus, alongside record GAAP and non-GAAP operating income and record net adds of large-ARR customers (the $500K+ ARR cohort grew 74% YoY). The AI Work Platform launch with native agents adds a strategic growth narrative on top of the financial beat, but the guidance raise is modest (~$14M at midpoint on a $4.1B market cap), keeping this solidly strong rather than a game-changer.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-11, items ] EX-99.1 2 exhibit_99-1.htm EXHIBIT 99.1 Exhibit 99.1 monday.com Announces First Quarter 2026 Results First quarter revenue of $351.3 million grew 24% year-over-year Record GAAP and non-GAAP operating income Record net adds of customers with more than $500,000 in ARR Launches AI Work Platform with Native Agents New York / Tel Aviv, May 11, 2026 -- monday.com (NASDAQ: MNDY), the AI work platform that turns strategy into execution, at scale, today reported financial results for its first quarter ended March 31, 2026. Management Commentary: &#8220;The results we delivered in Q1 reflect a business that is executing with discipline and building with ambition at the same time,&#8221; said monday.com co-founders and co-CEOs Roy Mann and Eran Zinman. &#8220;The launch of the AI Work Platform and our shift to consumption-based pricing build directly on that momentum. As AI takes on more work for our customers, our business grows with it. We believe the best chapter of monday.com&#8217;s story is the one we are writing now.&#8221; &#8220;Q1 was a strong quarter across every financial dimension, with revenue, margins and cash flow all coming in ahead of expectations,&#8221; said Eliran Glazer, monday.com CFO. &#8220;Perhaps most encouragingly, the AI productivity gains we are seeing inside our own organization are demonstrating that we can grow revenue without growing headcount in lockstep, a dynamic we believe will be a meaningful driver of operating leverage over time.&#8221; First Quarter Fiscal 2026 Financial Highlights: &#9679; Revenue was $351.3 million, an increase of 24% year-over-year. &#9679; GAAP operating income was $19.8 million, compared to $9.8 million in the first quarter of 2025; GAAP operating margin was 6%, compared to 3% in the first quarter of 2025. &#9679; Non-GAAP operating income was $49.0 million, compared to $40.8 million in the first quarter of 2025. Non-GAAP operating margin was 14%, same as in the first quarter of 2025, despite an approximately 190 basis point negative impact from FX. &#9679; GAAP basic and diluted net income per share was $0.58 and $0.57, respectively, compared to GAAP basic and diluted net income per share of $0.54 and $0.52, respectively, in the first quarter of 2025; non-GAAP basic and diluted net income per share was $1.17 and $1.15, respectively, compared to non-GAAP basic and diluted net income per share of $1.14 and $1.10, respectively, in the first quarter of 2025. &#9679; Net cash provided by operating activities was $104.7 million, with $102.8 million of adjusted free cash flow, compared to net cash provided by operating activities of $112.0 million and $109.5 million of adjusted free cash flow in the first quarter of 2025. Recent Business Highlights: &#9679; Net dollar retention rate was 110%. &#9679; Net dollar retention rate for customers with more than 10 users was 114%. &#9679; Net dollar retention rate for customers with more than $50,000 in ARR was 116%. &#9679
10848|BW|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|39.6|14.86|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 14.9% gap, 3.5x rvol||The only disclosed event is a Reg FD 8-K posting a boilerplate investor overview deck — no earnings, contract, guidance, or M&A, so there is no real catalyst to support HIGH. The filing actually flags going-concern and 2026 note-refinancing risks, the opposite of a positive driver. The name does not join any active narrative cohort (no shared data-center/power story is grounded), so the ~15% gap is unexplained/speculative and stays routine.|The only news identified is a Form 8-K (Items 7.01/9.01) filed on May 11, 2026, disclosing that Babcock & Wilcox posted a general investor presentation on its IR website. There are no earnings results, no EPS or revenue figures, no guidance raise, no contract win, no analyst upgrade, and no M&A activity present in the filing. The investor presentation itself contains only boilerplate forward-looking language and company overview material — no specific, verifiable catalyst that would justify a significant gap-up. This appears to be either a speculative/sector-driven move or a catalyst that is not identifiable from the available news.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-11, items 7.01,9.01] bw-20260511 0001630805 FALSE 0001630805 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 0001630805 us-gaap:CommonStockMember 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 0001630805 bw:SeniorNotes650Due2026Member 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 0001630805 us-gaap:SeriesAPreferredStockMember 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15 (d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 11, 2026 BABCOCK & WILCOX ENTERPRISES, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-36876 47-2783641 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 1200 East Market Street Suite 650 Akr