10851|INBX|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|75.6|11.65|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 11.6% gap, 3.5x rvol||Positive RANDOMIZED Phase 2 interim data for INBRX-106 in first-line PD-L1+ HNSCC vs a pembrolizumab control is a concrete, mechanism-validating clinical catalyst that is transformative for a $1.3B clinical-stage biopharma with no approved products. It is a real material event (sales-acceleration/new-product tier in Pradeep's hierarchy, the strongest a single-asset biotech gets) and clears the HIGH bar on catalyst alone. I hold tier HIGH but demote game_changer→strong: interim (not topline registrational) data with no Lane 1/Lane 2 theme tailwind and a moderate ~12% gap doesn't justify the top|The specific catalyst is the announcement of positive interim Phase 2 data for INBRX-106 (a hexavalent OX40 agonist) in combination with pembrolizumab versus pembrolizumab monotherapy in first-line PD-L1 positive metastatic/unresectable recurrent Head and Neck Squamous Cell Carcinoma (HNSCC) — a large and competitive oncology indication. For a clinical-stage biopharma with a $1.3B market cap and no approved products, a randomized Phase 2 trial showing positive results in a first-line setting against a pembrolizumab monotherapy control arm is a transformative, company-defining event. Positive randomized data in first-line HNSCC validates the mechanism and significantly de-risks the program, potentially setting up a registration-enabling trial and partnership discussions.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-11, items 7.01,8.01,9.01] inhibrx-20260511 FALSE 0002007919 0002007919 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 11, 2026 INHIBRX BIOSCIENCES, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-42031 99-0613523 (State or other jurisdiction of 