10853|NVEC|2026-05-11|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|10.83|strong|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.8% gap, 4.6x rvol||The catalyst is a routine quarterly earnings report plus a maintained (not raised) $1.00 dividend — bottom of the Pradeep hierarchy and largely a stable, mature-business event. The 27% net income jump rode mostly on a flat ~2% revenue line and an unchanged dividend, so there's no transformative or accelerating story to promote a $530M name, and NVEC joins none of the active AI/semiconductor narrative cohorts (spintronics sensors are not the data-center buildout story). A genuine but unremarkable beat with no guidance uplift caps this at routine.|NVE Corporation reported Q4 fiscal 2026 earnings with net income surging 27% YoY to $4.93M ($1.02/diluted share) vs. $0.80/share in the prior-year quarter, on a 5% revenue increase to $7.65M — a meaningful earnings beat for this small-cap. The company also maintained its $1.00/share quarterly cash dividend, signaling financial confidence. With two consecutive quarters of strong revenue and earnings growth cited by management, and no guidance raise explicitly provided, this is a solid beat but falls short of game-changer territory given the modest revenue scale (~$26M annually) and lack of forward guidance uplift.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-06, items 2.02,8.01] NVE Corp - Form 8-K SEC filing 0000724910 false 0000724910 2026-05-06 2026-05-06 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported) May 6, 2026 NVE Corp oration (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Minnesota 000-12196 41-1424202 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 11409 Valley View Road , Eden Prairie , Minnesota 55344 ( Address of principal executive offices ) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone num