10859|HTCO|2026-05-12|historical_scan|HIGH|72.0|24.82|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 24.8% gap, 30.5x rvol||The "transformative" deal-size ratio is a mirage: it is an authorized-share-capital expansion (489.9M→2B) plus enhanced Class B voting rights and up-to-1,000:1 consolidation authority — dilution/control mechanics, not a revenue, contract, or earnings event. No concrete fundamental driver exists to sustain momentum on this $47M micro-cap, and the setup joins no active narrative cohort. This is boilerplate governance PR dressed in superlatives; demote from the HIGH floor to routine.|The catalyst here is a shareholder-approved corporate governance overhaul: enhanced Class B voting rights (20→100 votes/share), a massive expansion of authorized share capital (Class A shares 489.9M→2B), and authorization of a potential up to 1,000:1 share consolidation. While the press release uses words like "transformative" and "pivotal milestone," none of these actions represent a concrete earnings beat, revenue event, new contract, or genuine business development. The authorized share capital increase and consolidation authority are actually dilution-risk signals for retail investors rather than value-creating catalysts. There is no verifiable fundamental driver — no earnings figures, no guidance raise, no named deal — that would justify a sustained momentum move on a $49M micro-cap.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-11, items ] EX-99.1 3 ea029005001ex99-1.htm PRESS RELEASE DATED MAY 11, 2026 Exhibit 99.1 High-Trend International Group Class A Shareholders Approve Major Corporate Governance Enhancements NEW YORK, May 11, 2026 /PRNewswire/ &ndash; High-Trend International Group (NASDAQ: HTCO) (&#8220;HTCO&#8221; or the &#8220;Company&#8221;), global ocean transportation company, today announced that the Company&#8217;s Class A shareholders approved a series of transformative corporate governance measures at an Extraordinary General Meeting held on May 7, 2026. The approved resolutions include a significant enhancement of voting rights attached to the Company&#8217;s Class B ordinary shares, a substantial increase in authorized share capital and the authorization of potential future share consolidations. Key Shareholder Approvals: Enhanced Class B Voting Rights: Class A shareholders approved a special resolution to increase the voting rights attached to each Class B ordinary share from twenty votes to one hundred votes on all matters subject to a vote at general meetings of the Company. Increased Authorized Share Capital: Class A shareholders approved an expansion of the Company&#8217;s authorized share capital from US$1,250,000 to US$5,275,250, increasing the number of authorized Class A ordinary shares from 489,900,000 to 2,000,000,000 and Class B ordinary shares from 10,100,000 to 110,100,000. Share Consolidation Authorization: Shareholders granted the Company&#8217;s Board of Directors discretionary authority to consolidate the Company&#8217;s issued and outstanding Class A ordinary shares at any time during a period of up to two years, provided that the accumulative consolidation ratio shall not exceed 1,000:1. The Board of Directors will retain full discretion on whether to implement any such consolidation, as well as the exact ratio and effective date. Amended Memorandum and Articles of Association: Shareholders approved the adoption of the Fourth Amended and Restated Memorandum and Articles of Association, which reflect the above changes and additionally established that certain major corporate actions will be subject to the prior written consent of the Majority of the holders Class B ordinary shares. &#8220;These shareholder approvals represent a pivotal milestone in High-Trend International Group&#8217;s corporate evolution,&#8221; said Mr. Christopher Nixon Cox, Chairman of the Company. &#8220;The enhanced governance framework and expanded capital structure provide the Company with greater strategic flexibility to pursue growth initiatives, strengthen our balance sheet, and create long-term value for all stakeholders. We remain committed to executing our vision as a leading global ocean technology company.&#8221; About High-Trend International Group High-Trend International Group is a global ocean transportation company with core businesses in international shipping. Forward-Looking Statements This press release contains forwar
10860|QUBT|2026-05-12|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|24.75|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 24.8% gap, 10.9x rvol||Concrete, verifiable earnings catalyst: revenue jumped ~95x YoY ($39K to $3.7M) with two completed bolt-on acquisitions (LSI, NuCrypt) advancing the roadmap and a $1.4B cash cushion that de-risks dilution for a $2.2B name. Revenue is still tiny in absolute terms and no guidance was raised, so this is sales-acceleration tier rather than transformative, and it is the company's own event rather than joining an active quantum/photonics narrative cohort. Real material catalyst plus 25% gap supports HIGH/strong but the thin absolute revenue and lack of theme/narrative tailwind cap it short of game_c|QUBT reported Q1 2026 earnings with revenue of $3.7 million, a massive surge from just $39 thousand in Q1 2025 — representing roughly a 95x year-over-year increase. The company also completed two strategic acquisitions (Luminar Semiconductor and NuCrypt) and ended the quarter with $1.4 billion in cash. While the company remains pre-profitability, the explosive revenue growth from near-zero is a concrete, verifiable catalyst with specific figures, and the strong balance sheet reduces dilution risk — making this a solid EP setup, though no formal guidance raise was disclosed.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-11, items 2.02,9.01] false 0001758009 0001758009 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 11, 2026 QUANTUM COMPUTING INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-40615 82-4533053 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 5 Marine View Plaza , Suite 214 Hoboken , NJ 07030 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) Reg