10861|PACS|2026-05-12|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|21.00|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 21.0% gap, 5.1x rvol||Concrete, verified Q1 earnings catalyst: net income +184% to $80.7M and Adjusted EBITDA +74.6%, with occupancy (90.8% vs ~79% industry) and skilled-mix gains confirming an operational beat, not boilerplate. The beat is material on a $5.5B cap and the 21% gap reflects real surprise, though a chunk is a one-time $16.3M WQIP benefit, capping it at strong rather than game_changer. No active theme/narrative tie-in (post-acute SNF unrelated to the AI/semis cohorts), so only the catalyst axis fires.|PACS reported Q1 2026 earnings with revenue of $1.42B (+11.2% YoY), net income surging 184.2% to $80.7M, and Adjusted EBITDA of $170.4M (+74.6% YoY) — a massive bottom-line beat driven by operational improvement and a $16.3M WQIP benefit not included in prior guidance. Occupancy of 90.8% significantly outpaces the industry average of ~79%, and same-store SNF revenue grew 8.0% with improving skilled mix. The scale of the earnings beat (net income nearly tripling) and strong operational KPIs on a $5.5B market-cap company represent a clear, verifiable, and material positive catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-11, items 2.02,9.01] pacs-20260511 false 0002001184 0002001184 2026-05-11 2026-05-11 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 11, 2026 PACS GROUP, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-42011 92-3144268 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification Number) 90 S. 400 W. Suite 700 Salt Lake City , Utah 84101 (Address of principal executive offices, including Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: ( 801 ) 447-9829 Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing 