10864|KOPN|2026-05-12|historical_scan|HIGH|72.0|13.88|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.9% gap, 5.9x rvol||KOPN announced a concrete, transformative catalyst: a Fabric.AI strategic collaboration to build MicroLED optical interconnects replacing copper between GPUs in AI data centers, backed by a $15M development order and a 19.9% equity stake, opening a multi-billion-dollar TAM that dwarfs its ~$10.6M quarterly revenue — and it directly joins the active "AI data center infrastructure demand" narrative. A $21.5M follow-on thermal contract (2x quarterly revenue) adds material support. I hold HIGH but demote from game_changer to strong because the deal is a development order and equity stake rather th|The primary catalyst is a transformative strategic collaboration with Fabric.AI to jointly develop Neural I/o™, a MicroLED-based optical interconnect technology for AI data centers, backed by a $15M initial development order and a 19.9% equity stake in Fabric.AI — opening a multi-billion-dollar addressable market that dwarfs KOPN's current revenue scale. Secondarily, a $21.5M follow-on thermal imaging production contract was awarded, which is highly material relative to KOPN's ~$10.6M quarterly revenue run rate. Q1 2026 revenues came in essentially flat YoY at $10.6M vs $10.5M with a massive 292% surge in Non-Product revenues, signaling the company's business mix is shifting toward high-value R&D and collaborative agreements — together these catalysts represent a fundamental business transformation for a ~$889M market cap company.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-12, items 2.02,9.01] false 0000771266 0000771266 2026-05-12 2026-05-12 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, DC 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of Earliest Event Reported) May 12, 2026 KOPIN CORPORATION (Exact Name of Registrant as Specified