10865|HLIT|2026-05-12|historical_scan|HIGH|50.4|13.41|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.4% gap, 8.7x rvol||Concrete, SEC-verified company-specific catalyst: Q1 Broadband revenue +43% YoY (78% Rest-of-Market), record backlog +87% to $582M, plus a full-year guidance raise to $475-495M — sales acceleration on the core growth engine for a $1.5B name. The pending Video-business sale is a divestiture, not an acquisition of HLIT, so M&A does not apply and the company keeps its momentum. No active theme/narrative match (data-center cohorts share sector but not this broadband/cable story), so theme axis stays dark, but the beat+raise is material enough to promote from the MODERATE floor to HIGH.|Harmonic reported Q1 2026 results with Broadband revenue up 43% YoY (including 78% Rest-of-Market growth), beating expectations, with backlog/deferred revenue surging 87% YoY to $582M — a record. The company also raised its full-year 2026 Broadband revenue outlook to $475M–$495M, a meaningful guidance raise. While there is a pending sale of the Video business to MediaKind, this is a divestiture (not an acquisition of HLIT), so the company retains its independence and trading momentum. The combination of strong beat + guidance raise on the core Broadband growth engine is a clear, verifiable, company-specific catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-11, items 2.02,9.01] 8-K false 0000851310 0000851310 2026-05-06 2026-05-06 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 6, 2026 HARMONIC INC. (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 000-25826 77-0201147 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) Commission File Number (IRS Employer Identification No.) 2590 Orchard Parkway San Jose , CA 95131 (Address of principal executive offices, including zip code) ( 408 ) 542-2500 (Registrant&#8