10866|WEN|2026-05-12|historical_scan|HIGH|42.0|12.57|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.6% gap, 7.2x rvol||The Q1 print is weak — global systemwide sales -5.5%, U.S. same-restaurant sales -7.8%, only $0.12 EPS, and no guidance raise (just a reaffirmation) — so the gap reads as a sentiment/relief move, not a fundamental beat. The China headline (up to 1,000 restaurants over 10 years) is a long-dated franchise agreement with no near-term revenue and is not material enough to transform a $1.3B turnaround business. No active theme/narrative match (the live cohorts are AI-data-center/semis, unrelated to fast food), so nothing lights the theme or narrative axes.|Wendy's reported Q1 2026 earnings with global systemwide sales down 5.5% YoY to $3.2B, U.S. same-restaurant sales down a steep 7.8%, and adjusted EPS of just $0.12. The company did announce a notable franchise agreement to build up to 1,000 restaurants in China over 10 years, but no guidance raise was issued — only a reaffirmation of full-year 2026 outlook. While the China deal is a positive headline, it is a long-term franchise agreement (not immediate revenue) from a company with a $1.3B market cap in an early-stage turnaround, and the underlying results reflect a business under significant pressure with no meaningful beat.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-08, items 2.02,9.01] 8-K Wendy's Co false 0000030697 0000030697 2026-05-08 2026-05-08 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, DC 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of Earliest Event Reported): May 8, 2026 THE WENDY&#8217;S COMPANY (Exact name of registrant, as specified in its charter) Delaware 1-2207 38-0471180 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) One Dave Thomas Boulevard , Dublin , Ohio 43017 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) (614) 764-3100 (Registrant&#821