10696|EOSE|2026-05-13|live|HIGH|115.2|31.11|strong||||1.20|07:00|EOSE gapped up due to a Joint Development Agreement with Turbine-X Energy for on-site power infrastructure targeting hyperscale AI data centers, combining gas-fired turbines with up to 2 GWh of Eos's zinc-based Indensity battery storage over three years, with first deployments in 2027. The deal news drove a 10-14% intraday surge on May 11, following a 22.4% jump to $7.79 on May 8 amid AI power dem|||Eos Energy Enterprises announced a joint development deal with Turbine-X Energy to pair zinc-based battery storage with gas-fired power for large-scale AI data centers. This is a major strategic partnership targeting the high-growth AI infrastructure market, representing a significant expansion into a new, high-value customer segment. The partnership addresses critical infrastructure needs and validates Eos's technology for enterprise-scale applications beyond traditional utility markets.|
10697|AIP|2026-05-13|live|HIGH|115.2|20.81|strong||||1.20|07:00|Arteris Inc (AIP) gapped up ahead of its fiscal Q1 2026 earnings release due May 12, following a multi-month breakout fueled by its MIPS collaboration announcement that drove 60% gains in 30 days. High-margin 92% gross margins in fiscal Q4 2025 and 22% YoY full-year revenue growth to $70.6 million position it as an AI training workloads play in semiconductors, with each GPU cluster needing its IP |||Arteris (AIP) reported Q1 2026 earnings with record revenue, delivering a +62.50% EPS beat and +8.70% revenue beat versus estimates. Management highlighted strong demand from AI chips, data center infrastructure, and automotive systems—all secular growth drivers. While the company posted a net loss, the earnings surprise and revenue growth trajectory on a neglected semiconductor IP stock constitutes a strong catalyst for the gap-up.|
10867|EOSU|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|62.4|49.63|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 49.6% gap, 7.1x rvol||EOSU is a 2X leveraged ETF tracking EOSE, not an operating company, so its 49.6% gap is pure derivative price action with no independent company-specific catalyst. No earnings, contract, policy, or theme story attaches to the instrument itself, and it joins no active narrative cohort. A catalyst is required for HIGH; this is mechanical leverage, so it demotes to routine/none.|EOSU is a leveraged 2X ETF that tracks EOSE (Eos Energy Enterprises) — it is a derivative instrument, not an operating company, so any gap-up is purely a function of price movement in the underlying EOSE stock. No news was found for EOSU itself, and no concrete, verifiable catalyst (earnings, FDA, contract, upgrade) has been identified. The gap-up reflects leveraged exposure to EOSE's price action, which is a non-company-specific, technical/momentum move with no independent catalyst.|
10868|NEBX|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|29.42|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 29.4% gap, 2.6x rvol||NEBX is a 2x leveraged daily ETF tracking NBIS, so its 29% gap is purely mechanical amplification of the underlying's move, not a discrete company-specific catalyst. There is no real, material event for NEBX itself — gap+volume alone never earns HIGH, and a derivative structural move is not a tradeable EP. Holds at floor (none/routine).|NEBX is a 2x leveraged daily ETF that tracks NBIS (Nebius Group), meaning its gap-up is entirely derivative of movement in the underlying NBIS stock — there is no independent company-specific catalyst for NEBX itself. No news was found for this ticker, confirming the move is purely mechanical leverage amplification of NBIS's price action. This is not a tradeable EP catalyst; the gap reflects the ETF's structure, not a discrete fundamental event.|
10869|NBIG|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|27.73|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 27.7% gap, 2.6x rvol||NBIG is a 2x leveraged ETF on NBIS, so the 27.7% gap is a purely mechanical derivative of the underlying's move with no company-specific catalyst for NBIG itself. There is no real, material event — the requirement for any HIGH/promotion fails outright. Any tradeable momentum belongs to the underlying NBIS, not this wrapper.|NBIG is a 2X leveraged ETF tracking NBIS (Nebius Group), meaning any gap-up in NBIG is purely a derivative move of NBIS's price action — not a company-specific catalyst for NBIG itself. No news was found for NBIG, and there is no independent catalyst; the move is entirely mechanical (2x daily leverage on the underlying). This is not a tradeable EP setup on NBIG — any momentum belongs to the underlying NBIS, not this ETF wrapper.|
10870|NBIL|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|27.68|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 27.7% gap, 2.7x rvol||NBIL is a 2x leveraged daily ETF tracking NBIS, not an operating company, so the gap is a derivative/technical reflection of the underlying — there is no company-specific catalyst (no earnings, contract, policy, or shortage event) tied to this instrument. A gap alone never earns HIGH, and here no real catalyst exists at all. No active narrative cohort is joined by an actual shared story.|NBIL is a 2x leveraged daily ETF tracking NBIS (Nebius Group), not an operating company with its own catalysts. No news was found to explain the gap-up, and any price movement is simply a leveraged reflection of the underlying stock NBIS moving up — not a company-specific catalyst. There is no earnings release, guidance raise, FDA decision, contract, or any other concrete event tied to this ETF itself; the gap is purely derivative/technical in nature.|
10871|WOLF|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|72.0|24.03|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 24.0% gap, 6.9x rvol||The "catalyst" is a relief bounce after weak Q3 results and soft Q4 guidance ($140M–$160M) — a dead-cat snap-back, not a positive fundamental event, so it fails the REAL-material-catalyst requirement for HIGH. No beat, no guidance raise, no transformative news, and the SiC sector tie does not match either active edge-AI or data-center-power narrative's specific story. A 24% gap on negative earnings is the market's vote without a supporting reason, so demote to routine/none.|The specific catalyst is a bounce/relief rally following Wolfspeed's Q3 2026 earnings release, but the results were decidedly weak — the news explicitly states "weak Q3 financials" and "soft fourth-quarter guidance" (Q4 revenue guided at $140M–$160M). The gap-up appears to be a technical dead-cat bounce or oversold snap-back after a prior sharp selloff on bad earnings, not a positive fundamental catalyst. There is no earnings beat, no guidance raise, and no transformative event — the stock is simply recovering from an exaggerated prior drop on disappointing results.|[Benzinga 2026-05-06] Wolfspeed Stock Surges Despite Weak Q3 Financials. Wolfspeed Inc (NYSE: WOLF) shares are bouncing Wednesday after sharp drop on weak third-quarter results and soft fourth-quarter guidance. [Benzinga 2026-05-05] Full Transcript: Wolfspeed Q3 2026 Earnings Call. [Benzinga 2026-05-05] Wolfspeed Sees Q4 Sales $140.000M-$160.000M.
10872|EOSE|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|23.09|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 23.1% gap, 6.0x rvol||Multi-layered real catalyst: a Cerberus JV (Frontier Power USA) with a $100M equity contribution and 2 GWh firm capacity reservation, paired with 445% YoY revenue growth ($57M) and reaffirmed $300-400M FY guidance — clearly material for a $2.1B LDES name. This is a JV formation, not a buyout of EOSE, so the M&A filter does not apply. No active theme/narrative cohort matches the LDES storage story, so theme/narrative axes stay dark, holding it at strong HIGH rather than promoting to game_changer.|EOSE reported Q1 2026 revenue of $57.0M, a 445% year-over-year increase, while reaffirming full-year 2026 revenue guidance of $300M–$400M. Simultaneously, the company announced the formation of "Frontier Power USA," a joint venture with Cerberus Capital Management that includes a $100M equity contribution and a 2 GWh firm capacity reservation agreement — materially significant relative to EOSE's revenue run-rate. The combination of explosive revenue growth, guidance reaffirmation, record production milestones, and a major strategic JV partnership with a credible institutional backer (Cerberus) constitutes a strong, multi-layered catalyst. Note: this is a JV formation, not an acquisition of EOSE, so it is not an M&A cap event.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-13, items 1.01,2.02,3.02,7.01,9.01] eose-20260512 0001805077 FALSE 0001805077 2026-05-12 2026-05-12 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(d) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 12, 2026 EOS ENERGY ENTERPRISES, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-39291 84-4290188 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 3920 Park Avenue Edison , New Jersey 08820 (Address of principal executive offices, including zip code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: ( 732 ) 225-8400 N/A (Former name or former address, if changed since last report) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common stock, par value $0.0001 per share EOSE The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; 1 Item 1.01 Entry into a Material Definitive Agreement. On May 12, 2026, Eos Energy Enterprises Inc. (the &#8220; Company &#8221;) entered into a binding term sheet (the &#8220; Term Sheet &#8221;) with CCM Frontier JV Holdco, LLC, an affiliate of Cerberus Capital Management, L.P. (&#8220; CCM Frontier &#8221;), which provides for, upon the closing of the transactions contemplated by the Term Sheet, the formation of a joint venture between the Company and CCM Frontier through Frontier Power USA Parent, LLC, a Delaware limited liability company (the &#8220; JV Company &#8221;). CCM Frontier and the Company expect to enter into definitive written agreements with respect to the transactions contemplated by the Term Sheet prior to the closing of such transactions. Equity Ownership At or prior to the closing of the transactions contempla
10873|VNET|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|22.51|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 22.5% gap, 13.0x rvol||A CATL-affiliated consortium acquiring up to 38.1% of VNET at $8.6914/ADS is a concrete, material strategic catalyst that signals deep institutional confidence in this $2.5B China data-center operator — credible and specific, not boilerplate. This is a secondary share purchase (control stays with the founder via the voting agreement), so it is a strategic-investment catalyst rather than a buyout, correctly NOT classified as M&A. It taps the live AI/data-center power & infrastructure narrative through a battery/energy-infrastructure backer, supporting HIGH at strong without rising to game_chang|The catalyst is the announcement of a major strategic investment by PJ Millennium I & II Limited (affiliates of CATL — Contemporary Amperex Technology Co., Limited, a global battery giant) purchasing up to 650,424,192 Class A ordinary shares at $8.6914 per ADS, which would give the buyers ~38.1% of VNET's total shares outstanding. This is NOT a traditional M&A/acquisition where the company is being taken private or fully acquired — it is a secondary share purchase between existing sellers and new strategic investors, with the company remaining publicly listed and independent. The deal brings a powerful, high-profile strategic backer (CATL-affiliated) into VNET, signaling strong institutional confidence and potential future business synergies in China's data center/AI infrastructure space, representing a material and credible catalyst for a $2.5B market cap company.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-13, items ] EX-99.1 2 tm2614496d1_ex99-1.htm EXHIBIT 99.1 Exhibit 99.1 VNET Announces New Strategic Investors BEIJING, May 13, 2026 -- VNET Group, Inc. (Nasdaq: VNET) (&ldquo;VNET&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), a leading carrier- and cloud-neutral internet data center services provider in China, today announced that PJ Millennium I Limited (&ldquo;Buyer I&rdquo;) and PJ Millennium II Limited (&ldquo;Buyer II&rdquo;, together with &ldquo;Buyer I&rdquo;, the &ldquo;Buyers&rdquo;) have entered into a share purchase agreement (the &ldquo;Share Purchase Agreement&rdquo;) with Success Flow International Investment Limited (&ldquo;Success Flow&rdquo;) and Choice Faith Group Holdings Limited (&ldquo;Choice Faith&rdquo;, together with &ldquo;Success Flow&rdquo;, the &ldquo;Sellers&rdquo;) to purchase from the Sellers in aggregate up to 650,424,192 Class A ordinary shares in the Company (the &ldquo;Proposed Investment&rdquo;), at a price of US$1.4486 per ordinary share in cash (which is equivalent to US$8.6914 per ADS). VNET also entered into a deed with the Buyers to provide certain representations and warranties and undertakings to the Buyers in connection with the Proposed Investment. The closing of the Proposed Investment is subject to conditions set forth in the Share Purchase Agreement, including approval by the shareholders of SDHG (as defined below), and is expected to take place in the fourth quarter of 2026. Both Buyers are wholly-owned subsidiaries of PJ Millennium Limited Partnership (&ldquo;PJ Millennium Partnership&rdquo;). The general partner of PJ Millennium Partnership is Lochpine BG I GP Limited, which is a non-controlled and non-consolidated affiliate of Contemporary Amperex Technology Co., Limited (stock codes: 300750.SZ and 03750.HK). Both Sellers are beneficially owned by Shandong Hi-Speed Holdings Group Limited ( &ldquo;SDHG&rdquo;) (stock code: 00412.HK). Immediately after the closing of the Proposed Investment, the Buyers will hold in aggregate approximately up to 38.1% of the total issued and outstanding shares of the Company, based on 1,708,149,858 ordinary shares issued and outstanding as of March 31, 2026. Under the Share Purchase Agreement, Seller B may dispose of up to 195,127,260 Class A ordinary shares held by it before the closing of the Proposed Investment, unless the Buyers require the closing in respect of all of such Class A ordinary shares to take place on or before September 15, 2026, subject to the terms and conditions of the Share Purchase Agreement. Concurrently with the signing of the Share Purchase Agreement, the Buyers entered into an investor rights agreement with the Company (the &ldquo;Investor Rights Agreement&rdquo;) and a voting and consortium agreement (the &ldquo;Voting and Consortium Agreement&rdquo;) with Mr. Josh Sheng Chen, Founder, Executive Chairperson and Interim Chief Executive Officer of VNET, and certain affiliated investment vehicles (collectively, the &ldquo;Fou
10874|SLS|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|20.98|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 21.0% gap, 7.8x rvol||For a late-stage clinical biotech with no revenue, the imminent pivotal Phase 3 REGAL binary readout (78 of 80 required events reached, final analysis days away) is the highest-magnitude catalyst type possible and is genuinely transformative relative to a $1.5B clinical-stage shell. However, the company remains blinded — this is anticipation of an event, not the event/data itself — so it falls short of game_changer, which would require the actual positive topline result. No active theme or narrative cohort supports it, so the grade rests purely on the catalyst axis.|The specific catalyst is the imminent Phase 3 REGAL trial data readout for galinpepimut-S (GPS) in AML: the independent CRO confirmed 78 of the required 80 pre-specified events have occurred as of May 11, 2026, meaning the final analysis is days away. For a late-stage clinical-stage biotech with no product revenue, a pivotal Phase 3 binary readout is the highest-magnitude catalyst possible, representing a potential transformative approval event. While the company remains blinded to outcomes, the near-certain imminence of the readout — combined with strong cash position ($107M+) and positive SLS009 Phase 2 data — is driving speculative pre-market buying characteristic of a game-changer setup.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-12, items 2.02,9.01] sls-20260512 0001390478 FALSE 0001390478 2026-05-12 2026-05-12 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(d) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of report (Date of earliest event reported): May 12, 2026 SELLAS Life Sciences Group, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-33958 20-8099512 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 7 Times Square, Su