10875|VELO|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|19.06|strong|MODERATE|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 19.1% gap, 9.1x rvol||The catalyst is a Q1 earnings beat (48% YoY rev growth, gross-margin inflection) but guidance was only reaffirmed, not raised, and the DLA IDIQ contract is just $9.8M over five years — immaterial against an ~$855M cap. No active theme/narrative match (the edge-AI and data-center-power cohorts don't fit metal additive manufacturing), so nothing lifts it above a solid-but-routine print. A small modest-magnitude catalyst on a sizable name doesn't support HIGH, so I demote toward MODERATE.|Velo3D reported Q1 2026 earnings with revenue of $13.8M, up 48% YoY, and achieved positive gross margin (17.2%) — a key inflection milestone. The company reaffirmed its full-year 2026 revenue guidance of $60M–$70M and expects to turn EBITDA positive in H2 2026. Additional catalysts include a $9.8M five-year IDIQ contract with the Defense Logistics Agency and a completed $50M capital raise, which together reinforce the growth narrative. The revenue growth rate, margin inflection, and guidance reaffirmation on a ~$834M market cap name make this a solid but not transformative beat — no guidance raise above prior targets, and the DLA contract ($9.8M) is modest relative to market cap.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-12, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] 8-K false 0001825079 0001825079 2026-05-12 2026-05-12 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(d) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported) : May 12, 2026 Velo3D, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-39757 98-1556965 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 2710 Lakeview Court , Fremont , California 94538 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) (408) 610-3915 Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code N/A (Former name or former address, if changed since last report.) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common stock, $0.00001 par value per share VELO The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 2.02 Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On May 12, 2026, Velo3D, Inc. (the &#8220;Company&#8221;) issued a press release announcing its financial results for the three months ended March 31, 2026 (the "Press Release"). In the Press Release, the Company also announced that it would be holding a conference call on May 12, 2026 at 2:00 p.m. Pacific Time to discuss its financial results for the three months ended March 31, 2026. Item 7.01 Regulation FD Disclosure. On May 12, 2026, the Company also published earnings presentation slides (the "Earnings Presen