10879|KRNT|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|66.0|13.00|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.0% gap, 8.8x rvol||Concrete, quantified earnings beat (rev $48.5M top-of-guidance, adj EPS $0.01 vs -$0.02) PLUS an above-consensus Q2 guide ($51-55M vs $50.6M) is a real material catalyst — sales-acceleration tier with durable AIC recurring revenue up 103% YoY and growing backlog. The beat magnitude is modest and the absolute revenue base small, so this clears HIGH/strong but doesn't reach game_changer. No active theme/narrative match (textile-print digital production doesn't join the edge-AI or data-center cohorts), so only the catalyst axis fires.|Kornit Digital reported Q1 2026 results with revenue of $48.54M, beating the $46.67M estimate and landing at the top of guidance, while adj. EPS of $0.01 beat the $(0.02) estimate. The company also issued Q2 revenue guidance of $51M–$55M, above the $50.61M consensus estimate. Supporting the beat is a 103% YoY surge in AIC (recurring revenue) and a growing Atlas MATRIX backlog, signaling durable business momentum. This is a solid earnings beat plus guidance raise on a $713M mid-cap industrial, qualifying as a strong catalyst — though not game_changer given the modest magnitude of the beat and the company's still-small absolute revenue base.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-13, items ] EX-99.1 2 ea029009101ex99-1.htm PRESS RELEASE, DATED MAY 13, 2026, TITLED "KORNIT DIGITAL REPORTS FIRST QUARTER 2026 RESULTS" Exhibit 99.1 Kornit Digital Reports First Quarter 2026 Results Total Revenues of $48.5 million, at Top End of Guidance Range Trailing Twelve-Month Impressions Up Approximately 12% Year Over Year, Driven by Continued Screen-to-Digital Shift AIC Revenues Increased Approximately 103% Year Over Year Delivered Positive Operating Cash Flow for Tenth Consecutive Quarter Strong Customer Response and Growing Atlas MATRIX Backlog Reinforce Expansion of Digital Production at Scale Enters Second Quarter with Strengthening Momentum, Improved Visibility and Continued AIC Transition Rosh-Ha ` Ayin, Israel &ndash; May 13, 2026 &ndash; Kornit Digital Ltd. (&ldquo;Kornit&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;) (Nasdaq: KRNT), a global leader in sustainable, on-demand, digital fashion and textile production, today reported financial results for the first quarter ended March 31, 2026. The results reflect the Company&rsquo;s continued progress in expanding digital production into scaled manufacturing environments, advancing the transition toward recurring revenues through the Company&rsquo;s All-Inclusive Click (&ldquo;AIC&rdquo;) model, and strengthening its position as a technology and platform leader for the global textile and apparel industry. &ldquo;The first quarter marked a strong start to the year and clear evidence that our strategy is translating into execution and measurable results,&rdquo; said Ronen Samuel, Chief Executive Officer of Kornit Digital. &ldquo;We delivered revenue at the top end of our guidance range and generated positive operating cash flow for the tenth consecutive quarter. Impressions growth remained strong, driven by higher utilization across our installed base and the ongoing shift from screen to digital production. At the same time, we continued expanding customer adoption of our AIC model and strengthening our recurring revenue foundation. We entered 2026 with a clear roadmap around innovation, workflow and platform expansion, and we are executing against it.&rdquo; Mr. Samuel continued, &ldquo;Konnections 2026 was a defining moment for Kornit and for the broader industry. Strong customer response to Atlas MATRIX, including a meaningful backlog of new and upgrade orders, reinforces that on-demand digital production is rapidly expanding beyond short-run customization into scaled production and manufacturing environments. We are seeing similar momentum around Apollo and increasing interest in connected workflow and automation capabilities following the PrintFactory acquisition. Atlas MATRIX, powered by Kornit&rsquo;s unique Karbon Shield technology, significantly expands digital production into polyester, sportswear and performance applications by overcoming dye migration challenges that historically limited digital production in these categories. At Texprocess in Frankfurt, we fu
10880|PSNL|2026-05-13|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|12.91|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.9% gap, 3.4x rvol||Medicare coverage expansion for the NeXT Personal MRD test is a concrete, company-specific reimbursement win that unlocks a billable late-stage solid-tumor population and validates clinical utility — a genuine commercial inflection for a ~$985M diagnostics name still building traction. This is a real material catalyst (sales acceleration / new-market unlock in Pradeep's hierarchy), not boilerplate, so it justifies promoting from the none floor to HIGH. It does not join either active narrative cohort (no edge-AI or data-center story), so only the catalyst axis fires; recent analyst PT cuts cap |The specific catalyst is Medicare coverage expansion for Personalis's NeXT Personal MRD (minimal residual disease) liquid biopsy test, now covering immunotherapy monitoring across late-stage solid tumors, supported by VHIO clinical data. This is a concrete, company-specific reimbursement win — Medicare coverage is a major commercial inflection point for a diagnostics company, as it directly unlocks a large, billable patient population and validates clinical utility. With a ~$976M market cap and a product still building commercial traction, expanded Medicare coverage is a meaningful and material catalyst. Note: analyst activity (Morgan Stanley PT cut, BTIG maintaining Buy with PT cut) is a headwind context, but the coverage expansion clearly drives the gap-up.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-13, items 5.07] 8-K false 0001527753 0001527753 2026-05-12 2026-05-12 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 12, 2026 Personalis, Inc. (Exact name of Registrant as Specified in Its Charter) Delaware 001-38943 27-5411038 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Empl