10704|VSNT|2026-05-14|live|HIGH|100.8|15.38|strong||||1.20|07:50|VSNT gapped up on anticipation of Q1 2026 earnings release before Thursday's open, following Seeking Alpha's earnings preview on May 13 and J.P. Morgan's note highlighting Versant as a standalone with more cash for self-investment. Stock closed at $40.44 on May 13 with elevated volume of over 2 million shares, support at $39.51 and resistance at $41.23. Recent positives include Versant's presentat|||The news items provided are generic headlines and conference summaries with no concrete catalyst tied to VSNT. The only item mentioning Versant directly ("Versant: Mispriced Cash Flow After A Spin-Off") is a vague analyst opinion piece with no specific earnings numbers, guidance figures, or dated announcement. None of the news includes verification of an actual earnings release, guidance raise, contract, FDA decision, or analyst upgrade—all lack specific dates, numbers, and verifiable details. This appears to be a penny stock gap lacking a substantive, verifiable catalyst.|
10705|CRMD|2026-05-14|live|HIGH|64.8|12.35|strong||||1.20|08:10|CRMD stock gapped up on strong Q1 2026 earnings beat reported before market open today, with EPS of $0.34 meeting consensus estimates after guidance was slashed low following Q4 2025's -29% miss. DefenCath commercial momentum stabilized sentiment, driving the gap despite trading 22.68% below 200-day MA at $7.50 prior close. Analysts maintain 4.25 buy rating and $15 target implying 100% upside, fue|||The news items provided are generic summaries and analyst commentary with no concrete catalyst. While there is mention of CorMedix (CRMD) analysts clustering price targets around $13–$15, this is speculative analyst opinion, not an actual company-specific catalyst like an earnings beat, guidance raise, FDA approval, or major contract. The earnings preview article explicitly states CRMD "does not possess the right combination of the two key ingredients for a likely earnings beat," suggesting no positive surprise is expected. Without specific reported earnings numbers, guidance figures, or a verifiable catalytic event, this gap-up appears to lack fundamental support and should be treated as routine intraday volatility.|
10706|ARX|2026-05-14|live|HIGH|100.8|17.64|strong||||1.20|09:50|ARX (Accelerant Holdings) gapped up 3.43% on the announcement of its Q1 2026 financial results release on May 13, with a conference call scheduled for May 14. The stock movement reflects investor anticipation ahead of earnings disclosure and the earnings call that just occurred today. This is a standard earnings-driven catalyst. The gap up typically occurs when companies announce strong results or|||Accelerant Holdings (ARX) reported Q1 2026 earnings with concrete beats: +7.60% EPS surprise and +10.47% revenue surprise. The company delivered stronger-than-expected results and management highlighted continued growth in its specialty insurance platform with expanding third-party insurer participation, suggesting positive guidance direction. This is a solid earnings beat with growth indicators that warrants a "strong" classification for an institutional financial services stock.|
10707|CPA|2026-05-14|live|HIGH|67.7|13.12|strong||||1.20|09:55|Copa Holdings (CPA) gapped up due to its Q1 earnings beat announced yesterday, reporting $5.16/share versus estimates—a 16.5% surprise. The results showed 20.5% EPS growth and 24.6% operating margin expansion from strong operational performance.|||Copa Holdings (CPA) reported Q1 2026 earnings with a +16.57% EPS beat and +1.80% revenue beat versus Wall Street estimates, coupled with strong operational metrics including 16.7% YoY RPM growth in April 2026. This earnings beat with solid operational momentum qualifies as a strong catalyst for a neglected airline stock, though the absence of explicit forward guidance raise in the news prevents a "game_changer" classification.|
10708|VIK|2026-05-14|live|HIGH|57.6|11.36|strong||||1.20|09:55|Viking Holdings (VIK) gapped up primarily due to strengthening analyst sentiment and upgraded price targets ahead of today's Q1 2026 earnings report. JPMorgan raised its target from $87 to $104 with an Overweight rating, while Susquehanna initiated coverage with a Positive rating and $100 price target. Citigroup also raised its target from $88 to $90, and Wall Street Zen upgraded from Hold to Buy.|||Viking Holdings reported Q1 CY2026 earnings with revenue of $1.05 billion, beating Wall Street estimates with 17.5% year-over-year sales growth, and additionally announced a new CEO appointment. The combination of a concrete earnings beat, strong operational momentum in cruise demand, and leadership change provides solid upside catalysts that justify the gap-up move.|
10881|ONDG|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|62.4|24.63|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 24.6% gap, 5.9x rvol||ONDG is a 2x leveraged ETF on ONDS, not an operating company, so it can have no company-specific catalyst — the gap is purely a derivative amplification of the underlying's price action. No concrete, verifiable event exists and no active narrative is joined, so this is a technical/momentum move that fails the mandatory material-catalyst test for any tier.|ONDG is a 2x leveraged ETF tracking ONDS (Ondas Holdings), not an operating company — it has no earnings, contracts, FDA decisions, or company-specific catalysts of its own. No news was found to explain the gap-up. The move is entirely derivative of price action in the underlying ONDS stock, amplified 2x by the ETF's structure, making this a technical/momentum gap with no concrete, verifiable catalyst.|
10882|ONDL|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|62.4|24.47|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 24.5% gap, 5.9x rvol||ONDL is a 2x leveraged daily ETF that mechanically tracks ONDS — it has no independent, company-specific catalyst, so the gap is merely a derivative reflection of the underlying's move. No verifiable event (earnings, contract, policy, theme) is tied to the instrument itself, and a gap alone never earns HIGH. Demote to none: there is no real catalyst to grade.|ONDL is a 2x leveraged daily ETF that tracks ONDS (Ondas Holdings) stock — it has no independent catalyst of its own. No news was found for ONDL, and any gap-up is simply a mechanical leveraged reflection of movement in the underlying security ONDS, not a company-specific catalyst. There is no concrete, verifiable event (earnings, FDA decision, contract, upgrade) tied to ONDL itself.|
10883|STAA|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|21.67|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 21.7% gap, 5.2x rvol||Concrete, grounded earnings catalyst: +119.6% Y/Y net sales (record Q1), swing from $(1.10) to +$0.10 GAAP EPS, and gross margin expansion 65.8%→73.6% — a genuine profitability reversal, not a numberless PR (sales-acceleration tier on Pradeep's hierarchy). The China-driven optics inflate the headline (ex-China growth only +6.0%), and the +21.7% gap on a $1.5B mid-cap with no theme/narrative tailwind warrants HIGH/strong rather than game_changer, which I reserve for theme-aligned or structurally lifted names. No active cohort fit, so theme/narrative axes stay dark.|STAAR Surgical reported Q1 2026 results with net sales of $93.5M — the highest first quarter in company history — up a stunning 119.6% Y/Y, swinging from a net loss of $(1.10) EPS to GAAP net income of $0.10/share and Adjusted EBITDA of $0.48/diluted share vs. a loss of $(0.53) a year ago. This is a dramatic operational turnaround on a $1.5B market cap company that had a "challenging 2025," with gross margin expanding meaningfully from 65.8% to 73.6% Y/Y. The magnitude of the revenue acceleration and profitability reversal — on a stock that was clearly under pressure — represents a transformative reset of expectations, firmly qualifying as a game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-13, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] 8-K 0000718937 STAAR SURGICAL CO 0000718937 2025-11-05 2025-11-05 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, DC 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of report (Date of earliest event reported): May 13, 2026 STAAR Surgical Co mpany (Exact Name of Registrant as Specified in Charter) Delaware 0-11634 95-3797439 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 25510 Commercentre Drive Lake Forest , California 92630 (Address of Princip