10884|POET|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|21.16|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 21.2% gap, 2.9x rvol||Concrete, verifiable commercial catalyst: a named-partner (Lumilens) supply agreement with a $50M firm purchase order (~2.6% of cap) and a credible $500M+ scale framework (~26% of cap) plus a warrant — real near-term revenue visibility, not boilerplate. The story (wafer-level photonic integration for AI optical networks / GPU interconnects) lands squarely in the active edge/AI-silicon narrative, lighting theme and narrative axes. Material but not transformative enough on the firm near-term order to push to game_changer, so it holds at strong/HIGH.|The specific catalyst is a supply agreement announced May 14, 2026 between POET Technologies and Lumilens, featuring an initial $50M purchase order for EOI-based optical engines with a stated potential to scale to $500M+ in cumulative purchases over five years. At a $1.9B market cap, the $50M initial order (~2.6% of market cap) is meaningful, and the $500M upside scenario (~26% of market cap) is highly significant for a company of this size. This is a concrete, verifiable commercial partnership — not a vague press release — backed by a named partner (Lumilens), a specific dollar figure, and a warrant structure ($8.25/share exercise price on ~22.9M shares), placing it firmly in "strong" territory given the real near-term revenue visibility plus a credible long-term scale framework tied to AI infrastructure demand.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-14, items ] EX-99.1 2 exh_991.htm PRESS RELEASE EdgarFiling EXHIBIT 99.1 POET Technologies and Lumilens Advance Wafer-Level Photonic Integration for Next-Generation AI Optical Networks Joint development and sale of high-speed optical modules based on the Electrical-Optical Interposer (EOI) -- a new paradigm for scale in the optical layer of AI compute SAN JOSE, Calif., May 14, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- POET Technologies Inc. ("POET" or the "Company") (NASDAQ: POET), a leader in highly integrated optical engines and light sources for AI networks, and Lumilens Inc. ("Lumilens"), an emerging leader in high-performance scale-up and scale-out optical interconnects for AI workloads, today announced they have entered into a supply agreement that establishes a strategic joint development and commercial technology partnership to advance a new class of wafer-level photonic integration for frontier AI infrastructure. Modern AI computing was made possible by successive leaps in wafer-level integration: first 2.5D electrical interposers that brought GPUs and HBM into a single package, then hybrid bonding that enabled today's HBM stacks and 3D logic. The optical layer, now the defining bottleneck for scaling AI, has not made that leap. At the center of the POET/Lumilens joint development program is a new paradigm for integration and module fabrication &#8211; the Electrical-Optical Interposer (EOI) &#8211; combining alignment-free wafer-level optical engine production with next-generation optical chipsets and advanced manufacturing capabilities, all to meet the ever-growing demands for scale and performance in AI infrastructure. POET and Lumilens have structured the joint EOI platform to deliver: &#149; Enhanced performance & density, enabling compact, high-bandwidth solutions for next-generation AI and data center architectures &#149; Active-alignment-free manufacturing, replacing the single largest cost, yield, and throughput constraint in optical engine production with wafer-scale processing &#149; Capital-efficient, high-volume manufacturing, allowing optical supply to scale with hyperscaler GPU fleet growth rather than against the labor-bound limits of conventional optical assembly The supply agreement between Lumilens and POET establishes a commercial framework to support the joint development program, and, as part of that framework, Lumilens has placed an initial purchase order with POET for the manufacturing of EOI-based engines valued at $50 million. This purchase order represents the first phase of a broader supplier relationship that could scale to $500+ million in cumulative purchases from POET over five years. In connection with the supply agreement, and to align both companies to the long-term value created through the partnership, POET has granted Lumilens a warrant to purchase up to 22,921,408 common shares. The warrant is immediately exercisable for 2,292,140 shares, with the remaining shares vesting and becoming exercisa
10885|GO|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|17.70|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 17.7% gap, 4.2x rvol||The catalyst is an in-line Q1 print with declining comps (-1.0%), 80bps gross-margin compression, a $180M GAAP net loss, and adjusted EPS halved to $0.05 from $0.13 — no beat, no raise, just "consistent with our guidance." The 17.7% gap is the market reacting to expectations relief, not a real material catalyst, and there is no theme/narrative tie (grocery discounter shares nothing with the Edge AI cohort). With deteriorating fundamentals and no concrete positive surprise, this is a routine gap that fails the HIGH catalyst requirement.|Grocery Outlet reported Q1 FY2026 earnings with net sales of $1.17B (+3.6% YoY), but comparable store sales declined 1.0%, gross margin compressed 80 bps to 29.6%, and the company posted a massive GAAP net loss of $180.3M (including $158M goodwill impairment and $18.2M restructuring charges). Adjusted EPS of $0.05 was a steep decline from $0.13 a year ago, and Adjusted EBITDA of $43.1M (3.7% margin) reflects significant deterioration. There is no earnings beat, no guidance raise, and no transformative catalyst — results appear to be in-line with the company's own guidance ("consistent with our guidance"), making this a routine in-line print with no positive surprise to drive sustainable momentum.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-13, items 2.02,9.01] go-20260513 0001771515 false 0001771515 2026-05-13 2026-05-13 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date earliest event reported): May 13, 2026 Grocery Outlet Holding Corp. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-38950 47-1874201 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 5650 Hollis Street , Emeryville , California 94608 (Address of principal e