10890|TRT|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|11.73|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 11.7% gap, 3.8x rvol||Concrete, verifiable catalyst: 124% YoY revenue growth ($16.5M) plus ~$7.8M of new AI-GPU burn-in board orders against a ~$100M micro-cap is genuinely material and directly ties into the active edge/AI-silicon narrative. Sales acceleration sits mid-tier in the Pradeep hierarchy (below theme/policy/shortage), so I hold HIGH but trim the floor's game_changer to strong — this is a real beat, not a transformative single event. The 11.7% gap with no RVOL/volume confirmation and a backward-looking earnings catalyst keeps it from full game_changer status.|Trio-Tech reported a massive 124% year-over-year revenue growth for Q3 FY2026 (quarter ended March 31, 2026), with total revenue of $16.5M, driven by surging demand for semiconductor reliability testing services tied to AI and EV automotive chips. The company also disclosed a concrete and material order pipeline: ~$5.3M in Burn-In Board orders for a next-generation AI GPU platform announced in March, plus an additional $2.5M in orders received since — totaling ~$7.8M in new orders against a $98M market cap, which is highly material. For a micro-cap semiconductor services company, a 124% revenue beat with strong forward demand signals and a recently strengthened balance sheet from equity financing constitutes a genuine, verifiable game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-14, items 2.02,9.01] trt20260514_8k.htm false 0000732026 0000732026 2026-05-14 2026-05-14 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, DC 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15( d ) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of report (Date of earliest event reported): May 14, 2026 TRIO-TECH INTERNATIONAL (Exact Name of Registrant as Specified in Its Charter) California (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) 1-14523 95-2086631 (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification N