10891|CPA|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|10.42|strong|MODERATE|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.4% gap, 3.4x rvol||Real, concrete earnings catalyst: ~12% EPS beat ($5.16 vs $4.61) with industry-leading 24.6% operating / 20.2% net margins up YoY despite higher fuel costs — a quantified sales-acceleration/earnings event, not boilerplate. No active theme or narrative cohort fit, and the 737 MAX order is long-term fleet sizing rather than transformative for a $5.3B cap, with no explicit guidance raise, so it stays strong/MODERATE rather than game_changer.|Copa Holdings reported Q1 2026 EPS of $5.16, decisively beating the $4.61 consensus estimate (~12% beat), on revenue of $1.052B vs. $1.033B expected. Margins were exceptional — operating margin of 24.6% and net margin of 20.2% — with EPS up 20.5% YoY, all while navigating a higher jet fuel cost environment. The results also include a confirmed dividend payment and a new Boeing 737 MAX order (40 firm + 20 options), though the order is sized for long-term fleet growth rather than being transformative relative to the $5.3B market cap. The beat is solid and margin-driven, but no explicit full-year guidance raise was cited in the release, keeping this from game_changer territory.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-14, items ] EX-99.1 2 cpa1q26ex-9911.htm EX-99.1 Document Copa Holdings Reports First-Quarter Financial Results Panama City, Panama --- May 13, 2026. Copa Holdings 1 , S.A. (NYSE&#58; CPA), today announced financial results for the first quarter of 2026 (1Q26), reflecting continued industry&#8209;leading profitability, disciplined execution, and the resilience of its business model amid a higher jet fuel price environment. Key highlights include&#58; &#8226; Net profit of US$212.5 million or US$5.16 per share, a 20.5% year&#8209;over&#8209;year increase in earnings per share. &#8226; Operating margin of 24.6% and net margin of 20.2%, increases of 0.8 and 0.5 percentage points, respectively, compared to 1Q25. &#8226; Capacity, measured in available seat miles (ASMs), grew by 14.0% year over year, and passenger traffic in RPMs increased by 15.0%. As a result, load factor increased by 0.8 percentage points to 87.2%. &#8226; Revenue per available seat mile (RASM) of 11.8 cents, an increase of 2.7% compared to 1Q25. &#8226; Operating cost per available seat mile (CASM) increased 1.6% year over year to 8.9 cents, while CASM excluding fuel (Ex-fuel CASM) decreased 1.0% to 5.8 cents. &#8226; The Company ended the quarter with approximately US$1.5 billion in cash, short-term and long-term investments, representing 40% of the last-twelve-months&#8217; revenues. &#8226; Adjusted Net Debt to EBITDA ratio ended 1Q26 at 0.7 times. &#8226; The Company repurchased US$45 million worth of shares during the quarter under the Company&#8217;s current US$200 million repurchase authorization. This represents approximately 1% of total outstanding shares as of the end of the quarter. &#8226; In 1Q26, the Company took delivery of 2 Boeing 737-MAX 8 aircraft to end the quarter with a total fleet of 127 aircraft. &#8226; Copa Airlines had an on-time performance for the quarter of 91.6% and a flight completion factor of 99.7%, once again positioning itself among the very best in the industry. Subsequent events &#8226; On May 13, 2026, the Board of Directors of Copa Holdings ratified its second dividend payment for the year of US$1.71 per share, payable on June 15, 2026, to shareholders of record as of May 29, 2026. &#8226; In April, at an event held in Panama, the Company publicly announced a Boeing 737 MAX aircraft order consisting of 40 firm orders and 20 purchase options. Deliveries are expected between 2030 and 2034, supporting long&#8209;term capacity growth while preserving flexibility within the Company&#8217;s existing fleet plan. &#8226; During the second quarter, the Company took delivery of two additional Boeing 737 MAX 8 aircraft, increasing its total fleet to 129 aircraft. 1 The terms &#8220;Copa Holdings&#8221; and the &#8220;Company&#8221; refer to the consolidated entity. The financial information presented in this release, unless otherwise indicated, is presented in accordance with International Financial Reporting Standards (IFRS). Se
10892|DDS|2026-05-14|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|10.34|strong|MODERATE|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.3% gap, 3.1x rvol||Real, material catalyst: Q1 EPS of $16.04 vs $10.39 with 3% comp growth and expanding gross margin is a genuine beat, supporting a strong/MODERATE grade. But ~$5.10/share of the upside is a non-recurring litigation settlement and there is no forward guidance or guidance raise, so I won't promote to game_changer. No active theme or narrative cohort applies (edge-AI cohort is unrelated), so only the catalyst axis fires.|Dillard's reported Q1 2026 earnings with EPS of $16.04 vs. $10.39 in the prior year quarter — a massive ~54% year-over-year increase — driven by 3% comparable store sales growth, a strong retail gross margin of 45.8%, and a one-time $104.1M pre-tax litigation settlement gain ($5.10/share after-tax). Excluding the litigation item, core EPS would be approximately $10.94, still a meaningful beat. However, the report lacks explicit forward guidance or a guidance raise, and a significant portion of the EPS upside is a non-recurring litigation settlement, which tempers the "game_changer" classification.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-14, items 2.02,9.01] Dillard&#8217;s, Inc._May 14, 2026 0000028917 false 0000028917 2026-05-14 2026-05-14 &#8203; &#8203; UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 &#8203; FORM 8-K &#8203; CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 14, 2026 &#8203; Dillard&#8217;s, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) &#8203; Texas (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; 1-6140 &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; 71-0388071 (Commission File Number) &#8203; (IRS Employer Identification No.) &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; 1600 Cantrell Road Little Rock , Arkansas &#8203; 72201 (Address of principal executive offices) &#8203; (Zip Code) &#8203; ( 501 ) 376-5200 (Reg