rein by reference. &#8203; Item 9.01 Financial Statements and Exhibits . &#8203; Exhibit No. &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; Description &#8203; &#8203; &#8203; 
10709|GEMI|2026-05-15|live|HIGH|96.0|22.24|strong||||1.00|07:00|The gap up in Gemini Space Station (GEMI) is essentially a squeeze on sentiment rather than a clean, single positive headline. Key pieces of context from the latest news flow: 1) Optics of growth versus underlying weakness   AInvest’s note on Gemini’s 42% year‑over‑year revenue growth (to about $50 million) is being framed as a “growth story,” even though the report makes clear that: - Core exchan|||GEMI reported Q1 2026 earnings with concrete metrics: revenue jumped 42% to $50.3 million with narrowing losses, simultaneously announced a $100 million strategic investment from Winklevoss Capital Fund (founders' family office) paid in bitcoin at $14/share. This combines a solid revenue beat with a significant insider confidence signal through substantial capital injection and the broader tailwind of major crypto legislative progress, making it a strong catalyst for a gap-up in a previously neglected crypto stock.|
10710|FIG|2026-05-15|live|MODERATE|57.6|8.65|strong||||1.20|07:00|FIG (Figma, NYSE:FIG) gapped up into and around its Q1 2026 earnings event, and the move is essentially an earnings‑run plus short‑covering around an oversold name with still‑strong growth expectations. Key catalysts behind the gap up: 1) Expectations for a solid Q1 print   – Street is looking for about $316 million in Q1 revenue, matching Figma’s guidance of $315–317 million, implying roughly 38%|||Figma reported Q1 2026 earnings with accelerating revenue growth, stronger seat expansion, and enterprise adoption, coupled with early monetization of AI features. The earnings beat combined with evidence of operational momentum (seat expansion, enterprise adoption, AI adoption acceleration) and management's positive positioning constitutes a solid catalyst, though no explicit guidance raise figure or specific EPS/revenue beat magnitude is detailed in the available snippets.|
10711|GLOB|2026-05-15|live|HIGH|89.3|10.59|strong||||1.20|09:50|GLOB is gapping up on a clean earnings reaction plus some “relief rally” dynamics around the ongoing lawsuit headlines. Key near-term catalysts and why the stock is higher: 1) Solid Q1 earnings and guidance (primary positive catalyst)      • Q1 results: Net income $37M, GAAP EPS $0.85; adjusted EPS $1.50, which matched Street expectations.      • Revenue: $607.1M versus about $602M expected – a sm|||Globant reported Q1 2026 earnings with revenue exceeding guidance (beat of +0.81%) and surpassing its guidance range, coupled with robust AI Pods growth and a new share repurchase program announcement. Additionally, Wedbush initiated coverage with an Outperform rating and $61 price target on April 9, adding analyst support to the positive earnings momentum on a previously neglected small-cap stock capitalizing on AI spending trends.|
10893|GEMI|2026-05-15|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|28.23|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 28.2% gap, 11.2x rvol||Concrete, company-specific 8-K catalyst: a $100M Bitcoin-funded private placement (~18% of the $560M cap) by the Winklevoss-controlled largest shareholder and CEO/President, a strong insider-conviction signal that supports the 28% gap. It is an insider PIPE rather than a theme/policy/sales-acceleration catalyst, so it stays strong rather than game_changer, and the edge-AI cohort is unrelated (no theme match). Material relative to size with a direct SEC source justifies holding the HIGH floor.|The catalyst is a $100M private placement by Winklevoss Capital Fund, LLC — the company's largest existing shareholder and the entity controlled by Gemini's own CEO and President (Tyler and Cameron Winklevoss) — funded via approximately 1,258 Bitcoin delivered as payment-in-kind at $14.00/share. This is a significant capital infusion (~18% of the $554M market cap) that signals insider conviction and strengthens the company's Bitcoin treasury strategy. While not a traditional earnings beat or guidance raise, the deal's scale relative to market cap and the high-profile insider backing make it a meaningfully bullish, company-specific catalyst rather than a routine event.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-14, items 1.01,2.02,3.02,7.01,9.01] gemi-20260514 0002055592 FALSE 0002055592 2026-03-19 2026-03-19 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 ___________________________________ FORM 8-K ___________________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 14, 2026 ___________________________________ Gemini Space Station, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) ___________________________________ Nevada (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) 001-42836 (Commission File Number) 33-3263417 (I.R.S