10894|MICC|2026-05-15|historical_scan|HIGH|32.4|13.02|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.0% gap, 6.3x rvol||The only grounded item is a routine 6-K disclosing ~€84K of insider open-market purchases by the CLO and CCO — immaterial against an $10.9B market cap and not a company-specific catalyst. No earnings, guidance, contract, upgrade, or M&A is present, and the ice-cream name shares no story with the edge-AI silicon cohort. A 13% gap without a real material catalyst stays routine/none.|The only news item found is a Form 6-K SEC filing disclosing routine Director/PDMR shareholding transactions — specifically, the Chief Legal Officer and Chief Creative Officer purchasing small amounts of shares on the open market (totaling roughly €84,000 combined) at prices of €12.60–12.70. There is no earnings release, guidance raise, major contract, analyst upgrade, or M&A event present in the filing. These insider open-market purchases are immaterial relative to MICC's $11.0B market cap and do not constitute a company-specific catalyst. No concrete, verifiable reason for a significant gap-up can be identified from the available news.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-15, items ] 6-K 1 f6k_051526.htm FORM 6-K UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 Form 6-K REPORT OF FOREIGN PRIVATE ISSUER PURSUANT TO RULE 13a-16 OR 15d-16 UNDER THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Dated May 15, 2026 Commission File Number: 001-42939 The Magnum Ice Cream Company N.V. (Translation of registrant's name into English) Reguliersdwarsstraat 63 1017 BK Amsterdam The Netherlands (Address of principal executive office) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant files or will file annual reports under cover of Form 20-F or Form 40-F. Form 20-F [ X ] Form 40-F [ ] This report on Form 6-K contains a Stock Exchange Announcement dated May 15, 2026 entitled &lsquo;Director/PDMR Shareholding&rsquo;. Indicate by check mark if the registrant is submitting the Form 6-K in paper