10895|RAMP|2026-05-18|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|27.44|mna|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 27.4% gap, 26.0x rvol||The 8-K confirms a signed Agreement and Plan of Merger for LiveRamp to be acquired by Publicis in an all-cash deal at $2.5B equity value, making this a textbook buyout. The price is now capped at the deal value, leaving no momentum trade despite the concurrent solid Q4 earnings. Grade mna per the M&A rule — the gap is acquisition-driven, not an episodic pivot.|LiveRamp (RAMP) has entered into a definitive Agreement and Plan of Merger to be acquired by Publicis Groupe S.A. in an all-cash transaction valuing the company at $2.5 billion equity value. The 8-K explicitly confirms a signed Merger Agreement with Merger Sub merging into LiveRamp, making it a wholly owned subsidiary of Publicis — a textbook M&A acquisition. Although Q4 earnings were also reported (revenue up 9% YoY, strong operating margin expansion), the dominant and deal-defining catalyst is the buyout; the stock price is now capped at the deal value with no momentum trade possible.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-18, items 1.01,2.02,5.02,5.03,7.01,9.01] false --03-31 0000733269 0000733269 2026-05-15 2026-05-15 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 15, 2026 LIVERAMP HOLDINGS, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-38669 83-1269307 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 225 Bush Street , Seventeenth Floor San Francisco , CA 94104 (Address of principal executive offices, including zip code) ( 888 ) 987-6764 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obl