10896|TE|2026-05-18|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|18.17|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 18.2% gap, 5.6x rvol||The cited "earnings beat" carries no concrete EPS, revenue, or guidance figures, so it is unverifiable and must default to routine per the numberless-earnings rule. Analyst reiterations to the same $8 PT signal limited fresh conviction, not a material new event. No active theme or narrative cohort and no direct source to lift it above the gap+enum floor.|The primary catalyst appears to be a Q1 earnings beat with strong revenue growth and progress on the 2.1GW Austin solar facility, supported by two analyst Buy reiterations/price target raises. However, the news articles contain NO specific financial figures — no EPS numbers, no revenue totals, no guidance metrics — making the earnings beat unverifiable and potentially fabricated. Per the critical verification rules, a vague earnings reference without concrete reported numbers must be classified as routine. The analyst notes also both maintain the same $8 price target (with one raise to $8), suggesting limited new conviction from the Street.|[Benzinga 2026-05-12] Needham Reiterates Buy on T1 Energy, Maintains $8 Price Target. [Benzinga 2026-05-12] BTIG Maintains Buy on T1 Energy, Raises Price Target to $8. [Benzinga 2026-05-12] Why Is T1 Energy Stock Gaining Tuesday?. TE stock climbs 13% on Q1 earnings beat. T1 Energy reports strong revenue growth and stays on schedule for its 2.1GW Austin solar facility.
10897|SATG|2026-05-18|historical_scan|HIGH|42.0|12.75|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.7% gap, 5.7x rvol||SATG is a 2x leveraged ETF whose move is a mechanical, derivative amplification of its underlying — there is no company-specific catalyst, earnings, or filing to ground a pivot. The gap+volume is just the vote with no real reason behind it, which never earns HIGH. Routine.|SATG is a 2x leveraged ETF tracking SATS (likely EchoStar or a crypto/satellite-related ticker), meaning any gap-up is purely a derivative move amplifying the underlying asset's price action — not a company-specific catalyst. No news was found for SATG itself, confirming there is no independent, verifiable catalyst. This is a leveraged ETF with no earnings, no guidance, no FDA events, and no contracts — its price movement is entirely mechanical and sector/momentum-driven.|
10898|CMPS|2026-05-18|historical_scan|HIGH|72.0|12.20|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.2% gap, 2.3x rvol||FDA granting a rolling NDA submission/review for COMP360 plus a Commissioner's National Priority Review Voucher, based on positive Phase 3 data, is a concrete, transformative regulatory catalyst for a $1.5B single-asset biotech — far above boilerplate earnings. Regulatory acceleration toward approval of a lead drug is the highest-conviction kind of binary biotech event and directly de-risks the timeline. Holds at HIGH/game_changer; the 12% gap is supported by a real, material, company-specific milestone.|The primary catalyst is the FDA granting COMPASS Pathways an NDA rolling submission and review for COMP360 (psilocybin therapy) based on positive Phase 3 data, with the final NDA submission on track for Q4 2026 — representing a concrete, accelerated regulatory pathway toward potential approval. Additionally, the company was awarded a Commissioner's National Priority Review Voucher (CNPV) for COMP360 in treatment-resistant depression, which further de-risks and accelerates the timeline. These are transformative regulatory milestones for a biotech of this size ($1.5B market cap), as an NDA rolling submission + priority review voucher signals high FDA confidence and meaningfully increases the probability and speed of approval for their lead asset.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-13, items 2.02,9.01] cmps-20260513 false 0001816590 0001816590 2026-05-13 2026-05-13 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of report (Date of earliest event reported): May 13, 2026 COMPASS PATHWAYS PLC (Exact Name of Registrant as Specified in Its Charter) England and Wales 001-39522 Not applicable (State or other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 33 Broadwick Street London W1F 0DQ Unite