10901|BIO|2026-05-18|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|10.98|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 11.0% gap, 4.4x rvol||A high-profile Elliott Management activist stake in a $7.7B neglected life-science tools name is a real, company-specific catalyst that can drive strategic/operational change — not a mere gap or sector drift. This is an activist entry, not an M&A deal, so momentum remains tradeable, and the ~11% gap plus a fresh RBC Outperform/$320 PT corroborate genuine institutional repricing. Activist catalysts sit below pure themes in the Pradeep hierarchy, so it earns a solid "strong" rather than game_changer.|The primary catalyst is news that activist investor Elliott Management has built a significant stake in Bio-Rad Laboratories (per WSJ, May 18, 2026). Elliott is a well-known activist hedge fund with a strong track record of driving operational improvements or strategic outcomes, making this a meaningful company-specific event. This is reinforced by RBC Capital's reinstatement of an Outperform rating with a $320 price target just days prior (May 15), suggesting growing institutional interest and positive sentiment. There is no acquisition/buyout agreement announced — this is an activist entry, not an M&A deal — so momentum trading remains viable. The combination of a high-profile activist stake in a $7.8B neglected life-science tools name is a genuine, verifiable catalyst that warrants a "strong" classification.|[Benzinga 2026-05-18] 'Activist Elliott Builds Big Stake in Life-Science Tools Supplier Bio-Rad' - WSJ. [Benzinga 2026-05-15] RBC Capital Reinstates Outperform on Bio-Rad Laboratories, Announces $320 Price Target.
10712|AGYS|2026-05-19|live|HIGH|72.0|14.81|strong||||1.20|07:00|AGYS gapped up on its latest earnings and guidance. Agilysys reported record Q4 and full‑year fiscal 2026 results after the close on May 18. Key positives that drove the move: • 17th consecutive record revenue quarter: Q4 revenue $82.9M, up about 11.7% year over year.   • Strong full-year growth: FY26 revenue $319.3M, up about 15.9%.   • High‑quality mix: subscription revenue up 24.1% in Q4 and 30|||Agilysys reported Q4 FY2026 earnings with a record revenue quarter and a significant 24.33% earnings beat, paired with strong SaaS growth, improved implementation capacity, and AI-driven innovation initiatives. The company also beat revenue estimates by 1.59%, demonstrating solid operational execution and market demand tailwinds in its hospitality software vertical, which supports a sustained momentum trade.|
