10714|EVTC|2026-05-19|live|MODERATE|54.7|11.25|strong||||1.20|07:15|EVTC’s recent gap up is being driven mainly by a combination of fresh institutional buying, visible insider accumulation, and solid fundamental guidance relative to the current share price. Key immediate catalysts: 1) Aggressive institutional accumulation Dana Investment Advisors disclosed on May 18 that it boosted its Evertec stake by 53.4% in Q4, to 126,297 shares, and several other institutions|||EVERTEC reported Q1 2026 earnings with higher revenue and adjusted EBITDA driven by Latin America growth and the Tecnobank acquisition, with adjusted EPS of ~$0.90 (a 3% increase). The combination of solid earnings growth, acquisition integration success, and ongoing momentum in a key geographic segment constitutes a concrete earnings beat. While the specific revenue beat/miss margin is not fully detailed in the available snippets, the explicit mention of higher results, EPS growth, and acquisition accretion provides sufficient verification of a real earnings catalyst rather than vague speculation.|
10902|AGYS|2026-05-19|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|29.86|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 29.9% gap, 11.2x rvol||Real, concrete beat-and-raise: record Q4 revenue $82.9M (+11.7%), adjusted EPS $0.63 vs $0.54, record EBITDA, plus FY27 guidance of $365-370M with ≥30% subscription growth — a meaningful acceleration with specific numbers (sales-acceleration tier). The 17th consecutive record quarter and strong forward guide justify HIGH/strong, but ~15% implied top-line growth on a $2.6B cap is solid execution rather than a transformative re-rating, so no promotion to game_changer. No theme/narrative cohort support to lift it further.|Agilysys reported its 17th consecutive record revenue quarter at $82.9M (+11.7% YoY) with Q4 adjusted EBITDA of $21.5M (vs. $14.8M prior year) and adjusted EPS of $0.63 (vs. $0.54), alongside full-year record revenue of $319.3M. The company issued strong FY2027 guidance of $365M–$370M in revenue with subscription revenue growth of at least 30% and adjusted EBITDA margin of 24%, representing a meaningful acceleration. The beat-and-raise combination is solid and concrete with specific figures, but the revenue growth rate (~15% implied for FY27) and market cap of $2.6B suggest a strong rather than game-changing catalyst — the guidance raise is meaningful but not a dramatic re-rating event.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-18, items 2.02,9.01] 8-K 0000078749 false 0000078749 2026-05-18 2026-05-18 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 18, 2026 AGILYSYS, INC. (Exact name of Registrant as Specified in Its Charter) Delaware 000-5734 34-0907152 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 3655 Brookside Parkway , Suite 300 Alpharetta , Georgia 30022 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) Registra