10722|ALAB|2026-05-20|live|HIGH|100.8|15.68|strong||||1.20|18:40|ALAB’s latest gap up is being driven by a clear fundamental catalyst: an RBC Capital Markets call tied to Amazon/Anthropic AI infrastructure demand. Key points behind the move: • RBC reiterated its Outperform rating on Astera Labs and raised its price target from $225 to $250.   • The note explicitly links upside to Amazon’s expanded deal with Anthropic and the resulting AI build‑out at AWS.   • R|||Astera Labs reported blowout quarterly earnings with 93% revenue growth driven by AI demand surge, coupled with a raised outlook and an analyst upgrade from Barclays (price target lifted to $200). This combination of a solid beat with guidance raise plus an analyst upgrade cluster is a textbook "strong" catalyst for a neglected semiconductor stock positioned in the high-growth AI connectivity segment.|
