10907|QUBX|2026-05-21|historical_scan|HIGH|62.4|21.66|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 21.7% gap, 7.5x rvol||QUBX is a 2X leveraged daily ETF on QUBT with no independent business, so its 21.7% gap is a purely mechanical, derivative amplification of the underlying — not a discrete company catalyst, which the rubric requires for any HIGH grade. No direct source, no theme/narrative join (quantum is not one of the active cohorts), and an ETF has no materiality relative to its own size. Demote to routine/none as the move is sector/momentum exposure rather than a verifiable EP event.|QUBX is a 2X leveraged daily ETF tracking QUBT (Quantum Computing Inc.), meaning any gap-up in QUBX is purely a derivative, amplified move of QUBT's price action — not a company-specific catalyst for QUBX itself. No news was found for QUBX, which is expected since it has no independent business operations, earnings, contracts, or FDA events. The gap-up is entirely mechanical, driven by whatever is moving the underlying QUBT stock, and represents sector/momentum exposure rather than a discrete, verifiable EP catalyst.|
