10909|INFQ|2026-05-21|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|20.75|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 20.8% gap, 9.0x rvol||Real, concrete government catalyst: a $100M CHIPS R&D LOI with the US Dept of Commerce (~3.5% of cap) is material and carries strong policy credibility for a pre-revenue quantum name, amplified by a $2B federal quantum initiative that constitutes a live government-policy theme. Government policy ranks high in the Pradeep hierarchy and the catalyst joins an active quantum-funding wave, lighting catalyst and theme axes. LOI (not finalized) and execution risk cap it below game_changer, so HIGH/strong holds.|The specific catalyst is Infleqtion signing a Letter of Intent (LOI) with the U.S. Department of Commerce's CHIPS R&D Office for $100M in milestone-based funding to advance neutral-atom quantum computing systems. At a $2.9B market cap, $100M represents roughly ~3.5% of market cap — meaningful and material for a pre-revenue quantum tech company, and carries strong government credibility. There is also a broader tailwind from the Trump Administration announcing a $2B quantum investment initiative, amplifying sector momentum on top of the company-specific news. However, since this is an LOI (not a finalized contract), it carries some execution risk, keeping it from "game_changer" territory.|[Benzinga 2026-05-21] Why Are Infleqtion, D-Wave Quantum, Rigetti Computing Shares Surging In Thursday Pre-Market?. Trump Administration to invest $2 billion in quantum firms, boosting shares of Infleqtion, D-Wave, Rigetti, IBM and others. [Benzinga 2026-05-21] Infleqtion Stock Jumps After Proposed $100M CHIPS Funding Deal. Infeqtion Inc. (NYSE: INFQ) shares are surging Thursday after signing $100 million CHIPS R&amp;D LOI to accelerate neutral-atom quantum systems. [Benzinga 2026-05-21] Infleqtion Signs LOI With US Department Of Commerce's CHIPS R&D Office For $100M Milestone‑Based Funding To Advance Neutral‑Atom Quantum Computing.
