10913|RGTI|2026-05-21|historical_scan|HIGH|68.4|10.69|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.7% gap, 5.5x rvol||Concrete, SEC-8K-backed government catalyst: a signed LOI with the U.S. Department of Commerce for up to $100M in CHIPS Act funding plus an equity stake — government-policy tier in the Pradeep hierarchy and strategically significant for a quantum pure-play. At ~1.5% of a $6.6B cap the dollars are only meaningful (not transformative), and it's a non-binding LOI rather than a definitive award, so it holds at strong/HIGH rather than promoting to game_changer. No active narrative cohort matches the quantum/CHIPS story, so theme/narrative axes stay dark.|The specific catalyst is a signed Letter of Intent (LOI) with the U.S. Department of Commerce for an award of up to $100 million in funding over three years under the CHIPS Act to accelerate superconducting quantum computing R&D. This is a concrete, verifiable government contract/award announcement backed by an SEC 8-K filing and press release. At ~$100M against a $6.6B market cap, the deal represents roughly 1.5% of market cap in direct funding — meaningful but not transformative on its own — however, the strategic significance of a U.S. government partnership, the CHIPS Act backing, and the equity stake component (signaling deep government commitment) elevate this above a routine catalyst for a quantum computing pure-play. No earnings beat or guidance raise is present, so game_changer is not warranted.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-21, items 3.02,7.01,8.01,9.01] false 0001838359 0001838359 2026-05-20 2026-05-20 0001838359 us-gaap:CommonStockMember 2026-05-20 2026-05-20 0001838359 us-gaap:WarrantMember 2026-05-20 2026-05-20 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 20, 2026 RIGETTI