10914|BIRK|2026-05-21|historical_scan|HIGH|30.0|10.63|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.6% gap, 4.2x rvol||The catalyst is a $250M accelerated share repurchase — a capital-allocation/defensive action (~3% of an $8.3B cap), not an operational outperformance, and buybacks rank at the bottom of the Pradeep hierarchy with no near-term earnings impact. No new earnings beat or guidance raise, no active theme/narrative fit, and recent analyst PT cuts signal the stock has been under pressure. Gap+volume alone never earns HIGH, and this immaterial-for-the-size catalyst confirms routine.|The specific catalyst is a $250 million Accelerated Share Repurchase (ASR) agreement announced on May 21, 2026, framed around management's belief that the share price is disconnected from fundamentals. While the CEO also reiterated confidence in 13-15% annual revenue growth in constant currency, no new earnings beat or guidance raise was reported — this is a capital allocation action, not an operational outperformance event. At an $8.3B market cap, a $250M buyback represents roughly 3% of market cap — meaningful but not transformative, and buybacks are generally not momentum catalysts as they don't change the fundamental earnings trajectory in a near-term, verifiable way. The most recent analyst actions (Telsey and BTIG both maintaining bullish ratings but *lowering* price targets on May 14) further suggest the stock has been under pressure, making this a defensive buyback signal rather than a game-changing catalyst.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-21, items ] EX-99.1 2 birk-ex99_1.htm EX-99.1 EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 PRESS RELEASE MEDIA CONTACT Birkenstock Holding plc ir@birkenstock-holding.com LONDON, UNITED KINGDOM   MAY 21, 2026 BIRKENSTOCK to execute $250 million Accelerated Share Repurchase TO TAKE ADVANTAGE OF DISCONNECT BETWEEN SHARE PRICE AND FUNDAMENTAL PERFORMANCE Birkenstock Holding plc (&#x201c;BIRKENSTOCK&#x201d; or the &#x201c;Company&#x201d;, NYSE: BIRK) announced today that it has entered into a $250 million accelerated share repurchase (&#x201c;ASR&#x201d;) agreement with Goldman Sachs International (&#x201c;Goldman Sachs&#x201d;). &#34;Short-term market dynamics have resulted in what we believe is a strong disconnect between our share price and the strength of our underlying fundamentals&#x201d;, said Oliver Reichert, CEO of Birkenstock Group and Member of the Board of Directors of the Company. &#34;We believe deploying our substantial cash position toward repurchasing our own shares represents the most attractive use of capital in the current environment. Given the volatile environment of the capital markets, we will continue evaluating market conditions to take advantage of further opportunities for share repurchases in the future.&#34; Oliver Reichert continues: &#34;The $250 million accelerated share repurchase is a strong statement that we believe in near-term and long-term value of BIRKENSTOCK. Our business continues to deliver outstanding performance and we see a huge runway for growth ahead for our beloved brand. We remain confident in our ability to achieve revenue growth of 13-15% annually in constant currency, while maintaining strong margins and strong free cash flow generation.&#34; Under the ASR agreement, on May 21, 2026, Birkenstock will make a payment of $250 million to Goldman Sachs and expects to receive initial delivery of approximately 6.0 million Birkenstock ordinary shares representing approximately 80 percent of the number of ordinary shares initially underlying the ASR agreement, based on the closing price of Birkenstock&#x2019;s ordinary shares of $33.21 on May 20, 2026. The final number of Birkenstock&#x2019;s ordinary shares to be repurchased will be based on the volume-weighted average price of Birkenstock&#x2019;s ordinary shares during the term of the ASR agreement, less a discount and subject to customary adjustments. At final settlement, Birkenstock may receive additional shares or, 1 BIRKENSTOCK HOLDING PLC   press release   MAY 21, 2026 under certain circumstances, may be required to make a cash payment pursuant to the terms of the ASR agreement. The transactions under the ASR agreement are expected to be completed before June 30, 2026. ABOUT BIRKENSTOCK Birkenstock Holding plc is the ultimate parent company of Birkenstock Group B.V. & Co. KG and its subsidiaries (the &#34;Birkenstock Group&#34;). BIRKENSTOCK is a global brand which embraces all consumers regardless of geography, gender, age and income and which is com
10915|GFS|2026-05-21|historical_scan|HIGH|56.4|10.28|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.3% gap, 2.8x rvol||GFS has a real, government-backed, dollar-quantified catalyst — a $375M federal award within IBM's $1B quantum foundry program — paired with the same-day launch of a dedicated Quantum Technology Solutions business, signaling a strategic pivot rather than boilerplate PR. Though $375M is only ~0.9% of the $42.6B cap, the catalyst is government-policy-backed (high in Pradeep's hierarchy) and positions GFS as a key manufacturing partner in the hot AI/quantum semiconductor theme, joining the active AI-infrastructure narrative. This concrete, theme-aligned policy award justifies promoting to HIGH/st|The primary catalyst is a concrete, government-backed award: GlobalFoundries is set to receive a $375M grant as part of a broader $1B IBM quantum chip foundry award, announced May 21, 2026. This is a named, dollar-quantified federal contract/award — verifiable and material. While $375M is modest relative to GFS's $42.3B market cap (~0.9%), it validates GFS as a key manufacturing partner in the emerging quantum computing space, which is further reinforced by the same-day launch of GFS's dedicated Quantum Technology Solutions business unit. Together, these two announcements signal a strategic pivot into high-growth quantum manufacturing — a meaningful positive development beyond a routine press release, though not quite transformative enough relative to market cap to warrant game_changer.|[Benzinga 2026-05-21] GlobalFoundries Launches Quantum Technology Solutions, New Quantum Business To Scale Manufacturing Capabilities. [Benzinga 2026-05-21] IBM Receiving $1B Award For Quantum Chip Foundry; GlobalFoundries To Receive $375M. [Benzinga 2026-05-19] GlobalFoundries Invests In Playground Global's Fund IV As Limited Partner Through GF Accelerate, Formalizing GF's Expanding Commitment To Early-Stage Deep Tech Startups.
10727|PPTA|2026-05-22|live|HIGH|72.0|11.00|game_changer||||1.00|07:00|Perpetua Resources (PPTA) gapped up on a very specific fundamental catalyst: U.S. government support and renewed attention on its Stibnite Gold Project’s strategic antimony supply role, combined with a strong project update. The latest key drivers are: 1) U.S. government funding/endorsement   PPTA has been a direct beneficiary of U.S. policy moves to secure domestic sources of critical minerals, e|||Perpetua Resources received approval from the U.S. Export-Import Bank (EXIM) for a $2.9 billion loan to finance its flagship Stibnite Gold project in Idaho. This is a transformative catalyst—securing government financing of this magnitude de-risks the project's development significantly, removing a major funding hurdle and validating the project's viability by a U.S. federal agency. The stock jumped 13-14% on the news, reflecting the substantial impact of this milestone.|
10916|IMRX|2026-05-22|historical_scan|HIGH|78.0|14.75|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 14.8% gap, 14.1x rvol||Concrete clinical readout — 17.3-month median OS in first-line metastatic pancreatic cancer vs ~11-12mo standard of care, with manageable tolerability — is a hard-numbered, program-de-risking catalyst that is highly material for a $269M late-stage oncology micro-cap. This is a specific company event (not vague PR or sector drift), squarely a strong sales-acceleration/new-product-tier catalyst that justifies HIGH. It does not join any active narrative cohort (the FDA-biotech cohort is a different shared story), so theme/narrative axes stay dark and it falls short of game_changer.|The primary catalyst is Immuneering's clinical data release (May 21) showing 17.3 months median overall survival (mOS) in first-line metastatic pancreatic cancer patients treated with atebimetinib (IMM-1-104) plus chemotherapy — a notably difficult-to-treat cancer with historically poor prognosis (standard of care mOS is roughly 11-12 months). The tolerability profile was described as manageable, with only two Grade 3+ treatment-related adverse event categories above 10%, both chemotherapy-related rather than drug-related. This is a concrete, specific Phase 3 clinical readout with hard survival numbers that meaningfully de-risks the program, making it a strong episodic catalyst for a $268M market cap late-stage oncology company. The earlier Q1 EPS beat ($-0.21 vs $-0.26 est.) is a secondary positive but minor for a pre-revenue biotech.|[Benzinga 2026-05-21] Immuneering Reveals 17.3 Months Median Overall Survival in First-Line Metastatic Pancreatic Cancer Patients Treated with Atebimetinib Plus Chemotherapy; Tolerability Profile Consistent With Prior Updates; Only Two Categories Of Grade 3 Or Higher Treatment-Related Adverse Events Observed In ≥10% Of Patients, Both Chemotherapy-Related. [Benzinga 2026-05-15] Immuneering Q1 EPS $(0.21) Beats $(0.26) Estimate.
10917|IMAX|2026-05-22|historical_scan|HIGH|36.0|13.70|mna|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.7% gap, 3.6x rvol||The sole catalyst is a WSJ report that IMAX is exploring a sale — a classic M&A/buyout-speculation event that caps upside at an eventual deal price rather than providing an operational growth driver. There is no earnings beat, new product, or theme alignment (the active cohorts are quantum/AI-semi/biotech, none of which IMAX joins). M&A speculation is a hard skip for EP momentum, so I confirm the mna grade.|The specific catalyst is a WSJ exclusive report that IMAX Corporation is exploring a sale, driven by growing demand for its premium large-format theaters. While this is not yet a definitive agreement or confirmed deal, "exploring a sale" is a classic M&A catalyst — it signals the company may be acquired, which caps the upside at any eventual deal price. This is a hard skip for EP/momentum trading, as there is no earnings beat or operational catalyst driving the move — purely acquisition speculation.|[Benzinga 2026-05-21] IMAX Shares Pop On Reports It's Exploring A Sale. IMAX is reportedly exploring a sale, as its premium large-format theaters see growing demand and market share. [Benzinga 2026-05-21] 'IMAX Is Exploring a Sale'- WSJ Exclusive.
