10924|RDWU|2026-05-26|historical_scan|HIGH|56.4|26.69|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 26.7% gap, 2.8x rvol||RDWU is a 2x leveraged ETF that mechanically delivers 200% of RDW's daily move — its gap is a derivative artifact, not an independent company catalyst. There is no real, material event for the ETF itself, so it fails the hard requirement for any tier above routine. Leveraged ETFs offer no EP setup; the entire move is borrowed from the underlying.|RDWU is a 2x leveraged ETF designed to deliver 200% of the daily price performance of its underlying asset (RDW). No company-specific news or catalyst was found. The gap-up is almost certainly driven entirely by movement in the underlying instrument (RDW), not any independent catalyst for RDWU itself. Leveraged ETFs like this mechanically amplify their underlying's moves and offer no EP trade setup.|
