10927|PONY|2026-05-26|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|15.47|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 15.5% gap, 4.7x rvol||Real, concrete catalyst: a 64% adj-EPS beat paired with a quantified upward revision to both 2026 robotaxi revenue growth (3x→3.5x+) and fleet size (3K→3.5K+ units) — sales-acceleration signal on a $3.5B autonomous-driving name. The revenue miss tempers it and there's no theme/narrative join (the active Lane 2 cohort is quantum computing, not robotaxi/AV), so it holds at strong rather than promoting to game_changer.|Pony AI reported Q1 2026 results with a significant adjusted EPS beat of $(0.09) vs. the $(0.25) estimate (64% beat), though revenue of $34.25M missed the $51.09M estimate. The key bullish catalyst is a meaningful guidance raise: management lifted its 2026 robotaxi revenue outlook from 3x to over 3.5x YoY growth, and expanded its robotaxi fleet size forecast from 3,000 to over 3,500 units. The combination of a substantial earnings beat and a concrete, quantified upward revision to both revenue growth and fleet scale on a $3.5B autonomous vehicle company justifies a "strong" classification — the guidance raise signals accelerating commercial momentum that outweighs the revenue miss.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-26, items ] EX-99.2 3 tm2615604d1_ex99-2.htm EXHIBIT 99.2 Exhibit 99.2 Hong Kong Exchanges and Clearing Limited and The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited take no responsibility for the contents of this announcement, make no representation as to its accuracy or completeness and expressly disclaim any liability whatsoever for any loss howsoever arising from or in reliance upon the whole or any part of the contents of this announcement. Pony AI Inc. &#23567;&#39340;&#26234;&#34892;* (A company controlled through weighted voting rights and incorporated in the Cayman Islands with limited liability) (Stock code: 2026) INSIDE INFORMATION UNAUDITED FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR THE QUARTER ENDED MARCH 31, 2026 This announcement is issued pursuant to Rule 13.09 of the Rules Governing the Listing of the Securities on The Stock Exchange of Hong Kong Limited and under Part XIVA of the Securities and Futures Ordinance (Cap. 571 of the Laws of Hong Kong). Pony AI Inc. (the &ldquo; Company &rdquo;) is pleased to announce the unaudited condensed consolidated results of the Company and its subsidiaries (the &ldquo; Group &rdquo;) for the three months ended March 31, 2026. The Company is pleased to announce the unaudited condensed consolidated results of the Group for the three months ended March 31, 2026 (the &ldquo; Q1 Results &rdquo;) published in accordance with applicable rules of the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission (the &ldquo; SEC &rdquo;). The Q1 Results have been prepared in accordance with generally accepted accounting principles in the United States of America (&ldquo; U.S. GAAP &rdquo;), which are different from the International Financial Reporting Standards. Attached hereto as Schedule I is the full text of the press release issued by the Company on May 26, 2026 (U.S. Eastern Time) in relation to the Q1 Results, some of which may constitute material inside information of the Company. * For identification purposes only 1 This announcement contains forward-looking statements. These statements are made under the &ldquo;safe harbor&rdquo; provisions of the U.S. Private Securities Litigation Reform Act of 1995. Statements that are not historical facts, including statements about the Company&rsquo;s beliefs, and expectations, are forward-looking statements. Forward-looking statements involve inherent risks and uncertainties, and a number of factors could cause actual results to differ materially from those contained in any forward-looking statement. In some cases, forward-looking statements can be identified by words or phrases such as &ldquo;may&rdquo;, &ldquo;will&rdquo;, &ldquo;expect&rdquo;, &ldquo;anticipate&rdquo;, &ldquo;target&rdquo;, &ldquo;aim&rdquo;, &ldquo;estimate&rdquo;, &ldquo;intend&rdquo;, &ldquo;plan&rdquo;, &ldquo;believe&rdquo;, &ldquo;potential&rdquo;, &ldquo;continue&rdquo;, &ldquo;is/are likely to&rdquo; or other similar expressions. Further information regarding these and other risks, uncertainties or factor
