10940|DY|2026-05-27|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|27.36|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 27.4% gap, 3.8x rvol||Record Q1 with revenues +56.1% (+24.7% organic), adjusted EPS $4.42, record $11.9B backlog (+46.5%), AND a raised full-year outlook is a textbook beat-and-raise on a multi-quarter record — a real, material earnings catalyst fully justifying a 27% gap. The bolt-on NTI acquisition is Dycom as acquirer (not a cap event) and adds a clean data-center/fiber-infrastructure theme tailwind tied to AI-driven buildout. Catalyst is unambiguous, concrete, and large relative to even a $13.7B cap; floor verdict holds.|Dycom reported record Q1 FY2027 results that exceeded the high end of their own guidance: contract revenues of $1.965B (+56.1% YoY, +24.7% organically), adjusted EPS of $4.42, adjusted EBITDA of $262.5M (13.4% margin), and record total backlog of $11.906B (+46.5% YoY) — all quarterly records. Critically, the company also raised its full-year FY2027 outlook, completing the classic beat-and-raise combo. The additional announcement of the National Technology Integrators acquisition to expand into high-growth data center infrastructure further amplifies the bullish narrative, though DY is the acquirer (not the target), so this is an offensive strategic move rather than an M&A cap event.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-27, items 2.02,9.01] dy-20260527 0000067215 false 0000067215 2026-05-27 2026-05-27 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(d) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 27, 2026 DYCOM INDUSTRIES, INC. (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its charter) Florida 001-10613 59-1277135 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission file number) (I.R.S. employer identification no.) 300 Banyan Blvd., Suite 1101 West Palm Beach FL 33401 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#82