10944|UMAC|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|32.77|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 32.8% gap, 13.3x rvol||The sole filing is a 7.01/9.01 8-K furnishing a routine investor presentation — no earnings, guidance, FDA decision, or named contract with a verifiable dollar value, so there is no concrete company-specific catalyst to support a real materiality judgment for a $1.2B cap. The Upgrade Energy "definitive agreement" is undisclosed-size and makes UMAC the acquirer (not an M&A cap event), and the Pentagon/Blue UAS language is forward-looking marketing boilerplate. UMAC is not in the active drone-defense cohort and joins no shared dated story, so the gap is sector-sentiment/promotional rather than c|The sole filed news is an 8-K (Items 7.01/9.01) disclosing the upload of a routine investor presentation to the company's website — there are no earnings results, no EPS/revenue figures, no guidance raise, no FDA decision, and no named major contract with a disclosed dollar value. The presentation references a "definitive agreement to acquire Upgrade Energy," but UMAC is the acquirer, not the target, so this is not an M&A cap event for UMAC itself; and the deal size is not disclosed, making materiality unverifiable relative to the $1.2B market cap. The gap-up appears driven by general drone/defense sector sentiment and marketing language (Pentagon initiative, Blue UAS Framework) rather than any concrete, company-specific, verifiable catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-26, items 7.01,9.01] Unusual Machines Form 8-K false 0001956955 0001956955 2026-05-26 2026-05-26 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported) May 26, 2026 Unusual Machines, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Nevada 001-41961 66-0927642 (State or other 