10946|PHR|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|18.07|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 18.1% gap, 4.1x rvol||Concrete, verifiable Q1 FY27 earnings show a genuine profitability inflection — net income of $3.0M vs. a $3.9M prior-year loss, Adjusted EBITDA up 47% YoY, and free cash flow more than doubling — a real company-specific catalyst that justifies the 18% gap, not boilerplate. This is a profitability swing (sales acceleration / inflection) for a $549M SaaS name, which is material but not transformative, and it does not join either active narrative cohort (no theme/narrative axis). Hold at HIGH/strong: real catalyst earns HIGH, but the absence of theme heat or a game-changing magnitude caps it bel|Phreesia reported Q1 FY2027 earnings (quarter ended April 30, 2026) with concrete, verifiable results: total revenue of $130.9M (+13% YoY), net income of $3.0M vs. a net loss of $3.9M in the prior year period, and Adjusted EBITDA of $30.5M vs. $20.8M — a 47% YoY improvement. Free cash flow more than doubled to $16.4M from $7.5M. These are meaningful beats across profitability and cash flow metrics for a ~$545M market cap SaaS company that was previously loss-making. The results demonstrate a clear inflection toward sustained profitability, which is a strong, company-specific catalyst for a mid-cap healthcare SaaS name.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-27, items 2.02,9.01] phr-20260527 false 0001412408 0001412408 2026-05-27 2026-05-27 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 ___________________________________ FORM 8-K ___________________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (date of earliest event reported) May 27, 2026 ___________________________________ Phreesia, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) ___________________________________ Delaware (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) 001-38977 (Commission File N