10947|LTRX|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|44.4|16.69|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 16.7% gap, 6.0x rvol||The only catalysts are a mechanical/passive Russell 3000 preliminary inclusion and a vague, numberless "progress update" on an AI threat-detection collaboration — neither is a concrete, material company event. The threat-detection angle does not match the active defense-drone/UAS cohort (which requires a real government/NATO UAS contract). Gap+volume alone is the market's vote, not a real catalyst, so this holds at routine/none.|The most recent news items for LTRX are: (1) a preliminary inclusion in the Russell 3000 Index announcement, and (2) a vague "progress update" on an AI-powered threat detection collaboration with Safe Pro — no specific contract value, milestones, or financial figures are provided. Neither catalyst is concrete or material enough to justify a significant gap-up: Russell index inclusions are mechanical/passive events with limited fundamental impact, and the Safe Pro collaboration update is a generic press release with no verifiable numbers. No earnings release, guidance raise, analyst upgrade cluster, or transformative deal is present in the news. The gap-up lacks a clear, verifiable company-specific catalyst.|[Benzinga 2026-05-27] Lantronix Announces Its Preliminary Inclusion In The Russell 3000 Index. [Benzinga 2026-05-20] Lantronix And Safe Pro Announce Progress On AI-Powered Threat Detection Collaboration.
10948|RCAT|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|16.26|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 16.3% gap, 8.9x rvol||The only identifiable event is an HC Wainwright Buy initiation with a $20 PT — an analyst opinion, not a company-specific transformative catalyst, and it sits at the bottom of the Pradeep hierarchy. RCAT (a drone/UAS maker) is conceptually adjacent to the active "Defense drone and UAS expansion" cohort, but there is no shared-story catalyst (no contract/award) to actually join that narrative, so the theme axis does not fire. A 16% gap on a boutique initiation alone is the market's vote without a material reason — routine.|The only identifiable news is an analyst initiation by HC Wainwright & Co. with a Buy rating and $20 price target (May 27, 2026). While analyst initiations can provide a short-term boost, a single initiation from a smaller boutique firm (HC Wainwright) is not a company-specific transformative event and does not meet the bar for "strong." The second news item is a generic retrospective piece with no actionable catalyst. There is no earnings beat, guidance raise, major contract, or transformative event visible in the provided news — the gap-up lacks a concrete, high-quality catalyst.|[Benzinga 2026-05-27] HC Wainwright & Co. Initiates Coverage On Red Cat Holdings with Buy Rating, Announces Price Target of $20. [Benzinga 2026-05-19] Here's How Much $1000 Invested In Red Cat Holdings 5 Years Ago Would Be Worth Today.
10949|DLTR|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|84.0|15.79|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 15.8% gap, 3.8x rvol||Concrete beat-and-raise: adjusted EPS +38% YoY, 3.5% comps, 120bp margin expansion, and a raised FY26 outlook — a real, quantified earnings catalyst, not boilerplate. Material for a $21.6B defensive name (the ~16% gap confirms the market's vote) but not transformative enough relative to its size for game_changer, and it joins no active theme/narrative cohort. Holds the HIGH/strong floor.|Dollar Tree reported Q1 FY2026 results with adjusted diluted EPS of $1.74, up 38% YoY, alongside 7.2% net sales growth and 3.5% comparable store sales growth — a clear and substantial earnings beat. The company raised its full-year fiscal 2026 adjusted EPS outlook to $6.70–$7.10 and provided solid Q2 guidance of 2.5–3.5% comp sales growth. Operating income margin expanded 120 basis points, and the company returned $595M to shareholders via buybacks in Q1, signaling confidence in the business. The beat-and-raise combination on a $21.4B market cap consumer defensive name is a strong, concrete catalyst, though not quite game_changer given the company's large size and the fact that guidance raises are somewhat expected in this environment.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-28, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] dltr-20260528 0000935703 false 0000935703 2026-05-28 2026-05-28 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 28, 2026 DOLLAR TREE, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Virginia 0-25464 26-2018846 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 500 Volvo Parkway Chesapeake, Virginia 23320 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) ( 757 ) 321-5000 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Check the appropr