10950|A|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|48.0|14.81|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 14.8% gap, 3.0x rvol||Concrete Q2 earnings beat (+10% revenue, +14% non-GAAP EPS, +130bps margin) with a guidance raise across revenue, margin, and EPS is a real, quantified company-specific catalyst — not boilerplate — which justifies promoting from the floor's tier=none to HIGH. A ~15% gap on a $36B name backed by a beat-and-raise is materially significant for a mature large-cap. No active theme/narrative match, so only the catalyst axis fires and it stays "strong" rather than game_changer.|Agilent Technologies reported Q2 FY2026 results with revenue of $1.83B (+10.0% reported, +6.3% core YoY), non-GAAP EPS of $1.49 (+14% YoY), and non-GAAP operating margin expansion of 130 bps YoY. The company raised its full-year FY2026 guidance, lifting the revenue range to $7.39B–$7.49B (midpoint +30bps), non-GAAP EPS to $6.00–$6.10 (+8 cents at midpoint), and increased operating margin expansion guidance by 10bps. This is a solid, concrete earnings beat with a meaningful guidance raise across revenue, margins, and EPS, supported by specific reported figures — a clear company-specific positive catalyst for a $36B market cap name.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-27, items 2.02,5.02,9.01] a-20260520 0001090872 false 0001090872 2026-05-20 2026-05-20 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 20, 2026 AGILENT TECHNOLOGIES, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-15405 77-0518772 (State or other jurisdiction (Commission (IRS Employer of incorporation) File Number) Identification No.) 5301 Stevens Creek Boulevard , Santa Clara , CA 95051 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code (800) 227-9770 (Former name or former addres