10951|CTRN|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|72.0|14.38|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 14.4% gap, 3.2x rvol||Real, quantified catalyst: preliminary Q1 sales +14.4% to $230.9M, comps +13.9%, EBITDA more than doubling, plus a raised FY26 outlook — a genuine sales-acceleration event well above boilerplate. For a ~$391M value retailer this is material fundamental momentum, but it sits in the sales-acceleration/earnings tier (not theme/policy/shortage) with no theme or narrative tailwind, so I hold HIGH but demote the game_changer floor to strong.|Citi Trends pre-announced Q1 2026 preliminary results showing total sales up 14.4% to $230.9M with comparable store sales growth of 13.9% (23.8% on a two-year stack), while Adjusted EBITDA more than doubled year-over-year to $13.5–$14.0M. The company simultaneously raised its fiscal 2026 guidance, lifting comp sales outlook to 8–10% (from 5–7%) and boosting full-year Adjusted EBITDA guidance to $35–$40M (from $34–$38M). For a ~$391M market cap value retailer, a comp sales acceleration of this magnitude combined with a doubling of EBITDA and a meaningful guidance raise represents a transformative earnings event with clear fundamental momentum.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-27, items 2.02,9.01] false 0001318484 0001318484 2026-05-27 2026-05-27 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 27, 2026 Citi Trends, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 000-41886 52-2150697 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 17 Park of Commerce Boulevard , Suite 200 ,&#8239; Savannah , Georgia 31405 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: ( 912 ) 236