10952|ONDL|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|50.4|13.65|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.7% gap, 5.2x rvol||ONDL is a 2x leveraged ETF tracking ONDS daily; it has no independent, company-specific catalyst — the gap is purely a derivative, amplified echo of the underlying. With no SEC filing, contract, earnings, or theme membership of its own, this is a structural move, not an EP-grade pivot.|ONDL is a 2x leveraged ETF that tracks the daily price movement of ONDS (Ondas Holdings) — it has no independent catalyst of its own. No news was found for ONDL itself, and any gap-up is purely a derivative move driven by ONDS's underlying price action, amplified 2x by the fund's structure. There is no company-specific, verifiable catalyst (no earnings, no FDA decision, no contract, no upgrade) to justify an EP trade.|
10953|CRSR|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|51.6|12.93|routine|MODERATE|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.9% gap, 25.8x rvol||The "strong earnings" and "AI compute expansion" headline carries no EPS, revenue, or guidance figures, leaving the earnings catalyst unverifiable and unquantified. The Elgato Stream Deck MCP/AI-assistant feature is a minor product announcement, immaterial to a ~$927M-cap name, and CRSR joins no active drone or nuclear-AI narrative. Gap+volume alone is only the market's vote, not a material catalyst — holds routine/MODERATE.|The Benzinga headline references "strong earnings results" and an "AI compute expansion," but critically provides no specific figures — no EPS, no revenue, no guidance numbers — making the earnings catalyst unverifiable and likely fabricated or paraphrased without substance. The second headline about Elgato/Stream Deck MCP support for AI assistants is a minor product feature announcement that is not material relative to CRSR's $917M market cap. Without concrete, verifiable earnings data, this cannot be classified as a strong or game-changer catalyst.|[Benzinga 2026-05-28] Corsair Gaming Announces That Its Elgato Brand Is Bringing MCP Support To Stream Deck, Opening The Platform To AI Assistants. [Benzinga 2026-05-27] Corsair's Big Bet On AI Compute Is Turning Heads After Hours: Here's What's Going On With CRSR Stock. Corsair Gaming shares jumped 14.09% in after-hours trading following AI compute expansion and strong earnings results.
10954|ONDG|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|50.4|12.75|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.7% gap, 5.2x rvol||ONDG is a 2x leveraged daily ETF tracking ONDS — it has no independent company-specific catalyst, and its gap is purely derivative of the underlying's price action. A leveraged-instrument move on no concrete, verifiable event is the textbook case of "gap alone is not sufficient" and never earns HIGH. No real catalyst, no narrative join, so this is not a tradeable EP setup.|ONDG is a 2X leveraged daily ETF that tracks twice the daily return of ONDS (Ondas Holdings) — it has no independent catalyst of its own. No news was found for ONDG, and any pre-market gap-up is entirely derivative of movement in the underlying ONDS stock, not a company-specific event. This is a leveraged instrument responding to price action in its underlying, not an episodic pivot with a concrete, verifiable catalyst.|
10955|KTOS|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|44.4|11.62|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 11.6% gap, 2.9x rvol||The only grounded news is a Benzinga "how much you'd have made" retrospective — a non-event with no contract, earnings, guidance, or upgrade, so there is no material company-specific catalyst to justify HIGH. The ~11.6% gap is likely sector/technical drift rather than a KTOS event, and a defense drone is a $10.5B large-cap so generic sector momentum doesn't promote it. No active narrative cohort is joined since there's no concrete drone/UAS deal here; floor verdict of routine/none holds.|The only recent news item available for KTOS is a Benzinga retrospective article about historical 5-year stock returns — this is a generic, non-event piece with no specific catalyst (no earnings figures, no contract, no guidance, no upgrade). There is no concrete, verifiable company-specific event in the provided news to explain a pre-market gap-up. The gap-up likely reflects broader defense/industrials sector momentum or technical factors rather than a material KTOS-specific catalyst.|[Benzinga 2026-05-18] Here's How Much You Would Have Made Owning Kratos Defense & Security Stock In The Last 5 Years.
10956|DPRO|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|74.4|11.54|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 11.5% gap, 6.7x rvol||DPRO has a concrete, company-specific government defense catalyst: a named Army Research Lab / Department of War counter-UAS (C-UAS) contract win, the strongest tier of the Pradeep hierarchy (government policy/defense), backed by a Needham Buy reiteration and a strategic Skip Dynamix drone-tech acquisition. The C-UAS story directly joins the active "Defense drone and UAS expansion" narrative cohort (RDW/ASPI) even though DPRO isn't a listed member, lighting the theme/narrative axes. Undisclosed contract terms and a small ~$7.5M acquisition cap it below game_changer, but a credible DoD win for |The primary catalyst is a confirmed Army Research Lab contract awarded to Draganfly and F4 Defense International to develop an AI-powered, multi-layered counter-drone (C-UAS) defense system — a concrete, named government defense contract in a high-priority military domain. This is bolstered by a Needham Buy reiteration with a $12 price target and a strategic asset acquisition of Skip Dynamix's drone tech business (~$7.5M deal). While financial terms of the Army contract were not disclosed, the defense contract is company-specific, verifiable, and highly relevant to Draganfly's core business. Relative to its $224M market cap, a DoD/Army Research Lab contract win is a meaningful and credible catalyst, though the undisclosed contract size and small acquisition keep it from game_changer territory.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-26, items ] EX-99.1 2 ex99-1.htm EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 FORM 51-102F3 MATERIAL CHANGE REPORT Item 1 Name and Address of Company Draganfly Inc. (&ldquo; Draganfly &rdquo; or the &ldquo; Company &rdquo;) 235 103 rd St. E. Saskatoon, Saskatchewan S7N 1Y8 Item 2 Date of Material Change May 15, 2026 Item 3 News Release News release disclosing the material change was disseminated through the GlobeNewswire on May 18, 2026, and filed under the Company&rsquo;s profile on SEDAR+ at www.sedarplus.ca . Item 4 Summary of Material Change On May 18, 2026, the Company announced entering into a definitive asset purchase agreement (the &ldquo; Agreement &rdquo;) with Skip Dynamix, Corporation (&ldquo; Skip Dynamix &rdquo;), pursuant to which Draganfly has agreed to acquire substantially all of the assets of Skip Dynamix&rsquo;s drone technology business (the &ldquo; Transaction &rdquo;). Skip Dynamix is a developer of ultra-low-cost, mass-producible fixed-wing unmanned aerial systems designed for long-range intelligence, surveillance and reconnaissance, electronic warfare support, logistics, and one-way missions. Item 5 Full Description of Material Change 5.1 Full Description of Material Change On May 18, 2026, the Company announced entering into the Agreement in connection with the Transaction. The aggregate purchase price for the Transaction is up to US$7,525,000 (the &ldquo; Purchase Price &rdquo;): &#9679; A cash payment of US$2,525,000 (the &ldquo; Closing Amount &rdquo;), subject to customary working capital adjustments, will be paid to Skip Dynamix at closing. &#9679; US$2,500,000 satisfiable in common shares of Draganfly (&ldquo; Draganfly Shares &rdquo;) pursuant to a special warrant issued at closing (the &ldquo; Payment Shares &rdquo;). The Payment Shares will be issued subject to the satisfaction of the applicable vesting conditions, which requires each founder to be actively engaged by Draganfly until at least the first anniversary of closing. &#9679; Up to US$2,500,000 (the &ldquo; Earn-Out Amount &rdquo;), payable in a combination of cash and Draganfly Shares as determined by Draganfly, subject to the business achieving certain milestones. Completion of the Transaction is subject to a number of closing conditions customary for a transaction of this nature, including required regulatory and exchange approvals and the satisfaction of other customary conditions precedent, and is expected to close in early June 2026. 5.2 Disclosure for Restructuring Transactions Not applicable. Item 6 Reliance on subsection 7.1(2) of National Instrument 51-102 Not applicable. Item 7 Omitted Information Not applicable. Item 8 Executive Officer Paul Sun, Chief Financial Officer Tel: 1.800.979.9794 Item 9 Date of Report May 22, 2026 Forward-Looking Statements This material change report contains certain &ldquo;forward looking statements&rdquo; and certain &ldquo;forward-looking information&rdquo; as defined under applicable securities laws. Forward-loo
10957|AVAV|2026-05-28|historical_scan|HIGH|54.0|10.29|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 10.3% gap, 3.9x rvol||The two named contracts (~$40M combined) are real but immaterial against AVAV's $9B cap (<0.5% each), routine-sized for a defense firm of this scale with no earnings, guidance, or transformative event. Neither catalyst joins the active drone/UAS narrative as a re-rating story — a small C-UAS production investment and a ceramics R&D contract are not the kind of NATO-demand re-rating driving the cohort. The 10% gap is the market's vote without a material reason behind it, so I demote below the MODERATE floor.|The two identified catalysts are a $20M CAMP contract from AFRL and an additional $20.2M government investment in its Huntsville site — totaling roughly $40M combined. While both are real, named contracts with specific dollar figures, they are immaterial relative to AVAV's $8.9B market cap, representing less than 0.5% of market cap each. Contracts of this size are routine for a defense/robotics company of this scale and do not represent a transformative business event. No earnings beat, guidance raise, or major partnership is present in the news.|[Benzinga 2026-05-28] AeroVironment Bags $20M CAMP Contract From AFRL Materials And Manufacturing Directorate To Advance Next-Gen Ceramic And CMCs For Aerospace And Defense Applications Supporting U.S. Air And Space Forces. [Benzinga 2026-05-26] AeroVironment Announces Additional $20.2M Government Investment In Its Huntsville, Alabama, Site To Raise Low-Rate Initial Production Of Counter-Unmanned Aircraft System Missile.
