ts, accessories and apparel portfolio to fully optimiz
10748|DELL|2026-05-29|live|HIGH|115.2|36.26|strong||||1.20|07:00|DELL’s latest gap-up was driven by a massive upside earnings surprise and AI-related upside in its Q1 FY27 report, which confirmed an acceleration in AI server demand and much stronger-than-expected top-line growth. Key points behind the gap higher: 1) Blowout Q1 FY27 earnings   Dell reported record quarterly revenue of roughly $43.8 billion, up about 88% year over year, essentially nearly doublin|||Dell Technologies reported earnings and raised full-year revenue and earnings guidance significantly above analyst estimates, driven by surging demand for AI infrastructure and servers. The company's guidance raise coupled with strong execution on a high-conviction AI growth thesis represents a solid catalyst that justifies the 38-40% premarket surge. This is a meaningful catalyst but falls short of "game_changer" given it's within the expected AI infrastructure narrative rather than a surprise transformative event.|
10749|CHA|2026-05-29|live|MODERATE|50.4|12.48|routine||||1.20|07:45|CHA likely gapped up on a Japan-market/AI-themed catalyst rather than a company-specific headline, because CHA is a Japan-linked equity and the strongest fresh macro driver in the news is the continued surge in Japanese stocks on AI enthusiasm, improving GDP/inflation, and foreign inflows. The most direct catalyst in the available news is the broad Japan rally, not a clearly identified CHA-specifi|||The news items reference Q1 2026 and Q4 2025 earnings calls with mentions of "4.5% revenue increase" and a "$150 million share repurchase program," but lack specific EPS numbers, actual earnings beat/miss confirmation, or forward guidance raises. The articles are primarily analyst commentary and valuation pieces ("Is It Time To Reconsider") without concrete catalytic details. The $150M buyback is a financial engineering move, not an earnings surprise or transformative event. Without verified beat numbers and guidance raise specifics, this appears to be routine quarterly results dressed up as headline news.|
10750|PD|2026-05-29|live|MODERATE|50.4|18.15|routine||||1.20|08:35|PD (PagerDuty) most recently gapped up on a combination of fundamental and event-driven catalysts rather than a single headline. The latest meaningful upside gap in PD has typically been driven by: • A stronger-than-expected quarterly earnings print (revenue and ARR growth ahead of guidance, improving operating margin, and reiteration or raise of full‑year outlook).   • Ongoing confidence in its c|||PagerDuty reported Q1 earnings that exceeded revenue expectations with a +1.50% revenue beat (hitting $121M) and a +33.33% earnings surprise, while also providing guidance that exceeded market expectations and non-GAAP operating margin guidance. The catalyst combines a solid earnings beat with new strategic initiatives (usage-based pricing shift, new CEO leadership, AI-driven growth tailwinds), which qualifies as a strong fundamental catalyst—not a game-changer magnitude but clearly positive visibility and strategic repositioning in a technology platform space.|
10751|ASAN|2026-05-29|live|MODERATE|53.3|11.56|routine||||1.20|09:45|ASAN’s latest gap up is being driven by a positive earnings surprise and AI-related growth momentum from its most recent quarterly report. The most immediate catalyst is Asana’s Q1 FY2027 earnings: the company reported EPS of $0.10 versus a $0.07 consensus, a roughly 43% beat, which is a meaningful upside surprise for a name that historically traded on revenue growth and cash burn rather than prof|||ASAN reported Q1 FY2027 earnings with revenue of $205.1M, beating guidance and exceeding market expectations (+9.5% YoY growth). The company provided guidance raises for Q2 and raised outlook driven by strong AI product adoption, improved customer retention, and expansion activity. This is a concrete earnings beat with guidance raise on a work management platform with improving AI monetization trends, meriting a "strong" classification rather than "routine" due to the specific financial metrics and forward guidance improvements.|
10752|BHVN|2026-05-29|live|MODERATE|64.8|11.47|strong||||1.20|09:50|BHVN’s latest gap-up appears to be driven by a company-specific catalyst, but the provided results do not include BHVN-specific news, so I can’t verify the exact headline behind today’s move. The only BHVN-related item in the results is a foreign stock list that identifies BHVN as BioMarin Pharmaceutical, not a news item or market catalyst. If you want the most likely explanation for a sharp biote|||Biohaven reported a narrower Q1 2026 net loss of $130.53M (improvement versus prior year) accompanied by multiple positive developments: a Zacks Rank upgrade to #2 (Buy), a new Canaccord initiator coverage with Buy rating and $21 price target, and filing of a mixed shelf registration for future funding flexibility. The combination of improved profitability metrics, analyst upgrade cluster (Zacks + Canaccord), and clear timelines for pivotal trials creates a solid positive catalyst for a neglected biotech stock.|
10960|REPL|2026-05-29|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|69.44|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 69.4% gap, 9.7x rvol||A binary regulatory catalyst — FDA alignment on a BLA resubmission for lead asset RP1, with the agency committing to prioritize the review as an "urgent matter" — is a company-defining event for a $727M clinical-stage biotech with no approved products, reversing a prior CRL setback and opening a credible path to first commercial approval. The 69% gap reflects genuine regulatory de-risking, not boilerplate, and is transformative relative to a single-asset pipeline company of this size. No active narrative cohort applies (oncolytic immunotherapy is not the live drone/nuclear stories), so theme/n|The catalyst is a planned BLA resubmission for RP1 (vusolimogene oderparepvec) in combination with nivolumab for advanced melanoma, following productive collaborative dialogue with the FDA. Critically, the FDA has indicated it will treat the resubmission as an "urgent matter" and will prioritize its review — a highly significant signal for a clinical-stage biotech with a $725M market cap and no approved products. This represents a clear path to potential FDA approval for Replimune's lead asset after a prior setback, which is a transformative, company-defining event that could unlock commercial-stage status for the first time.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-29, items 7.01,9.01] false 0001737953 0001737953 2026-05-29 2026-05-29 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 29, 2026 REPLIMUNE GROUP, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-38596 82-2082553 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification Number) 500 Unicorn Park Drive Suite 303 Woburn , MA 0