10961|PD|2026-05-29|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|25.40|strong|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 25.4% gap, 5.4x rvol||The catalyst is an earnings beat-and-buyback, but the substance is weak: revenue grew only 1% YoY with flat ARR ($496M) and no guidance raise, and the $100M repurchase merely replaces a prior completed program. Per the hierarchy this is a margin/profitability beat with no theme, no sales acceleration, and no narrative-cohort match (the active cohorts are defense-drone and nuclear-AI). A sluggish-growth SaaS name gapping on a routine in-line-ish print with a recycled buyback does not clear the bar for HIGH despite the deterministic material deal-ratio flag.|PagerDuty reported Q1 FY2027 earnings with revenue of $121.0M (+1% YoY) and non-GAAP operating income of $29.7M (24.6% margin), both exceeding guidance. The company also announced a new $100M share repurchase program and delivered its fourth consecutive quarter of GAAP profitability ($10.2M net income). While top-line growth remains sluggish (1% YoY, flat ARR at $496M), the beat-and-buyback combination on a ~$661M market cap stock is a meaningful catalyst, though the lack of a meaningful guidance raise and stagnant ARR tempers enthusiasm below game_changer territory.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-28, items 2.02,8.01,9.01] pd-20260527 FALSE 0001568100 0001568100 2026-05-27 2026-05-27 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 _________________________ FORM 8-K _________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 27, 2026 _________________________ PAGERDUTY, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) _________________________ Delaware 001-38856 27-2793871 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 600 Townsend St. , Suite 200 San Francisco , California 94103 (Address of Principal Execut