10967|CHA|2026-05-29|historical_scan|HIGH|74.4|14.67|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 14.7% gap, 9.3x rvol||Concrete, verified earnings beat (~65% EPS, ~13% revenue) is a real material catalyst for a $2.3B name, easily clearing the HIGH bar over a bare gap. However, declining YoY operating income/GAAP net income, softening Greater China GMV, and the absence of any forward guidance raise cap this at strong rather than game_changer. No active theme/narrative cohort match (tea retailer, not defense/nuclear), so only the catalyst axis fires.|Chagee reported Q1 2026 results with adjusted EPS of $0.38 vs. $0.23 estimate (~65% beat) and revenue of $514M vs. $456M estimate (~13% beat), both concrete and verified with specific figures. However, operating income and GAAP net income declined year-over-year (RMB547M vs. RMB821M and RMB448M vs. RMB677M respectively), and Greater China GMV softened due to economic headwinds and competition — tempering the euphoria. No forward guidance raise was mentioned in the filing, which prevents a game_changer classification despite the strong top- and bottom-line beats.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-05-29, items ] EX-99.1 2 tm2615738d1_ex99-1.htm EXHIBIT 99.1 Exhibit 99.1 Chagee Announces First Quarter 2026 Unaudited Financial Results SHANGHAI, May 29, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Chagee Holdings Limited (NASDAQ: CHA) (&ldquo;Chagee&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;), a leading premium tea drinks brand serving healthy and delicious freshly-made tea drinks, today announced its unaudited financial results for the first quarter ended March 31, 2026. First Quarter 2026 Operational Highlights 1 &middot; As of March 31, 2026, there were 7,531 teahouses within the Company&rsquo;s teahouse network in Greater China and overseas, representing a 12.7% increase in the number of teahouses as of March 31, 2025. &middot; Total GMV generated in the first quarter of 2026 was RMB7,917.8 million. Geographically, total GMV generated in overseas markets was RMB426.4 million in the first quarter of 2026, representing a 139.0% year-over-year increase; total GMV generated in Greater China market was RMB7,491.4 million, compared to RMB8,048.4 million in the same quarter of 2025. &middot; Average monthly GMV per teahouse in Greater China was RMB356,080 in the first quarter of 2026, representing a 5.5% increase from RMB337,358 in the fourth quarter of 2025. &middot; Chagee had 50.0 million active members in the first quarter of 2026, representing an 11.7% increase from the fourth quarter of 2025. First Quarter 2026 Financial Highlights &middot; Net revenues were RMB3,546.0 million (US$514.1 million), compared to RMB3,392.7 million in the same quarter of 2025. &middot; Operating income in the first quarter of 2026 was RMB547.2 million (US$79.3 million), compared to RMB820.8 million in the same quarter of 2025. &middot; GAAP net income was RMB447.7 million (US$64.9 million), compared to RMB677.3 million in the same quarter of 2025. &middot; Non-GAAP net income, which adjusts for share-based compensation expenses in the amount of RMB59.0 million, was RMB506.7 million (US$73.5 million), compared to RMB677.3 million in the same quarter of 2025. 1 Please refer to the section &ldquo;Key Definitions&rdquo; for detailed definitions on certain terms used. 1 First Quarter 2026 Financial Results Total net revenues were RMB3,546.0 million (US$514.1 million), compared to RMB3,392.7 million in the same quarter of 2025. &middot; Net revenues from franchised teahouses in the first quarter of 2026 were RMB2,743.9 million (US$397.8 million), compared to RMB3,149.9 million in the same quarter of 2025. This was mainly attributable to a decrease in total GMV in Greater China resulting from the economic headwinds as well as intense industry competition. Net revenues from franchised teahouses represented 77.4% of the Company&rsquo;s total net revenues for the first quarter of 2026. &middot; Net revenues from company-owned teahouses in the first quarter of 2026 were RMB802.1 million (US$116.3 million), representing an increase of 230.4% from RMB242.8 million in the same quar
10968|NXT|2026-05-29|historical_scan|HIGH|44.4|13.70|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 13.7% gap, 2.4x rvol||NXT is the ACQUIRER (buying Prevalon), so M&A cap rules don't apply; the deal is a real, material catalyst paired with a concrete FY27 revenue guidance raise ($3.8–4.1B → $4.0–4.4B) backed by 6 GWh deployed BESS and 1.3 GW of firm AI/hyperscaler contracts. Entry into the BESS + AI-data-center power market is a strategically meaningful platform expansion that taps the live AI-power-demand theme, justifying promotion above the none floor. The $365M price is only ~2% of cap so this is strong rather than game_changer, but the guidance raise plus new high-growth market entry clears the bar for HIGH|Nextpower (NXT) announced a definitive agreement to acquire Prevalon Energy for up to $365M, entering the Battery Energy Storage (BESS) and AI Data Center markets — strategically transformative for a $17.7B solar infrastructure company. Critically, this is an ACQUIRING company (NXT is buying Prevalon, not being bought), so MNA cap rules do not apply. Alongside the deal, NXT raised its FY2027 revenue outlook to $4.0B–$4.4B from a prior $3.8B–$4.1B, a meaningful guidance raise backed by Prevalon's 6 GWh of deployed BESS and 1.3 GW in firm AI/hyperscaler supply contracts. The $365M deal size is modest (~2% of NXT's $17.7B market cap), but the combination of a guidance raise, new high-growth market entry (AI data centers, BESS), and strategic expansion of the platform elevates this above a routine catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-28, items 3.02,7.01,9.01] nxt-20260528 false 0001852131 0001852131 2026-05-28 2026-05-28 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, DC 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 28, 2026 Nextpower Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-41617 36-5047383 (State or other jurisd