10969|HPE|2026-05-29|historical_scan|HIGH|32.4|11.96|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.0% gap, 6.3x rvol||The gap is a sympathy/read-through move off Dell's Q1 AI-server beat, not an HPE-specific catalyst — no HPE earnings, guidance, contract, or upgrade exists in the corpus. Sector momentum and broad market drift never earn HIGH on their own, and HPE's $60B cap further dilutes any read-through. Stays routine/none.|The gap-up in HPE appears to be driven by sector momentum from Dell's blowout Q1 earnings beat on AI demand, which lifted HPE as a sympathetic/read-through play — not by any HPE-specific catalyst. There are no HPE earnings, guidance raise, contract, or upgrade details in the news. The most recent HPE-specific headline is simply that HPE stock "jumped" in reaction to Dell's results, which is a sector-momentum move, not a company-specific episodic pivot.|[Benzinga 2026-05-29] Stock Market Today: S&P 500, Dow Futures Inch Up As US-Iran Deal Awaits Trump Approval — Dell, Agilent, Hewlett Packard Enterprise In Focus. U.S. stock futures edged up on Friday after closing higher on Thursday, with all the major indexes gaining as investors kept a close watch on the Iran war developments. The U.S. and Iran have reportedly reached an agreement to extend the ongoing ceasefire by 60 days, but it is currently awaiting final approval from President Donald Trump. [Benzinga 2026-05-28] Hewlett Packard Enterprise Stock Jumps After Dell's Massive Q1 Beat On AI Demand. Dell&#39;s blowout Q1 results and optimistic AI server revenue outlook boost HPE stock. [Benzinga 2026-05-21] If You Invested $100 In Hewlett Packard Stock 5 Years Ago, You Would Have This Much Today.
