10753|NOW|2026-06-01|live|MODERATE|54.7|10.31|strong|||theme|1.20|07:20|NOW’s latest gap-up was driven primarily by a string of AI-focused partnership headlines and a bullish Wall Street call, with the core catalyst being a new multi‑year AI partnership with Experian that the market is treating as a major agentic‑AI workflow win. Key catalysts behind the gap and follow‑through: 1) Experian AI partnership (primary driver) ServiceNow announced a global, multi‑year deal |ServiceNow's gap-up is driven by validation as a key beneficiary of the broader agentic-AI secular trend, amplified by Nvidia CEO endorsement and multi-year AI partnerships (Experian, Wipro); this is a theme-level driver shared across AI infrastructure/platform beneficiaries, not idiosyncratic to NO||The primary catalyst for NOW's pre-market surge is validation from Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang regarding agentic AI opportunities for software partners, specifically calling out ServiceNow. This represents a major partnership validation and positive sentiment amplification from a market leader, positioning NOW as a key beneficiary of the agentic AI trend. Combined with ServiceNow's expanded enterprise AI partnerships (Experian, Wipro) and multi-year contracts, this creates momentum for the stock and suggests strong bullish analyst sentiment ahead.|
10754|TNDM|2026-06-01|live|MODERATE|54.7|10.52|strong|||sales_acceleration|1.20|08:45|Tandem Diabetes Care (TNDM) most recently gapped up on a combination of improving sentiment around its growth and financing profile, not on a single, dramatic company-specific event like an FDA approval or M&A. The key identifiable recent catalyst has been its upsized 0% convertible note offering, which was increased to about $265 million due to strong demand. That kind of upsizing and zero‑coupon|TNDM's gap-up reflects a multi-quarter revenue/earnings inflection and beat-and-raise execution (Q3 beat + positive full-year EBITDA guidance reaffirmation), demonstrating idiosyncratic sales acceleration and margin improvement in the insulin pump market, not a theme, policy, or supply driver.||Tandem Diabetes Care (TNDM) beat Q3 2025 expectations on revenue and earnings, exceeded analyst views, and reaffirmed positive EBITDA guidance for full-year 2025. The 16.7% gap-up reflects investor enthusiasm for the company's ability to deliver results while maintaining its profitability roadmap, a significant validation for a healthcare/medical device company in a competitive insulin pump market.|
10755|SAIC|2026-06-01|live|MODERATE|50.4|15.51|routine|||sales_acceleration|1.20|09:45|SAIC gapped up on its latest earnings report, which came in better than expectations and reset guidance/contract momentum higher, prompting a positive repricing of the stock. Key points on the catalyst and news flow: 1) Earnings release timing   Science Applications International (SAIC) reported quarterly results this morning before the open, and the stock was explicitly on traders’ “earnings rada|SAIC gapped on an earnings beat (better-than-expected revenue of $1.91B) with reset contract momentum and guidance improvement—a company-specific multi-quarter earnings inflection reaction, not a sector theme, policy driver, or structural supply shortage.||SAIC reported Q1 CY2026 earnings with better-than-expected revenue of $1.91 billion, up 1.5% year-over-year, beating analyst expectations. The news explicitly states "upbeat" results and "stock soars," indicating a solid earnings beat that drove the pre-market gap-up. This qualifies as a strong catalyst: concrete earnings beat with positive sentiment, though the news does not mention a formal guidance raise or analyst upgrade cluster, preventing a game-changer classification.|
10756|ALOY|2026-06-01|live|HIGH|86.4|14.25|strong|||policy|1.20|09:55|ALOY gapped up on a new strategic rare-earth supply MOU announced with Ramaco Resources. REalloys said the non-binding agreement could give it rights to up to 20% of future mixed rare earth carbonate production from Ramaco’s Brook Mine in Wyoming, which the market is likely interpreting as a major step toward a U.S.-based mine-to-magnet supply chain.[1] The catalyst is fundamentally a supply-chain|U.S. domestic rare-earth supply chain development driven by Pentagon's 2027 China ban and critical minerals security policy, not a theme (all peers benefit equally), sales beat, or isolated company news—this is a geopolitical/regulatory mandate reshaping supply access.||The primary catalyst is REalloys' 15-year offtake agreement with Greenland's Tanbreez project securing heavy rare earths (dysprosium and terbium), which addresses critical supply chain concerns ahead of the Pentagon's 2027 China ban. This is a concrete, multi-decade contract win that directly addresses geopolitical supply chain risk and demonstrates the company's ability to secure alternative rare earth sources outside China, validating the fundamental investment thesis. Combined with broad rare earth sector strength following recent funding news and easing of China's export restrictions, this positions ALOY as a beneficiary of structural tailwinds in rare earth supply diversification.|
10757|SKM|2026-06-01|live|MODERATE|50.4|10.69|strong|||theme|1.00|09:55|SK Telecom Co. (SKM) has not had a clear, stock-specific positive catalyst reported in the very latest news; the recent notable move has actually been a decline tied to sector and macro factors rather than a gap higher. Recent price action commentary points to SKM dropping around 3–4% on elevated volume, with weakness attributed to: - Pressure on the broader telecom sector from higher interest-rat|SK Telecom's strategic partnership with Arm and Rebellions to build AI inference infrastructure is part of the broader AI infrastructure/data-center secular tailwind shared across telecom and infrastructure peers, not idiosyncratic to SKM alone—this positions the company within an industry-wide them||SK Telecom announced a major strategic collaboration with Arm Holdings and Rebellions to build AI inference infrastructure using Arm's new data center CPU (Neoverse CSS V3). This is a transformative partnership positioning SK Telecom as a key player in the enterprise AI infrastructure buildout, directly benefiting from the surge in AI demand and enterprise adoption. The partnership with Arm—a dominant semiconductor licensing company—represents significant validation and positions SK Telecom in a high-growth adjacency beyond traditional telecom services.|
10972|ELMT|2026-06-01|historical_scan|HIGH|96.0|24.67|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 24.7% gap, 11.3x rvol||Concrete, verifiable earnings catalyst: revenue +20.7%, adjusted EBITDA +106% to 16.4% margin, adjusted EPS $0.24 vs $0.10, and a record backlog up ~52% YoY to $113.3M signaling genuine ADG demand acceleration on a freshly-IPO'd, under-followed $567M name — a real company-specific event, not boilerplate. It does not join any active narrative cohort (defense-drone cohort is autonomous systems, a different story) so theme/narrative axes don't fire, capping it short of game_changer. Sales acceleration ranks lower in the Pradeep hierarchy than theme/policy, so I hold HIGH but trim to strong rather|ELMT reported Q1 FY2026 earnings with concrete, verifiable figures: revenue up 20.7% YoY to $56.0M, adjusted EBITDA more than doubled (+106%) to $9.2M (16.4% margin vs. 9.6% prior year), adjusted EPS of $0.24 vs. $0.10 prior year, and gross margin expanded 260bps to 21.2%. Most strikingly, the open order backlog surged ~52% YoY to a record $113.3M, signaling strong forward demand acceleration in Aerospace, Defense & Government — a highly favored sector. For a ~$561M market cap industrial company on Nasdaq with what appears to be a recently completed IPO (raising $125.5M), this combination of explosive EBITDA growth, margin expansion, and record backlog on a still-neglected emerging public company represents a high-quality, company-specific earnings catalyst consistent with a game-changer classification.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-05-29, items 2.02,9.01] false 0002101698 0002101698 2026-05-29 2026-05-29 iso4217:USD xbrli:shares iso4217:USD xbrli:shares UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(d) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): May 29, 2026 The Elmet Group Co. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaw