10988|NVTS|2026-06-03|historical_scan|HIGH|57.6|18.50|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 18.5% gap, 3.4x rvol||The only event is a soft PR mention of participation in Nvidia's partner ceremony at Computex — no contract, revenue, or binding agreement, so there is no concrete, material catalyst to anchor a sustained EP move on a $5B-cap name. The Nvidia brand halo and AI-buildout theme provide ambient lift but "trade-show participation" is boilerplate and does not constitute joining a cohort's specific story. Per the rubric a gap alone never earns HIGH, and here the catalyst is immaterial, so I demote below the floor.|The only news item is a Benzinga article noting Navitas Semiconductor's participation in Nvidia's Partner Ceremony at the Computex Forum in Taipei. This is a soft, PR-style event mention — no specific contract value, no revenue figures, no earnings beat, no guidance raise, and no binding agreement announced. While association with Nvidia carries brand halo, "participation in a partner ceremony" at a trade show is a vague, non-material event relative to Navitas's $5.0B market cap. No concrete, verifiable catalyst can be identified to justify a sustained EP move.|[Benzinga 2026-06-03] Navitas Semiconductor Notes Participation In Nvidia's Partner Ceremony At Computex Forum In Taipei.
10989|GME|2026-06-03|historical_scan|HIGH|72.0|11.28|game_changer|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 11.3% gap, 2.9x rvol||Concrete, company-specific catalyst: record Q1 results (net income $389.6M vs $44.8M, operating income swinging from a loss to $143.3M) confirmed by an 8-K/EX-99, plus a $2.0B buyback that is ~20% of the $9.9B cap — clearly material and earns HIGH. The earnings inflection is real but a large chunk of net income comes from non-operating digital-asset/derivative gains (adjusted net income $179.3M), so it's strong rather than a true game_changer. No active theme or narrative cohort participation, so theme/narrative axes stay dark.|GameStop reported Q1 FY2026 earnings (quarter ended May 2, 2026) with record-breaking results: net sales of $835.3M (+14% YoY), highest quarterly net income in company history at $389.6M (vs. $44.8M prior year), and highest first quarter operating income in history at $143.3M (vs. an operating loss of $10.8M prior year). Alongside these blowout results, the Board approved a new $2.0 billion share repurchase authorization, signaling aggressive capital return to shareholders. The combination of a dramatic earnings inflection — swinging from operating losses to record profits — plus a massive $2B buyback on a ~$9.9B market cap company constitutes a transformative, company-specific catalyst of the highest order.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-06-02, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] gme-20260602 0001326380 false 0001326380 2026-06-02 2026-06-02 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K Current Report Pursuant To Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): June 2, 2026 GameStop Corp. (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 1-32637 20-2733559 (State or Other Jurisdiction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 625 Westport Parkway , Grapevine , TX 76051 ( 817 ) 424-2000 (Address, Inc