10767|MRLN|2026-06-05|live|MODERATE|60.0|27.99|routine|||other|1.00|07:00|MRLN gapped up on news that Merlin Inc. successfully completed a critical design review for its autonomous planes, which triggered a sharp re‑rating of the stock and heavy speculative buying in premarket trade. Specifically, coverage this morning highlighted that Merlin Inc. wrapped up its critical design review for its autonomous aircraft platform, and the stock was indicated up about 40% in earl|Critical design review completion is a routine engineering milestone with no concrete revenue impact, customer contract, or regulatory approval—a pedestrian developmental checkpoint typical of pre-revenue aerospace programs, lacking the specificity and binding commercial substance needed for theme, ||The reported catalyst is the completion of a "critical design review" for Merlin's autonomous aircraft platform — a developmental milestone, not a concrete revenue-generating event. There are no specific numbers (contract value, revenue, EPS, guidance figures), no named customer or government counterparty, and no binding commercial agreement mentioned. Critical design reviews are internal/regulatory engineering checkpoints that are common in aerospace development and carry no guaranteed path to commercialization or cash flows, making this a low-quality, non-verifiable catalyst typical of pre-revenue defense tech companies. The 40% gap appears driven by speculative momentum rather than a concrete, fundamental company event.|
10768|TTAN|2026-06-05|live|HIGH|100.8|16.28|strong|||sales_acceleration|1.20|07:00|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-06-04, items 2.02,9.01] TTAN (ServiceTitan) gapped up on the back of a strong earnings print and upbeat guidance. The latest clear catalyst was the company’s fiscal Q1 2027 report released on June 4. ServiceTitan posted revenue of about $268.8 million, up roughly 25% year over year, with platform revenue of about $260.6 million and gross transaction volume of $21.7 billion. At |ServiceTitan posted a beat-and-raise earnings report (25% YoY revenue growth, margin expansion, and bullish forward guidance), which is a company-specific multi-quarter revenue inflection with no sector-wide theme, policy, or shortage driver; this is textbook sales_acceleration.||ServiceTitan reported fiscal Q1 2027 results on June 4, 2026, posting revenue of ~$268.8M (+25% YoY) with non-GAAP operating income of ~$40.8M, demonstrating meaningful margin improvement alongside top-line growth. Management issued bullish forward guidance of ~$284–286M for Q2 and ~$1.13–1.14B for full-year FY2027, implying sustained mid-20s growth. The combination of a solid revenue beat, improving profitability metrics (narrowing GAAP operating loss), and an upbeat guidance raise is a textbook strong EP catalyst — though it falls short of "game_changer" given TTAN is an established, well-followed SaaS name rather than a neglected one.|
10769|AGX|2026-06-05|live|HIGH|86.4|10.96|game_changer|||sales_acceleration|1.20|07:05|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-06-04, items 2.02,9.01] AGX (Argan Inc.) gapped up on the back of a very strong earnings print released after yesterday’s close, which materially beat expectations and highlighted record results. Key latest catalyst: Argan reported record Q1 FY2027 results on June 4: - Revenue of about $291 million, up roughly 50% year over year. - Gross margin of about 21%. - Net income around|AGX gapped on a material earnings beat (+50% YoY revenue, $3.24 EPS vs. expectations) with record Q1 results and a $2.8B backlog — a company-specific multi-quarter revenue/earnings inflection, idiosyncratic to Argan and not part of a broader sector theme, policy driver, or supply shortage.||Argan reported record Q1 FY2027 earnings on June 4, 2026, with revenue of ~$291M (+50% YoY), EPS of ~$3.24 diluted, adjusted EBITDA of ~$56M, and a massive $2.8B backlog alongside ~$1.0B in cash — all concrete, verifiable figures. The scale of top-line growth, strong margins (~21% gross), and fortress balance sheet represent a material positive earnings surprise on a relatively under-followed industrial name. This combination of a massive beat, record metrics, and a visibility-rich backlog driving a stock repricing qualifies as a game-changer catalyst.|
10991|MRLN|2026-06-05|historical_scan|HIGH|80.0|27.99|strong|HIGH|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 28.0% gap, 18.7x rvol||Concrete, verifiable company-specific milestone: Merlin passed Critical Design Review for its C-130J autonomy program with USSOCOM, a prestigious military customer — a real de-risking event that validates the tech and points toward a funded production contract. The ~39% AH reaction confirms the market read it as material for a $662M defense-AI name. Held at strong rather than game_changer because no contract dollar value or revenue inflection is disclosed, and the AI-silicon cohort is a sector adjacency, not this defense-autonomy story.|The specific catalyst is the completion of a Critical Design Review (CDR) for Merlin's C-130J autonomy program with USSOCOM (U.S. Special Operations Command) — a concrete, verifiable military program milestone announced after the close on June 4, 2026, triggering a ~39% after-hours spike. For a $676M market cap aerospace/defense AI company, successfully passing a CDR with a prestigious U.S. military customer (USSOCOM) is a significant de-risking event that validates the technology and strongly implies progression toward a funded production contract. While no contract dollar value is disclosed, the strategic importance of USSOCOM backing and the magnitude of the price reaction support a "strong" classification — it is a clear, company-specific, verifiable catalyst, though not quite "game_changer" territory without a confirmed contract value or revenue inflection.|[Benzinga 2026-06-05] Merlin Clears Critical Design Review, Stock Rockets Higher. Merlin (NASDAQ: MRLN) shares are trading higher Friday after completing Critical Design Review for its C-130J autonomy program with USSOCOM. [Benzinga 2026-06-05] Merlin Stock Is Trending Overnight — Here's Why It Spiked Over 30% In After-Hours Session. Merlin shares jumped 39.28% in after-hours trading after completing the Critical Design Review for its USSOCOM-backed C-130J autonomy program. [Benzinga 2026-06-04] Merlin Stock Soars After The Close: Here's Why. Merlin shares are rising after hours on Thursday after the company announced it completed critical design review for its C-130J autonomy program.
10992|ETHD|2026-06-05|historical_scan|HIGH|40.0|12.44|routine|none|floor||1.00|09:35|Historical scan: 12.4% gap, 3.4x rvol||ETHD is a -2x inverse Ether ETF; its gap is a purely mechanical derivative move reflecting a decline in ETH, not a company-specific catalyst. There is no earnings, contract, policy, or theme event — no EP-qualifying catalyst exists. Gap+volume alone never earns HIGH, so it stays routine.|ETHD is a leveraged inverse ETF (-2x) designed to track the daily inverse performance of Ether (ETH). No company-specific news was found. The gap-up is almost certainly driven by a significant decline in the price of Ether in the crypto market, which mechanically causes this inverse ETF to rise — this is a derivative/mechanical price move, not a company-specific catalyst. There is no earnings event, guidance, contract, or any other EP-qualifying catalyst present.|
