12322|WEN|2026-06-24|live|MODERATE|54.0|25.34|routine|MODERATE|judge|management_change|1.00|09:00|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-06-23, items 5.02,7.01,9.01] WEN’s latest gap up is tied to company-specific news: the appointment of Steve Cirulis as Chief Financial Officer and Chief Strategy Officer, effective June 23, 2026. This executive change is being treated as the primary fresh catalyst and has driven a stock-specific move rather than a broad sector rotation. Context and detail: Wendy’s announced tha|Steve Cirulis appointment as CFO and Chief Strategy Officer is a routine executive transition with no disclosed earnings, guidance, or financial metrics; this is a structural management change but lacks the profile of a high-impact leadership pivot.|The fresh, SEC-sourced catalyst is a CFO/Chief Strategy Officer appointment — a management change, the weakest rung of the Pradeep hierarchy, with no earnings, revenue, guidance, or contract attached. A single exec swap rarely justifies a sustained EP move and does not warrant promotion above the routine floor despite the large gap and 100th-percentile volume, which alone are never sufficient for HIGH. The relevant turnaround pedigree (Cirulis/Wright from Potbelly) hints at a future story but is not itself a material, near-term financial driver.|The catalyst is a CFO transition announcement: Wendy's appointed Steve Cirulis as CFO and Chief Strategy Officer, replacing Ken Cook, effective June 23, 2026. While Cirulis brings relevant turnaround experience from Potbelly (where he partnered with current CEO Bob Wright), a CFO appointment is a routine management change — there are no earnings results, guidance raises, revenue figures, major contracts, or analyst upgrades disclosed. Leadership changes of this nature are not company-specific financial catalysts that justify a sustained EP move, and the gap-up, if real, lacks a concrete fundamental driver to support momentum trading.|
12323|MU|2026-06-25|live|HIGH|96.0|17.71|game_changer|HIGH|judge|shortage|1.20|07:00|Micron reported record fiscal Q3 2026 results with revenue of $41.46B — a massive 74% sequential surge from $23.86B and a staggering 346% year-over-year increase from $9.30B — accompanied by an 84.6% GAAP gross margin and $24.67 diluted EPS. The press release also highlights "even stronger outlook for Q4" (guidance raise) and the execution of multi-year "transformational Strategic Customer Agreeme|Micron's 346% YoY revenue surge and record margins reflect structural supply-demand imbalance in memory chips (DRAM/NAND) driven by AI infrastructure buildout and data center capacity constraints, not merely company-specific execution—the transformational customer agreements lock in this sector-wide|Fresh, primary-sourced 8-K earnings (filed today) show record revenue of $41.46B — +74% Q/Q and +346% Y/Y — with gross margin exploding to 84.6%, a Q4 guidance raise, and multi-year "transformational Strategic Customer Agreements," the load-bearing revenue-acceleration signal that the market pays for on a growth/AI-memory name. This rides the active AI/memory super-cycle theme and is unambiguously material even at $1.18T market cap, so the materiality concern is resolved upward despite no separate web direct source. The catalyst is verified, dated, and revenue-driven — game_changer holds.|Micron reported record fiscal Q3 2026 results with revenue of $41.46B — a massive 74% sequential surge from $23.86B and a staggering 346% year-over-year increase from $9.30B — accompanied by an 84.6% GAAP gross margin and $24.67 diluted EPS. The press release also highlights "even stronger outlook for Q4" (guidance raise) and the execution of multi-year "transformational Strategic Customer Agreements" designed to enhance durability and predictability of revenue. The combination of record-shattering revenue growth, explosive margin expansion, a forward guidance raise, and transformative long-term customer agreements represents one of the strongest earnings catalysts possible for a semiconductor name of this scale.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-06-24, items 2.02,9.01] mu-20260624 0000723125 FALSE 0000723125 2026-06-24 2026-06-24 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 June 24, 2026 Date of Report (date of earliest event reported) MICRON TECHNOLOGY, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 1-10658 75-1618004 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 8000 South Federal Way Boise , Idaho 83716 -9632 (Address of principal executive offices and Zip Code) ( 208 ) 368-4000 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading symbol Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, par value $0.10 per share MU Nasdaq Global Select Market Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use