12324|SNX|2026-06-25|live|HIGH|72.0|11.22|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:40|TD SYNNEX reported record fiscal Q2 2026 results with revenue of $19.6B (+31% YoY), significantly above the high end of guidance, and non-GAAP diluted EPS of $4.85 (+62.2% YoY), also significantly above the high end of outlook. This is a concrete, fresh earnings release (SEC 8-K filed June 25, 2026) with massive beats on both revenue and EPS accompanied by a 9% dividend increase, indicating strong|TD SYNNEX reported a multi-quarter earnings inflection with record revenue (+31% YoY), a massive EPS beat (+62.2% YoY, far above guidance), and a 9% dividend hike—a company-specific idiosyncratic beat-and-raise with no evidence of a sector-wide theme or policy driver, placing it in the sales_acceler|Fresh, primary-source earnings (8-K filed 2026-06-25) show revenue +31% YoY to $19.6B significantly above the high end of guidance — genuine top-line acceleration, the load-bearing signal for HIGH, not just an EPS beat. This clears the catalyst bar and justifies HIGH/strong. But $19.6B revenue on a $22.8B distributor is a thin-margin (6.8% gross) business with no theme or narrative alignment, so I trim game_changer to strong; record-quarter distribution beats rarely sustain Lane-1-level momentum.|TD SYNNEX reported record fiscal Q2 2026 results with revenue of $19.6B (+31% YoY), significantly above the high end of guidance, and non-GAAP diluted EPS of $4.85 (+62.2% YoY), also significantly above the high end of outlook. This is a concrete, fresh earnings release (SEC 8-K filed June 25, 2026) with massive beats on both revenue and EPS accompanied by a 9% dividend increase, indicating strong forward momentum. The combination of record revenue, dramatic top-line acceleration, and a substantial EPS beat far above guidance across both Distribution and Hyve segments qualifies this as a game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-06-25, items 2.02,9.01] snx-20260625 0001177394 false 16202 Ba