ecause there is no earnings/guidance raise directly tied to today's news, and the Q1 beat details are not freshly disclosed today.|[Benzinga 2026-07-01] Morgan Stanley Upgrades Grindr to Overweight, Raises Price Target to $18. [Web summary] GRND likely gapped up on the Morgan Stanley upgrade, which raised Grindr from Equalweight to Overweight and lifted the price target to $18 from $15. The firm said the move was driven by upcoming product catalysts, especially the ultra-premium EDGE tier and the new telehealth service Woodwork.[1] The immediate news flow also included continued bullish commentary around Grindr’s growth setup, with Morgan Stanley citing a product-led monetization pivot and room for the company to close the monetization gap versus other dating apps.[1] Another supporting catalyst was the company’s recent first-quarter 2026 results, which beat revenue expectations, plus prior positive commentary from other firms and leadership changes at the board level.[1] If you want, I can also break down whether the gap looks driven more by the analyst upgrade, the product launch roadmap, or the Q1 earnings momentum.
