12339|TSEM|2026-07-14|live|HIGH|80.0|18.57|game_changer|HIGH|judge|policy|1.00|07:00|Tower Semiconductor filed a 6-K on July 14, 2026 announcing a Japan government (METI)-backed strategic capacity expansion for 300mm Silicon Photonics, Silicon Germanium, and advanced packaging — a transformative, government-supported manufacturing scale-up directly tied to AI/data-center demand. Critically, Tower simultaneously raised its forward business model targets to $3.6B in revenue and $1.2|Japan government (METI) subsidy/backing for transformative 300mm capacity expansion in AI-critical Silicon Photonics and advanced packaging is a structural policy driver; the simultaneous massive guidance raise ($3.6B 2028 target vs. $3.19B consensus) is a secondary earnings inflection enabled by th|Fresh primary-source 6-K (July 14, 2026) confirms a METI/Japan-government-backed dual-track 300mm SiPho/SiGe capacity expansion tied directly to AI/data-center demand — the strongest tier of Pradeep catalyst (theme + government policy) with a direct SEC filing. It carries a concrete forward guidance RAISE to $3.6B revenue / $1.2B net profit for 2028 (~13% above ~$3.19B consensus), the load-bearing revenue signal for a growth name. Materiality is transformative and freshness is established via primary source, so HIGH/game_changer holds despite the direct-source flag being absent in metadata.|Tower Semiconductor filed a 6-K on July 14, 2026 announcing a Japan government (METI)-backed strategic capacity expansion for 300mm Silicon Photonics, Silicon Germanium, and advanced packaging — a transformative, government-supported manufacturing scale-up directly tied to AI/data-center demand. Critically, Tower simultaneously raised its forward business model targets to $3.6B in revenue and $1.2B in net profit for 2028, well above the prior Street consensus of ~$3.19B — a massive, specific guidance raise on a growth name. The combination of a government-backed transformative capacity expansion (dual-track, multi-fold capacity increase) with a concrete and substantial guidance raise (~13% revenue beat vs. consensus) on a $26B market-cap company with clear AI optical connectivity tailwinds qualifies as a game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-07-14, items ] 6-K 1 zk2635682.htm 6-K UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION W ashington, D.C. 20549 FORM 6-K REPORT OF FOREIGN PRIVATE ISSUER PURSUANT TO RULE 13a-16 OR 15d-16 OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 F or the month of July 2026 No.3 Commission File Number 0-24790 TOWER SEMICONDUCTOR LTD. (Translation of registrant's name into English) Ramat Gavriel Industrial Park P.O. Box 619, Migdal Haemek, Israel 2310502 (Address of principal executive offices) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant files or will file annual reports under cover of Form 20-F or Form 40-F. Form 20-F &#9746; Form 40-F &#9744; On July 14, 2026, the Registrant Announces Tower Semiconductor with METI Support Announces Strategic Capacity Expansion in Japan SIGNATURES Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned, thereunto duly authorized. TOWER SEMICONDUCTOR LTD. Date: July 14, 2026 By: /s/ Nati Somekh Name: Nati Somekh Title: Corporate Secretary Tower Semiconductor with METI Support Announces Strategic Capacity Expansion in Japan Significant Multiples of Silicon Photonics and Silicon Germanium Capacity to Support Accelerating Customer Demand MIGDAL HAEMEK, Israel, July 14, 2026 &#8211; Tower Semiconductor (NASDAQ/TASE: TSEM), a leading foundry of high-value analog semiconductor solutions, today announced a parallel dual-track strategic expansion of its 300mm Silicon Photonics (SiPho), Silicon Germanium (SiGe), and advanced packaging capabilities in Japan, with support from the Government of Japan. The expansion is designed to support the rapidly growing long-term customer demand, substantially increasing the Company&#8217;s manufacturing capacity and extending its technology leadership. Russell Ellwanger, Tower&#8217;s CEO, stated: &#8220;We are honored and appreciative that the Government of Japan has selected Tower to lead the expansion of these strategically important technologies. Together, we are building a globally differentiated center of excellence founded on technology leadership, manufacturing excellence, and exceptional product quality. Since becoming the majority owner of the former Panasonic Semiconductor manufacturing operations, now TPSCo, this group has established a reputation for transforming cutting-edge innovation into high-volume manufacturing excellence. For these reasons, with the support of the Government of Japan, we will create a globally differentiated, advanced R&D and manufacturing center of excellence for Silicon Photonics, Silicon Germanium, and advanced optical packaging of very significant scale. By combining Tower's specialized technology leadership with Japan's unparalleled manufacturing expertise, world-class research institutions, and deeply committed workforce, we are building a strategic platform that will drive innovation, economic growth, and semiconductor leadership for decades
12340|CLSK|2026-07-14|live|HIGH|96.0|17.15|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:00|CleanSpark announced today (July 14, 2026) a 20-year triple-net lease with a high-investment-grade global technology company for its Sandersville, Georgia data center campus (175 MW of critical IT load), generating $6.6B in contracted revenue over the initial term (up to $11.6B with extension options) — nearly 2x the company's $3.2B market cap. Additionally, the tenant has signed a letter of inten|A transformative, company-specific multi-year revenue inflection (20-year contract generating $6.6B–$11.6B in contracted recurring cash flows) that fundamentally revalues the business model from mining to infrastructure services—idiosyncratic to CleanSpark, not a sector-wide theme or policy driver.|Fresh, primary-source 8-K/press wire dated today (2026-07-14) discloses a 20-year triple-net data-center lease worth ~$6.6B contracted revenue (up to $11.6B), roughly 2x the $3.2B market cap — a genuinely transformative catalyst that revalues CLSK from a Bitcoin miner into a contracted digital-infrastructure platform with investment-grade cash flows. The bolt-on LOI/exclusivity over the entire 885 MW Texas portfolio compounds the theme (AI/data-center buildout) and narrative re-rating. Direct source is verified and freshness is established, so materiality-driven promotion is warranted and the |CleanSpark announced today (July 14, 2026) a 20-year triple-net lease with a high-investment-grade global technology company for its Sandersville, Georgia data center campus (175 MW of critical IT load), generating $6.6B in contracted revenue over the initial term (up to $11.6B with extension options) — nearly 2x the company's $3.2B market cap. Additionally, the tenant has signed a letter of intent and exclusivity arrangement covering CleanSpark's entire Texas portfolio of up to 885 MW, signaling a substantially larger relationship ahead. This is a transformative, freshly disclosed contract tha