12348|HAS|2026-07-21|live|HIGH|72.0|10.61|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|09:50|Hasbro reported Q2 2026 earnings on July 21, 2026 with revenue up 16% YoY, driven by Wizards and Digital Gaming (+27%) and Consumer Products (+5%), with Magic: The Gathering crossing $500M in quarterly revenue for the first time ever. Adjusted EPS came in at $1.28 and adjusted operating profit grew 14% YoY. Critically, management raised full-year 2026 financial guidance and announced a $1B share r|Hasbro reported a multi-quarter earnings inflection with broad-based revenue acceleration (16% YoY), a record MTG milestone (+27% in Wizards/Digital), guidance raise, and operational leverage (14% operating profit growth) — classic company-specific sales_acceleration driven by organic business momen|Fresh, primary-source 8-K/press release (filed 7/21/2026) shows the load-bearing growth signal: revenue +16% YoY with Wizards/Digital Gaming +27%, a record Magic: The Gathering $500M quarter, AND an explicit full-year guidance RAISE plus a $1B buyback — exactly the revenue-acceleration-with-guidance-raise combination the market pays for on quality names. That legitimizes the gap and promotes above the MODERATE floor to HIGH/strong. It falls short of game_changer because HAS is a large, mature toy company (no active theme/narrative match, the growth is strong but incremental rather than transfo|Hasbro reported Q2 2026 earnings on July 21, 2026 with revenue up 16% YoY, driven by Wizards and Digital Gaming (+27%) and Consumer Products (+5%), with Magic: The Gathering crossing $500M in quarterly revenue for the first time ever. Adjusted EPS came in at $1.28 and adjusted operating profit grew 14% YoY. Critically, management raised full-year 2026 financial guidance and announced a $1B share repurchase program, signaling strong conviction in continued growth — a combination of record revenue milestone, broad-based acceleration, guidance raise, and capital return makes this a high-quality EP catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-07-21, items 2.02,9.01] has-20260721 7/21/2026 0000046080 false 0000046080 2026-07-21 2026-07-21 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): July 21, 2026 Hasbro, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Rhode Island 1-6682 05-0155090 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 1027 Newport Avenue Pawtucket, Rhode Island 02861 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: ( 401 ) 431-8697 Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act. Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, $0.50 par value per share HAS The NASDAQ Global Select Market Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934. Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 2.02 Results of Operations and 