12350|ARWR|2026-07-22|live|HIGH|80.0|19.57|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:55|Today's fresh catalyst is the topline readout from the Phase 3 SHASTA-3 and SHASTA-4 trials of plozasiran in severe hypertriglyceridemia, announced July 22, 2026, showing deep, durable, and consistent median triglyceride reductions of 79% and 81% from baseline — a highly compelling clinical result. This is a major de-risking event for ARWR's lead asset: plozasiran already has a commercial foothold|Positive Phase 3 trial readout (SHASTA-3 and SHASTA-4) representing a major clinical de-risking and TAM expansion from rare disease (FCS) to the far larger severe hypertriglyceridemia market, enabling a blockbuster-class commercial inflection for plozasiran—this is company-specific, multi-indication|Fresh, dated (July 22) primary catalyst: positive Phase 3 SHASTA-3/4 topline for plozasiran showing 79%/81% median triglyceride reductions — a pivotal, near-registration-quality de-risking event that expands the lead asset from a rare-disease product (FCS) into the far larger severe hypertriglyceridemia market. For a $10.5B biotech this is transformative, TAM-expanding data supporting a sustained re-rating, not a one-day pop. The EU-approval and analyst-PT items are older/secondary, but the SHASTA readout alone is a textbook game_changer, so hold at HIGH; no active theme/narrative match (biote|Today's fresh catalyst is the topline readout from the Phase 3 SHASTA-3 and SHASTA-4 trials of plozasiran in severe hypertriglyceridemia, announced July 22, 2026, showing deep, durable, and consistent median triglyceride reductions of 79% and 81% from baseline — a highly compelling clinical result. This is a major de-risking event for ARWR's lead asset: plozasiran already has a commercial foothold in familial chylomicronemia syndrome (FCS), and a successful Phase 3 readout in the far larger severe hypertriglyceridemia indication materially expands the drug's total addressable market, transforming it from a rare-disease product into a potential blockbuster cardiometabolic franchise. For a $10.5B biotech, this kind of pivotal Phase 3 success with near-registration-quality data is a textbook game-changer catalyst that can drive a sustained re-rating, not just a one-day pop.|[Benzinga 2026-07-22] Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals Announces Topline Results For Phase 3 SHASTA-3 And SHASTA-4 Clinical Studies Of Plozasiran In Patients With Severe Hypertriglyceridemia; Observes Deep, Durable, And Consistent Median Triglyceride Reductions Of 79% And 81% From Baseline. [Benzinga 2026-07-17] JP Morgan Maintains Overweight on Arrowhead Pharma, Raises Price Target to $95. [Web summary] ARWR’s recent gap up has been driven primarily by renewed bullish sentiment around its cardiometabolic and CNS pipeline and the commercial ramp of REDEMPLO, rather than a single same‑day headline. The latest discrete fundamental catalyst is the European Union marketing authorization for REDEMPLO (plozasiran) for familial chylomicronemia syndrome, which has reset revenue expectations and supported the move. More detail on the drivers: 1. EU approval / marketing authorization for REDEMPLO   The most recent clear fundamental catalyst is the European Commission authorization of REDEMPLO (plozasiran) in the EU for reducing triglycerides in adults with familial chylomicronemia syndrome. That decision expanded the drug’s geographic footprint beyond the U.S. and Australia and reinforced the view that REDEMPLO can drive a meaningful revenue ramp over the next several years, which has been explicitly cited as a key reason investors are willing to pay a premium multiple for ARWR after its run. This EU authorization is the latest concrete news item that can justify a sharp repricing and helps explain the gap up as investors update commercial assumptions for plozasiran. 2. Analyst initiation and upgrades plus valuation reset   The stock’s move has also been supported by fresh bullish coverage: Stifel initiated ARWR with a Buy and a high double‑digit price target in mid‑July, which added incremental institutional support and brought momentum traders back into the name. That initiation came on the heels of a very strong multi‑month run, and the gap move looks like a combination of shorts covering and long‑only investors leaning into the new targets and revenue models that bake in larger Redemplo and pipeline contributions. Recent fundamental commentary has framed the stock as “fairly priced” but supported by strong sales trajectory and pipeline optionality, which tends to pull in breakout‑style flows when the chart sets up. 3. Pipeline run‑up into heavy 2H26 data   ARWR is now in a dense catalyst window, and the gap up fits a classic biotech “run‑up” pattern into multiple near‑term readouts rather than a single news print. Key upcoming events being actively traded include:   • Phase 3 SHASTA‑3/4 topline data in severe hypertriglyceridemia in Q3 2026, which could materially broaden plozasiran’s market beyond FCS and would validate the broader cardiometabolic thesis.   • Initial clinical data for ARO‑DIMER‑PA (the dual PCSK9/APOC3 RNAi program) in mixed hyperlipidemia later in Q3.   • Initial ARO‑MAPT CNS platform data in late Q3/early Q4 for tau‑targeted Alzheimer’s/ta
12351|EFOR|2026-07-22|live|MODERATE|50.4|12.37|routine|MODERATE|judge|pre_catalyst_anticipation|1.20|09:50|The gap-up in EFOR lacks a fresh, concrete, company-specific catalyst today. The only identifiable dated news item is a Truist Securities upgrade to Buy with a $36 price target (July 22), but this predates today's gap and is not a new disclosure. The web summary explicitly confirms there is no new 8-K, press release, or earnings surprise this morning, characterizing the move as a technical/momentu|The gap-up occurs ahead of the July 29 Q2 earnings print with no fresh disclosed catalyst; the move reflects anticipatory positioning into an imminent but not-yet-public earnings release, consistent with pre-catalyst-anticipation behavior rather than a post-announcement reaction or technical-only mo|No fresh, dated company-specific catalyst today — the only dated item (Truist upgrade, 7/22) predates the gap and the web summary explicitly confirms no new 8-K, PR, or earnings surprise this morning. The move is a technical/momentum breakout ahead of the 7/29 Q2 print, with prior credit-facility and ownership news already stale. No direct source and no active narrative match, so the driver is UNIDENTIFIED and the setup holds at the routine floor.|The gap-up in EFOR lacks a fresh, concrete, company-specific catalyst today. The only identifiable dated news item is a Truist Securities upgrade to Buy with a $36 price target (July 22), but this predates today's gap and is not a new disclosure. The web summary explicitly confirms there is no new 8-K, press release, or earnings surprise this morning, characterizing the move as a technical/momentum breakout ahead of the July 29 Q2 earnings print. With no fresh fundamental event driving the gap, this is classified as routine.|[Benzinga 2026-07-22] Truist Securities Upgrades Everforth to Buy, Raises Price Target to $36. [Web summary] EFOR’s latest gap up appears to be a technically driven move in Everforth, Inc. rather than a single, discrete news headline catalyst today. Here’s what is driving it: 1) Price action and technicals   – Everforth (EFOR) is trading around $19.1, up roughly 4–5% from the prior close, and has broken higher from the recent $17–18 range.   – Technical screens show the stock in a buy/strong‑buy configuration: MACD positive, RSI in buy territory, and moving averages supportive of upside, indicating a momentum/technical breakout rather than a reaction to fresh fundamental news.   – Over the last several sessions, the stock has been grinding higher off recent lows, which can set up an opening gap once marginal buyers chase the move and shorts cover. 2) Recent fundamental and sentiment backdrop   There is no new earnings release or company‑specific headline today tied to the gap; the next scheduled fundamental catalyst is Q2 2026 earnings on July 29.   Recent news flow over the last few weeks has been moderately constructive but not explosive:   – Extension and upsizing of a $600m revolving credit facility and maturity to 2031, which improves financial flexibility.   – Governance/annual meeting outcomes (directors, pay plan, auditor approval) and a 13G filing showing AQR with a 6%+ stake, supporting the institutional ownership story.   – An analyst rating move to “Hold” and a consensus target still implying sizable upside from current levels.   3) How I would characterize today’s move for trading purposes   Given the absence of a new 8‑K, press release, or earnings surprise this morning, the gap up is best viewed as:   – A short‑term momentum/technical catalyst (buyers reacting to improving technical setup and prior positive corporate actions) rather than a fresh, specific news item.   – Positioning and sentiment shift ahead of the Q2 print, with some investors repricing the name after the refinancing and the visibility on liquidity, plus institutional accumulation signals.   So if you are trading it intraday, treat today’s gap as a technical/momentum move built on earlier credit‑facility and ownership news plus expectations into the 7/29 earnings call, not a new standalone headline this morning.
12352|NVCR|2026-07-23|live|HIGH|84.0|15.54|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|09:05|NovoCure reported Q2 2026 earnings today with record net revenues of $183.6M, up 16% YoY, driven by 18% global active patient growth — concrete figures with clear acceleration in the core business. The quarter also included a significant regulatory milestone: CE Mark received for Optune Pax for locally advanced pancreatic cancer, with Germany already launching in the EU and 280+ active patients. G|A company-specific multi-quarter revenue and earnings inflection (16% YoY growth, 18% patient growth, 78% gross margin expansion) driven by operational execution and market adoption—idiosyncratic to NovoCure, not a sector theme or policy driver.|Fresh, primary-sourced 8-K (filed today 2026-07-23) reports Q2 revenue of $183.6M up 16% YoY driven by 18% active patient growth — real REVENUE acceleration on a growth name, the load-bearing signal, plus a fresh CE Mark for Optune Pax in pancreatic cancer and margin expansion to 78%. That is a genuine material catalyst for a $1.8B company, warranting HIGH. Absence of an explicit guidance raise and reliance partly on one-time items (tariff refund, one-time revenue) caps it at strong rather than game_changer; no theme/narrative match (oncology, not the AI-datacenter cohort).|NovoCure reported Q2 2026 earnings today with record net revenues of $183.6M, up 16% YoY, driven by 18% global active patient growth — concrete figures with clear acceleration in the core business. The quarter also included a significant regulatory milestone: CE Mark received for Optune Pax for locally advanced pancreatic cancer, with Germany already launching in the EU and 280+ active patients. Gross margin expanded meaningfully to 78% (vs. 74% prior year), and the CEO commentary points toward a path to profitability — a solid beat with a strong operational/regulatory kicker, though no explicit full-year guidance raise was disclosed in the available text, keeping this just below game-changer territory.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-07-23, items 2.02,9.01] nvcr-20260723 0001645113 false 0001645113 2026-07-01 2026-07-31 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 July 23, 2026 Date of Report (date of earliest event reported) NovoCure Limited (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Jersey 001-37565 98-1057807 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) No. 4 The Forum, Grenville Street St. Helier Jersey JE2 4UF (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) + 44 (0) 15 3475 6700 Registrant's telephone number, including area code (Former name or former address, if changed since last report.) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions (see General Instruction A.2. below): &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Ordinary Shares, no par value NVCR The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark