12354|THC|2026-07-24|live|HIGH|60.0|14.31|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:05|Tenet Healthcare reported Q2 2026 earnings on July 23, 2026, with Adjusted EPS surging 52.2% YoY to $6.12 (vs. $4.02 prior year), Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA rising 16.3% to $1.304B and well exceeding the high end of guidance, and Hospital EBITDA margins expanding meaningfully to 18.0% from 15.6%. Critically, management raised full-year 2026 Adjusted EBITDA guidance by ~$295M at the midpoint to $|Tenet Healthcare's 52% EPS surge, 16% EBITDA beat, margin expansion to 18% from 15.6%, and $295M+ midpoint guidance raise on both EBITDA and FCF reflect a multi-quarter idiosyncratic operational inflection—not a sector-wide theme, policy/regulatory driver, or supply shortage—consistent with company-|Fresh, primary-source 8-K/press release (2026-07-23) shows a genuine earnings beat WITH a broad-based guidance RAISE (FY EBITDA +$295M and FCF +$225M at midpoint) plus a $2.0B buyback expansion — a real, dated, material catalyst that clears the HIGH bar. However this is a non-revenue-stage $17B mature hospital operator, not a growth/theme name, and the headline is driven by EPS/EBITDA and one-time favorable comps rather than a structural theme; the guidance raise (~6%) is solid but not transformative for a company this size. I hold HIGH but demote the grade from game_changer to strong — no the|Tenet Healthcare reported Q2 2026 earnings on July 23, 2026, with Adjusted EPS surging 52.2% YoY to $6.12 (vs. $4.02 prior year), Consolidated Adjusted EBITDA rising 16.3% to $1.304B and well exceeding the high end of guidance, and Hospital EBITDA margins expanding meaningfully to 18.0% from 15.6%. Critically, management raised full-year 2026 Adjusted EBITDA guidance by ~$295M at the midpoint to $4.83B–$5.03B, and raised Adjusted Free Cash Flow outlook by ~$225M at the midpoint to $2.725B–$3.025B — a substantial and broad-based raise. The board also authorized a $2.0B increase to the share repu