12361|CORT|2026-07-30|live|HIGH|96.0|24.21|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:00|Corcept reported Q2 2026 revenue of $256.1 million, a strong 32% YoY increase, driven by both its legacy Korlym/authorized generic business ($208.6M) and the rapidly ramping Lifyorli oncology launch ($47.6M, FDA-approved March 2026 with over 1,300 patients already on treatment and accelerating monthly demand). The company simultaneously raised its full-year 2026 revenue guidance to $1.1–$1.2 billi|Multi-quarter revenue inflection and beat-and-raise driven by dual organic growth engines (legacy Korlym acceleration + new Lifyorli oncology launch ramping), signaling company-specific momentum independent of sector tailwinds.|Fresh, primary-source 8-K/press release dated today shows +32% YoY revenue ($256.1M) with a formal full-year guidance RAISE to $1.1–1.2B — the load-bearing signal for a growth name, plus an accelerating new-product oncology launch (Lifyorli, 1,300+ patients). This is a genuine, dated revenue-acceleration-plus-guidance-raise catalyst, not a numberless PR, so it clears the HIGH bar despite has_direct_source=false. The tariff-truce cohort is unrelated (no shared story), so no theme/narrative axis lights; it holds at strong rather than game_changer given the $10B cap and only moderate net-income g|Corcept reported Q2 2026 revenue of $256.1 million, a strong 32% YoY increase, driven by both its legacy Korlym/authorized generic business ($208.6M) and the rapidly ramping Lifyorli oncology launch ($47.6M, FDA-approved March 2026 with over 1,300 patients already on treatment and accelerating monthly demand). The company simultaneously raised its full-year 2026 revenue guidance to $1.1–$1.2 billion, a meaningful uplift that signals management confidence in continued momentum across both its Cushing's syndrome and oncology franchises. The combination of a clear revenue beat (+32% YoY), a dual-engine growth story with a new product launch accelerating, and a formal guidance raise constitutes a strong — potentially game_changer-adjacent — catalyst, though the $10B market cap and still-moderate net income expansion ($43M vs. $35.1M) keep it firmly in the "strong" tier rather than transformative.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-07-29, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] cort-20260729 0001088856 false 0001088856 2026-07-29 2026-07-29 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 July 29, 2026 Date of Report (date of earliest event reported) Corcept Therapeutics Incorporated (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 000-50679 77-0487658 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 101 Redwood Shores Parkway , Redwood City , CA 94065 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) ( 650 ) 327-3270 Registrant's telephone number, including area code Not Applicable (Former name or former address, if changed since last report.) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions (see General Instruction A.2. below): &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, $0.001 par value CORT The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 193