12366|SIMO|2026-07-30|live|HIGH|80.0|19.18|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|09:10|SIMO reported a massive Q2 2026 earnings beat with revenue of $451.0M (+127% Y/Y, +32% Q/Q) crushing the $403.4M estimate, and non-GAAP EPS of $2.43 beating the $2.14 estimate. The company also issued strong Q3 2026 guidance of $519M–$541M in sales, well above prior expectations, implying continued sequential acceleration. Revenue growth is broad-based and structural — driven by explosive Ferri/Bo|SIMO exhibited a multi-quarter company-specific revenue inflection and beat-and-raise (127% Y/Y growth, crushing estimates by 12%, with forward guidance 29%+ above prior expectations) driven by idiosyncratic product adoption (Ferri/Boot solutions, eMMC+UFS, enterprise SSDs) in AI infrastructure and |Fresh SEC 6-K (filed 7/30/2026) delivers the load-bearing signal for a growth name: revenue +32% Q/Q, +127% Y/Y crushing estimates, PLUS a Q3 guidance RAISE to $519-541M implying continued acceleration, with margin expansion (op margin 22.4% vs 11.2% Y/Y) — this is structural, broad-based growth (Ferri +1,690%, eMMC/UFS +95-100%), not a one-time item. The AI-infrastructure/edge-storage narrative aligns with a hot theme, reinforced by the Wedbush target hike to $400. Primary-source revenue+guidance confirmation makes this a legitimate game_changer despite has_direct_source=false on the web laye|SIMO reported a massive Q2 2026 earnings beat with revenue of $451.0M (+127% Y/Y, +32% Q/Q) crushing the $403.4M estimate, and non-GAAP EPS of $2.43 beating the $2.14 estimate. The company also issued strong Q3 2026 guidance of $519M–$541M in sales, well above prior expectations, implying continued sequential acceleration. Revenue growth is broad-based and structural — driven by explosive Ferri/Boot Drive solutions (+1,690% Y/Y), eMMC+UFS (+95-100% Y/Y), and enterprise SSD controllers (+50-55% Y/Y) — reflecting a genuine business transformation into AI infrastructure and edge storage, not a one-time item.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-07-30, items ] EX-99.1 2 d114913dex991.htm EX-99.1 EX-99.1 Exhibit 99.1 Silicon Motion Announces Results for the Quarterly Period Ended June 30, 2026 &#8195; NEWS RELEASE Business Highlights &#149; Second quarter of 2026 sales increased 32% Q/Q and increased 127% Y/Y &#149; SSD controller sales: 2Q of 2026 increased 5% to 10% Q/Q and increased 50% to 55% Y/Y &#149; eMMC+UFS controller sales: 2Q of 2026 increased 15% to 20% Q/Q and increased 95% to 100% Y/Y &#149; Ferri & Boot Drive solutions sales: 2Q of 2026 increased 110% to 115% Q/Q and increased 1,690% to 1,695% Y/Y Financial Highlights 2Q 2026 GAAP 2Q 2026 Non-GAAP* &#149; Net sales $451.0 million (+32% Q/Q, +127% Y/Y) $451.0 million (+32% Q/Q, +127% Y/Y) &#149; Gross margin 50.2% 50.2% &#149; Operating margin 22.4% 23.1% &#149; Earnings per diluted ADS $3.99 $2.43 * Please see reconciliations of U.S. Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (&#8220;GAAP&#8221;) to all non-GAAP financial measures mentioned herein towards the end of this news release. TAIPEI, Taiwan and MILPITAS, Calif., July 30, 2026 &#8211; Silicon Motion Technology Corporation (NasdaqGS: SIMO) (&#8220;Silicon Motion,&#8221; the &#8220;Company,&#8221; &#8220;we&#8221; or similar terms) today announced its financial results for the quarter ended June 30, 2026. For the second quarter of 2026, net sales (GAAP) increased sequentially to $451.0 million from $342.1 million in the first quarter of 2026. Net income (GAAP) also increased sequentially to $136.1 million, or $3.99 per diluted American depositary share (&#8220;ADS&#8221;) (GAAP), from net income (GAAP) of $66.8 million, or $1.97 per diluted ADS (GAAP), in the first quarter of 2026 For the second quarter of 2026, net income (non-GAAP) increased sequentially to $83.1 million, or $2.43 per diluted ADS (non-GAAP), from net income (non-GAAP) of $53.8 million, or $1.58 per diluted ADS (non-GAAP), in the first quarter of 2026. All financial numbers are in U.S. dollars unless otherwise noted. 1 Second Quarter of 2026 Review &#8220;Our shift from a consumer-focused NAND flash controller maker to a diversified leader in controllers and storage solutions &#8212; from AI infrastructure to the edge &#8212; is accelerating rapidly,&#8221; stated Wallace Kou, President & CEO of Silicon Motion. &#8220;The second quarter delivered exceptional growth in revenue, gross margin, and operating margin &#8212; powered by our Embedded eMMC & UFS business, our Enterprise and Edge SSD controller business, and our rapidly growing storage solutions business focusing on Ferri for Automotive & Enterprise Boot Drives. The first two quarters delivered a record-breaking start to the year, and we expect that momentum to continue into the second half. With our ongoing product and market expansion, we are building a resilient platform for sustainable, high-quality revenue and profitability growth for years to come.&#8221; Key Financial Results (in millions, except percentages and per AD
12367|LRCX|2026-07-30|live|HIGH|84.0|18.95|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|09:50|Lam Research reported Q4 FY2026 earnings on July 29, 2026, with revenue of $6.72B (+15.1% QoQ) and non-GAAP EPS of $1.82, both representing strong sequential acceleration alongside meaningful margin expansion (non-GAAP operating margin up 340 bps QoQ to 38.4%). The revenue growth acceleration and significant margin improvement are the core catalyst, reflecting robust semiconductor equipment demand|Lam Research delivered a multi-quarter earnings inflection with sequential revenue acceleration (+15.1% QoQ) and substantial margin expansion (340 bps), reflecting company-specific strength in semiconductor equipment demand—idiosyncratic performance independent of sector-wide policy or supply driver|Fresh, primary-sourced 8-K/EX-99 dated 2026-07-29 shows load-bearing revenue acceleration (+15.1% Q/Q) plus 340 bps non-GAAP operating margin expansion — exactly the signal the market pays for on a semi-equipment name, materially confirmed by SEC filing. The catalyst is real, fresh, and material for a $380B mega-cap despite no listed direct-source flag (the corpus itself is the primary source). Absence of an explicit guidance raise in the excerpt caps it at strong rather than game_changer; no active theme/narrative alignment.|Lam Research reported Q4 FY2026 earnings on July 29, 2026, with revenue of $6.72B (+15.1% QoQ) and non-GAAP EPS of $1.82, both representing strong sequential acceleration alongside meaningful margin expansion (non-GAAP operating margin up 340 bps QoQ to 38.4%). The revenue growth acceleration and significant margin improvement are the core catalyst, reflecting robust semiconductor equipment demand. However, the filing excerpt does not include explicit forward guidance figures (a full guidance raise would elevate this to game_changer), keeping this classified as strong rather than game_changer based on available data.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-07-29, items 2.02,9.01] lrcx-2