12368|COHU|2026-07-31|live|HIGH|80.0|22.71|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:00|Cohu reported Q2 FY2026 earnings with net sales of $149.0M, up 38% year-over-year and beating expectations, with non-GAAP EPS of $0.26 (vs. $0.02 in Q2 FY2025) — a dramatic profitability inflection. The company also raised its AI-driven compute opportunity pipeline to approximately $850M, signaling a meaningful guidance/outlook upgrade. Test cell utilization rose sequentially to 80%, confirming br|Cohu's gap-up reflects a multi-quarter idiosyncratic revenue and earnings inflection (38% YoY sales growth, EPS swing from $0.02 to $0.26) and raised AI-driven guidance ($850M pipeline), not a sector-wide theme or policy driver — this is company-specific momentum meeting raised expectations.|Fresh, primary-sourced 8-K/PR (filed 2026-07-30) shows Q2 net sales +38% Y/Y to $149M AND sequential acceleration ($125M→$149M), a genuine loss→near-breakeven inflection, and a raised AI-compute pipeline to ~$850M — a real, material catalyst that joins the live "AI & Data Center Semiconductor Surge" story. Revenue is load-bearing and accelerating here (not an EPS-only beat), so this clears the growth-name bar and merits HIGH. I demote from game_changer to strong: GAAP is still a small loss, the "turnaround" leans on non-GAAP, and the AI pipeline is an opportunity figure rather than a hard guid|Cohu reported Q2 FY2026 earnings with net sales of $149.0M, up 38% year-over-year and beating expectations, with non-GAAP EPS of $0.26 (vs. $0.02 in Q2 FY2025) — a dramatic profitability inflection. The company also raised its AI-driven compute opportunity pipeline to approximately $850M, signaling a meaningful guidance/outlook upgrade. Test cell utilization rose sequentially to 80%, confirming broad-based end-market recovery; the combination of massive revenue acceleration, a near-total loss-to-profit turnaround, and a raised AI pipeline outlook qualifies this as a game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-07-30, items 2.02,9.01] cohu20260728_8k.htm false 0000021535 0000021535 2026-07-30 2026-07-30 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of Earliest Event Reported): July 30, 2026 Cohu, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-04298 95-1934119 _____________________ (State or other jurisdiction _____________ (Commission ______________ (I.R.S. Employer of incorporation) File Number) Identification No.) 12367 Crosthwaite Circle , Poway , California 92064 _________________________________ (Address of principal executive offices) ___________ (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code: 858 - 848-8100 Not Applicable ______________________________________________ Former name or former address, if changed since last report Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of Each Class Trading Symbol(s) Name of exchange on which registered Common Stock , $1.00 par value COHU The NASDAQ Stock Market LLC Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934. Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 2.02 Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On July 30, 2026, the Company issued a press release regarding its financial results for the second fiscal quarter ended June 27, 2026. The Company&#8217;s press release is attached as Exhibit 99.1 to this Current Report on Form 8-K and incorporated by reference herein. The information in this Item 2.02 of this Current Report on Form 8-K and the Exhibit attached hereto shall not be deemed &#8220;filed&#8221; for purposes of Section 18 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (the &#8220;Exchange Act&#8221;) or otherwise subject to the liabilities of that section, nor shall it be deemed incorporated by reference in any filing under the Securities Act of 1933 or the Exchange Act, regardless of any general incorporation language in such
12369|NWL|2026-07-31|live|HIGH|60.0|13.42|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:00|Newell Brands reported Q2 2026 Adj. EPS of $0.42, massively beating the $0.20 estimate (a 110% beat), with revenue of $1.994B also topping the $1.978B estimate. More importantly, the company dramatically raised its FY2026 Adj. EPS guidance to $0.73–$0.77 vs. the prior $0.56–$0.60 range and the $0.58 consensus — a ~30%+ raise that signals a structural acceleration in the turnaround. This is a class|Newell Brands delivered a 110% EPS beat paired with a ~30% full-year guidance raise, signaling a multi-quarter structural earnings inflection tied to company-specific operational turnaround—idiosyncratic to NWL, not a sector theme or regulatory driver.|Fresh, primary-wire-dated (2026-07-31) Q2 earnings with a huge EPS beat ($0.42 vs $0.20) AND a ~30% FY EPS guidance raise, importantly accompanied by a revenue beat and raised sales guidance — so the load-bearing signal isn't EPS-only. But NWL is a low-growth consumer-defensive name where the raise is driven mainly by margin/productivity rather than a demand/revenue inflection (sales guide barely moved), so this is a strong margin-turnaround print, not a transformative demand game_changer. No hot theme or narrative cohort membership to lift it; I hold HIGH but demote from game_changer to stron|Newell Brands reported Q2 2026 Adj. EPS of $0.42, massively beating the $0.20 estimate (a 110% beat), with revenue of $1.994B also topping the $1.978B estimate. More importantly, the company dramatically raised its FY2026 Adj. EPS guidance to $0.73–$0.77 vs. the prior $0.56–$0.60 range and the $0.58 consensus — a ~30%+ raise that signals a structural acceleration in the turnaround. This is a classic game-changer setup: a massive EPS beat on a consumer defensive turnaround story paired with a transformative full-year guidance raise that resets the earnings base well above Street expectations.|[Benzinga 2026-07-31] Newell Brands Sees Q3 Adj EPS $0.18-$0.20 vs $0.20 Est; Sees Sales $1.842B-$1.860B vs $1.841B Est. [Benzinga 2026-07-31] Newell Brands Raises FY2026 Adj EPS Guidance from $0.56-$0.60 to $0.73-$0.77 vs $0.58 Est; Raises FY2026 Sales Guidance from $7.204B-$7.348B to $7.276B-$7.348B vs $7.287B Est. [Benzinga 2026-07-31] Newell Brands Q2 Adj. EPS $0.42 Beats $0.20 Estimate, Sales $1.994B Beat $1.978B Estimate. [Web summary] The most recent gap up in NWL is being driven by a combination of improving fundamentals, expectations around upcoming earnings, and index reclassification flows rather than a single, discrete news headline like M&A or a surprise guidance hike. Key catalysts behind the move: 1) Earnings momentum and margin improvement   Recent coverage highlights that Newell has been steadily expanding gross and operating margins through productivity, automation, cost control, and disciplined pricing. In Q1 2026, normalized gross margin rose to about one‑third of sales and operating margin also ticked higher, with productivity and net pricing more than offsetting tariffs, inflation, and lower volumes. That has led to a material wave of upward earnings estimate revisions and a strong year‑to‑date price move, which sets up a positive expectation bias into the next print. This improving profitability profile is a core fundamental driver behind the stock’s recent strength. 2) Positioning into the upcoming Q2 earnings   The market is now trading the story ahead of the Q2 release. Sell‑side commentary going into the quarter emphasizes front‑end commercial improvements (innovation, new business development, streamlined organization) plus restructuring and supply‑chain efficiencies as tailwinds for the top line and margins, even against a still‑soft consumer backdrop. That earnings setup – with the company expected to show further stabilization and incremental progress rather than deterioration – is attracting buyers into the event and can easily produce a gap if positioning was light and short interest elevated. 3) Russell index reclassification flows   At the end of June 2026, Newell was removed from the Russell 1000 and Midcap indices and added to the Russell 2000. That kind of index reshuffle forces mechanical selling and buying by passive funds and quant strategies, and can create dislocations around the effective date. Once those flows clear, value and turnaround investors often step in, betting that forced selling pushed the stock below fundamentals. The post‑reconstitution repositioning into a perceived turnaround is another technical driver supporting a sharp move higher. 4) Turnaround narrative and sentiment shift   Recent analysis frames 2026 as a stabilization year rather than a deepening downcycle: productivity, simplification, and pricing actions are now more visible, while tariff and category headwinds are at least better understood. Year‑to‑date performance in the stock is already strong versus its consumer staples pe
12370|FLNC|2026-07-31|live|HIGH|60.0|10.02|game_changer|HIGH|judge|new_product|1.00|07:00|The recent gap up in FLNC was driven primarily by its inclusion as a key battery storage partner in Nvidia/Siemens’ new AI data center power architecture, reinforced by a subsequent Citi upgrade that highlighted energy storage demand and upside into earnings. Specifically, Siemens and Nvidia released a reference design for large-scale AI “factories” that explicitly incorporates Fluence’s SmartStac|Fluence's SmartStack battery system is being positioned as a critical TAM-expanding component within Nvidia/Siemens' new AI data center power architecture reference design, materially broadening FLNC's addressable market from renewable-only storage into core AI infrastructure—a landmark product/plat|The core driver — Nvidia/Siemens naming Fluence's SmartStack as the sole battery-storage partner in their AI data-center reference architecture — is a company-specific, transformative endorsement that reframes a $2.5B storage name into a direct AI-power-infrastructure play, and it directly JOINS the active "AI-Driven Power & Grid Infrastructure Boom" narrative (EME/PWR). This lights all three axes and is corroborated by a Citi upgrade and record multi-billion backlog. Only caution: has_direct_source=false and freshness rests on a web summary, so despite promotion to HIGH the confidence is temp|The core catalyst is today's Nvidia/Siemens reference architecture for large-scale AI data center "factories" explicitly naming Fluence's SmartStack battery energy storage system as the designated power solution — reframing FLNC from a renewables/storage name into a direct AI infrastructure play and triggering a ~45% intraday spike. This is highly company-specific and transformative in nature: being the sole named battery storage partner across multiple Nvidia ecosystem designs is a landmark strategic endorsement that materially expands Fluence's addressable market and credibility at scale. The Citi upgrade to Buy with a higher price target, citing AI data center exposure and record multi-billion-dollar backlog growth, provided meaningful follow-through support and reinforced the structural re-rating thesis.|[Web summary] The recent gap up in FLNC was driven primarily by its inclusion as a key battery storage partner in Nvidia/Siemens’ new AI data center power architecture, reinforced by a subsequent Citi upgrade that highlighted energy storage demand and upside into earnings. Specifically, Siemens and Nvidia released a reference design for large-scale AI “factories” that explicitly incorporates Fluence’s SmartStack battery energy storage system as a critical part of the electrical architecture for power‑intensive AI data centers. This positioned Fluence as a direct beneficiary of the AI infrastructure build‑out, and reports noted it was the only named battery storage partner across multiple Nvidia ecosystem designs. That news triggered a violent move: the stock jumped roughly 45% intraday on the announcement as the market repriced FLNC from a renewables/storage name to an AI‑infrastructure power play. Shortly after, Citi upgraded FLNC from Neutral to Buy with a bullish price target and framed it as one of several energy‑storage‑focused names poised to benefit from accelerating grid‑scale and data‑center storage demand. The upgrade came on top of a record reported backlog around the mid‑single‑digit billions and growing U.S. contracting tied to clean‑energy policy, reinforcing the narrative that rising AI‑related demand and policy‑driven storage deployments could drive earnings and margin upside. So in terms of catalysts: 1) Core gap-up driver: Nvidia/Siemens AI data center architecture naming Fluence’s SmartStack as the battery energy storage solution, reframing FLNC as a strategic AI power‑infrastructure supplier and prompting a 40–50% spike. 2) Follow‑through support: Citi’s upgrade to Buy with a higher target, emphasizing energy storage demand, AI data center exposure, and backlog growth as reasons for near‑term upside.
12371|FET|2026-07-31|live|HIGH|84.0|16.04|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|09:10|FET reported Q2 2026 results with revenue of $226M (up 8% sequentially), adjusted EBITDA of $32M (up 39% sequentially), and adjusted EPS of $1.16 (up 147%), alongside a book-to-bill of 104% signaling strong demand. Critically, management raised full-year 2026 guidance across all metrics — revenue to $870-$910M (+13% YoY), adjusted EBITDA to $115-$125M (+40% YoY), and adjusted net income to $42-$52|FET posted a multi-quarter revenue and earnings inflection with a substantial broad-based guidance raise (revenue +13% YoY, EBITDA +40% YoY, net income +571% YoY) driven by 13% market share gains and operating leverage—idiosyncratic company-specific acceleration unrelated to sector-wide theme, polic|Fresh, primary-source 8-K (filed 2026-07-30) confirms Q2 results with an across-the-board full-year guidance RAISE — revenue $870-910M (+13% YoY), adjusted EBITDA +40%, plus margin expansion (230-300bps) and 13% market-share gain, so the growth is revenue/demand-driven and structurally supported, not a one-time EPS anomaly. Book-to-bill of 104% and raised guidance are the load-bearing HIGH signals; the dramatic EPS jump is corroborated by operational leverage rather than a settlement/tax item. Not lifted to game_changer: no theme/narrative match (oilfield services isn't the active AI-power/gri|FET reported Q2 2026 results with revenue of $226M (up 8% sequentially), adjusted EBITDA of $32M (up 39% sequentially), and adjusted EPS of $1.16 (up 147%), alongside a book-to-bill of 104% signaling strong demand. Critically, management raised full-year 2026 guidance across all metrics — revenue to $870-$910M (+13% YoY), adjusted EBITDA to $115-$125M (+40% YoY), and adjusted net income to $42-$52M (+571% YoY) — a broad and substantial guidance raise. While the sequential EPS improvement is dramatic, it reflects genuine operational leverage (margin expansion of 230-300bps, 13% market share growth) rather than one-time items, and the guidance raise is material relative to the company's scale, supporting a strong classification rather than game_changer given the oilfield services sector context and lack of a truly transformative structural event.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-07-30, items 2.02,9.01] fet-20260730 0001401257 false Common Stock, par value $0.01 per share FET CHX 0001401257 2026-07-30 2026-07-30 0001401257 fet:Exch_XNYSMember 2026-07-30 2026-07-30 0001401257 fet:Exch_XCHIMember 2026-07-30 2026-07-30 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 ___________________________________ FORM 8-K ___________________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): July 30, 2026 FORUM ENERGY TECHNOLOGIES, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-35504 61-1488595 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 10344 Sam Houston Park Drive Suite 300 Houston TX 77064 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) 281 949-2500 Registrant's telephone number, including area code Not Applicable (Former name or former address, if changed since last report) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol Name of each exch