12378|LIFE|2026-08-04|live|HIGH|80.0|16.29|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:20|Ethos Technologies reported Q2 2026 earnings with revenue of $189.6M, representing 113% year-over-year growth — the second consecutive quarter of 100%+ YoY growth — driven by 131% growth in Direct Channel Revenue and 90% growth in Third-Party Channel Revenue. The company also delivered GAAP net income of $19.5M (10% margin) and Adjusted EBITDA of $35.2M (19% margin), demonstrating both explosive t|Second consecutive quarter of 100%+ YoY revenue growth with expanding margins demonstrates a company-specific multi-quarter earnings inflection and beat-and-raise pattern, idiosyncratic to Ethos Technologies and independent of any sector theme, policy, or supply constraint.|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: 8-K + EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-03 shows Q2 revenue +113% Y/Y to $189.6M — a second consecutive 100%+ growth quarter with GAAP profitability ($19.5M net income, 19% adj. EBITDA margin), exactly the revenue-acceleration signal the market pays for on a growth name. The simultaneous $100M buyback (~4.5% of a $2.2B cap) is a meaningful shareholder-return add-on, not the load-bearing driver. No active theme/narrative fit (insurtech vs. AI cohorts), but catalyst quality alone sustains the HIGH/game_changer floor.|Ethos Technologies reported Q2 2026 earnings with revenue of $189.6M, representing 113% year-over-year growth — the second consecutive quarter of 100%+ YoY growth — driven by 131% growth in Direct Channel Revenue and 90% growth in Third-Party Channel Revenue. The company also delivered GAAP net income of $19.5M (10% margin) and Adjusted EBITDA of $35.2M (19% margin), demonstrating both explosive top-line acceleration and improving profitability. The Board simultaneously authorized a $100M share repurchase program (~4.5% of market cap), adding a shareholder-return signal on top of a blowout growth print.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-03, items 2.02,8.01,9.01] 8-K 0001788451 false 00017