12379|AEIS|2026-08-04|live|HIGH|84.0|15.39|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:55|AEIS reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 3, 2026, with revenue of $574M (+30% YoY), beating the high end of guidance, alongside record semiconductor revenue (+33% YoY) and non-GAAP EPS of $2.74, also above the high end of guidance. The results were described as "record" across multiple metrics including cash flow from operations ($86M). However, while the beat is robust and broad-based, the filing|AEIS demonstrated a multi-quarter revenue and earnings inflection with 30% YoY revenue growth and 33% YoY semiconductor revenue growth, both beating the high end of guidance with record cash flow — a broad-based, idiosyncratic acceleration absent sector-wide tailwinds or policy drivers.|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: 8-K/EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-03 shows Q2 revenue of $574M, +30% Y/Y and +12% Q/Q with record semiconductor revenue +33% Y/Y and a beat above the high end of guidance — revenue acceleration is exactly the load-bearing signal for this class, not the EPS line. The AI/data-center power and semiconductor-demand story directly joins active Lane 2 narratives (AI-driven power/grid infrastructure, semiconductor AI demand), lighting theme/narrative even though AEIS is not a listed cohort member. Held at strong rather than promoted to game_changer because no explicit forward |AEIS reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 3, 2026, with revenue of $574M (+30% YoY), beating the high end of guidance, alongside record semiconductor revenue (+33% YoY) and non-GAAP EPS of $2.74, also above the high end of guidance. The results were described as "record" across multiple metrics including cash flow from operations ($86M). However, while the beat is robust and broad-based, the filing excerpt does not include explicit forward guidance figures (a specific Q3 revenue/EPS guidance range), which is required to confirm a guidance raise — preventing a full game_changer classification despite the strong to