12380|CAT|2026-08-04|live|HIGH|60.0|10.00|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|08:00|Caterpillar reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 4, 2026 with sales and revenues of $20.5 billion (+24% YoY vs. $16.6B prior year), marking the first time in company history it has exceeded $20B in a single quarter. Adjusted EPS of $8.17 vs. $4.72 in Q2 2025 represents a ~73% YoY beat, with operating margin expanding dramatically from 17.3% to 20.9% (GAAP) driven by higher volume and favorable pric|Caterpillar's 24% YoY revenue beat, 73% EPS beat, margin expansion from 17.3% to 20.9%, all-segment broadening, and strong order backlog represent an idiosyncratic multi-quarter revenue and earnings inflection—not a sector-wide theme, policy driver, or supply shortage, but company-specific operation|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: 8-K + EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-04 shows record Q2 revenue of $20.5B (+24% YoY, first ever $20B quarter) with operating margin expanding 17.3%→20.9% and adjusted EPS $8.17 vs $4.72 — revenue-led, not an EPS-only or one-time print. A ~24% top-line acceleration with growing backlog across all three segments is extraordinary for a mega-cap industrial bellwether, and a 10% gap on 10x pre-market RVOL confirms genuine repricing. The demand inflection reads as the machinery/power-systems arm of the active AI data center power & grid infrastructure narrative (EME/PWR cohort|Caterpillar reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 4, 2026 with sales and revenues of $20.5 billion (+24% YoY vs. $16.6B prior year), marking the first time in company history it has exceeded $20B in a single quarter. Adjusted EPS of $8.17 vs. $4.72 in Q2 2025 represents a ~73% YoY beat, with operating margin expanding dramatically from 17.3% to 20.9% (GAAP) driven by higher volume and favorable price realization. The CEO highlighted strong order rates and a growing backlog reflecting broadening momentum across all three primary segments, signaling durable demand acceleration — this is a massive r