12382|BTDR|2026-08-04|live|HIGH|80.0|24.10|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|08:20|The fresh catalyst is the August 4, 2026 Benzinga report disclosing that Bitdeer AI executed a 16-year, ~$4.7B lease deal through its Tydal Data Center AS subsidiary with Volta Tydal AS to provide 121 IT megawatts. At a ~$2.8B market cap, a $4.7B long-term contract is transformative — it substantially exceeds the company's current market cap and provides multi-year revenue visibility in the high-g|A concrete, company-specific $4.7B multi-year data-center capacity lease deal with named counterparty (Volta Tydal AS), specific MW commitment (121 IT MW), and explicit 16-year term—delivering transformative revenue visibility and a multi-quarter/multi-year earnings inflection idiosyncratic to Bitde|Fresh, dated (2026-08-04) wire report of a 16-year, ~$4.7B lease through Bitdeer's Tydal subsidiary with Volta Tydal AS for 121 IT MW — a contract value ~1.7x the $2.8B market cap, i.e. transformative multi-year revenue visibility, not sector drift. It is concrete and company-specific (named counterparty, dollar value, MW capacity), so the catalyst axis is real even though a primary SEC/press-release source isn't in the corpus. It also plainly joins the live "AI data center infrastructure buildout / AI-driven power & grid" narrative cohorts as a new name with the same story (AI/HPC capacity le|The fresh catalyst is the August 4, 2026 Benzinga report disclosing that Bitdeer AI executed a 16-year, ~$4.7B lease deal through its Tydal Data Center AS subsidiary with Volta Tydal AS to provide 121 IT megawatts. At a ~$2.8B market cap, a $4.7B long-term contract is transformative — it substantially exceeds the company's current market cap and provides multi-year revenue visibility in the high-growth AI/HPC infrastructure segment. This is a concrete, freshly dated, company-specific deal with named counterparties, specific dollar value, and specific capacity figures, qualifying it as a game-changing catalyst rather than routine sector momentum.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-08-03, items ] EX-16.1 2 ea029966401ex16-1.htm LETTER FROM MALONEBAILEY TO THE SEC Exhibit 16.1 August 3, 2026 U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission 100 F Street, N.E. Washington, DC 20549 We have read the statements included in the Current Report on Form 6-K of Bitdeer Technologies Group to be filed with the Securities and Exchange Commission on or about August 3, 2026. We agree with all statements pertaining to us. We have no basis on which to agree or disagree with the other statements contained therein. /s/ MaloneBailey, LLP www.malonebailey.com Houston, Texas August 3, 2026 [Benzinga 2026-08-04] Bitdeer AI Executes 16-Year, ~$4.7B Lease Deal Through Its Tydal Data Center AS Subsidiary With Volta Tydal AS To Provide 121 IT Megawatts. [Benzinga 2026-07-28] Keefe, Bruyette & Woods Maintains Market Perform on Bitdeer Techs, Lowers Price Target to $14. [Web summary] The most recent gap-up in BTDR was driven by Bitdeer’s June 2026 production and operations update, which showed a major surge in Bitcoin mining output, hash rate, and visible progress on its global data center and ASIC/AI build‑out. Specifically, Bitdeer reported mining 990 BTC in June, its best month ever and almost five times the 203 BTC mined in June last year, with self-mining hash rate up to 73 EH/s versus 16.5 EH/s a year ago and 70.2 EH/s in May. That update, which highlighted Bitdeer pulling further ahead of rival Cipher in scale, triggered an immediate double‑digit intraday move as the stock jumped more than 10% on the news. The same June operating release has been framed by analysts as a key test of the “undervalued” thesis, given the combination of fast-growing production, expanding data center projects in Malaysia and Norway, and scaling of proprietary SEALMINER hardware and AI/HPC capacity. Around this move, sentiment has been reinforced by: • Market commentary noting BTDR’s aggressive expansion plans (Tydal, Norway site, additional land acquisitions) and the AI/HPC segment plus external SEALMINER sales as major upside drivers. • News items flagging institutional accumulation and a strong 6‑month momentum profile tied to revenue acceleration. • Prior updates (May 2026 operations, AI cloud capacity expansion, 370% production surge) that set the backdrop for the June beat and helped build expectations for continued hash‑rate and production growth. In short, the latest gap-up was catalyzed by a very strong June operations report showing record Bitcoin production, sharply higher hash rate, and visible execution on its mining, ASIC, and AI/data center strategy, which collectively re-priced BTDR as a leading high-growth miner/AI infrastructure play rather than a marginal Bitcoin proxy.
12383|ZBRA|2026-08-04|live|HIGH|60.0|10.75|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|08:35|Zebra Technologies reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 4, 2026, delivering record performance with net sales of $1,557M (+20.4% YoY), adjusted EBITDA of $431M (+61.4% YoY), and non-GAAP diluted EPS of $6.35 — with gross margin expanding 540 bps to 53.0%. Critically, the company also raised its full-year outlook, which is the key EP trigger on a $13.9B market cap growth name. Organic net sales grow|Zebra delivered a multi-quarter earnings inflection (20.4% YoY net sales growth, 61.4% EBITDA growth, 540 bps margin expansion) coupled with a raised full-year outlook, signaling genuine demand acceleration and idiosyncratic operational leverage—this is company-specific sales acceleration, not a sec|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: 8-K/EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-04 shows record Q2 net sales +20.4% Y/Y with 540bps gross margin expansion and an explicit full-year guidance raise — a textbook revenue-plus-raise EP trigger, so HIGH is justified. But this is a $13.9B mature enterprise-hardware name where reported growth is flattered by $73M of IEEPA tariff recoveries and organic growth is a more modest 9.2%, so it is material rather than transformative. No active AI/data-center narrative or theme membership to lift it, hence strong rather than game_changer.|Zebra Technologies reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 4, 2026, delivering record performance with net sales of $1,557M (+20.4% YoY), adjusted EBITDA of $431M (+61.4% YoY), and non-GAAP diluted EPS of $6.35 — with gross margin expanding 540 bps to 53.0%. Critically, the company also raised its full-year outlook, which is the key EP trigger on a $13.9B market cap growth name. Organic net sales growth of 9.2% demonstrates genuine underlying demand acceleration beyond tariff recoveries, and the combination of massive revenue beat, margin expansion, and guidance raise qualifies this as a game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-04, ite