12384|AMRC|2026-08-04|live|HIGH|50.0|38.72|routine|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|09:45|Ameresco reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 3 with revenues of $515.5M, Non-GAAP EPS of $0.20, and Adjusted EBITDA of $62.8M, accompanied by a raise to 2026 EPS guidance. The standout catalyst is a record $1.8B in new project awards in the quarter — including $1.2B driven by data center power infrastructure demand — pushing total backlog up 32% Y/Y to a record $6.73B and awarded backlog up 65% to|Ameresco's catalyst is a company-specific multi-quarter revenue inflection: record $1.8B in new project awards (65% Y/Y awarded backlog growth), 32% Y/Y total backlog expansion to $6.73B, and upward EPS guidance revision—idiosyncratic operational acceleration, not a sector-wide theme or policy drive||Ameresco reported Q2 2026 earnings on August 3 with revenues of $515.5M, Non-GAAP EPS of $0.20, and Adjusted EBITDA of $62.8M, accompanied by a raise to 2026 EPS guidance. The standout catalyst is a record $1.8B in new project awards in the quarter — including $1.2B driven by data center power infrastructure demand — pushing total backlog up 32% Y/Y to a record $6.73B and awarded backlog up 65% to $4.4B. The massive backlog expansion and guidance raise signal strong revenue visibility and accelerating business momentum, warranting a "strong" classification, though the headline EPS/revenue figures alone are modest relative to the $1.2B market cap.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-03, items 2.02,9.01] amrc-20260803 FALSE 0001488139 0001488139 2026-08-03 2026-08-03 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 3, 2026 Ameresco, Inc. (Exact Name of Registrant as Specified in Charter) Delaware 001-34811 04-3512838 (State or Other Juris- diction of Incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 111 Sp