12388|KODK|2026-08-05|live|HIGH|54.7|10.86|strong||fallback|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:00|Kodak reported Q2 2026 earnings with concrete, verifiable numbers: revenue of $311M (+18% YoY), gross profit of $82M (+61% YoY), gross margin expanding from 19% to 26%, and Operational EBITDA of $36M vs. $9M in Q2 2025 — a 4x improvement. Critically, this marks the fourth consecutive quarter of YoY growth in revenue, gross profit, and Operational EBITDA, and the company swung from a GAAP net loss |Multi-quarter revenue, gross profit, and EBITDA inflection with four consecutive quarters of YoY growth, expanding margins, and a GAAP loss-to-profit swing—a company-specific turnaround with no theme, policy, or shortage driver evident.||Kodak reported Q2 2026 earnings with concrete, verifiable numbers: revenue of $311M (+18% YoY), gross profit of $82M (+61% YoY), gross margin expanding from 19% to 26%, and Operational EBITDA of $36M vs. $9M in Q2 2025 — a 4x improvement. Critically, this marks the fourth consecutive quarter of YoY growth in revenue, gross profit, and Operational EBITDA, and the company swung from a GAAP net loss of $26M to net income of $17M, representing a meaningful turnaround inflection. AM&C segment revenue surged 40% YoY, adding structural credibility to the growth story. No formal guidance raise was disclosed in the filing, which keeps this from game_changer territory, but the magnitude of the beat across all key metrics — with accelerating margins and consecutive quarterly improvement — is a clearly strong, fresh, and verifiable catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-04, items 2.02,9.01] 8-K 0000031235 false NJ 0000031235 2026-08-04 2026-08-04 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 ________________ Form 8-K ________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 4, 2026 EASTMAN KODAK COMPANY (Exact name of registrant as specified i