12389|TATT|2026-08-05|live|HIGH|61.9|11.79|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:20|The fresh catalyst is TATT's Q2 2026 earnings release (Benzinga, 2026-08-05): Adjusted EPS of $0.35 beat the $0.30 estimate, and revenue of $52.94M significantly beat the $44.86M estimate — an ~18% revenue surprise. The August 2026 investor presentation (SEC 6-K filed today) reinforces the momentum narrative. Revenue growth is strong and the beat is material relative to the company's scale, though|TATT posted a material ~18% revenue beat ($52.94M vs. $44.86M estimate) and EPS beat ($0.35 vs. $0.30) in Q2 2026, indicating a multi-quarter revenue/earnings inflection that is idiosyncratic to the company, not driven by sector theme, policy, shortage, or new product launch.|Fresh, dated catalyst: Q2 2026 results released 2026-08-05 with revenue of $52.94M vs $44.86M consensus (~18% top-line surprise) plus an EPS beat, corroborated by a same-day SEC 6-K investor presentation — revenue is the load-bearing signal on a growth/backlog story and it is accelerating versus the $41.2M prior quarter. Materially significant for a $541M aerospace MRO name riding a record ~$580M backlog, and the 37x pre-market RVOL confirms the market repricing the growth trajectory. No explicit guidance raise in the evidence and no active theme/narrative cohort membership (defense/AI cohorts|The fresh catalyst is TATT's Q2 2026 earnings release (Benzinga, 2026-08-05): Adjusted EPS of $0.35 beat the $0.30 estimate, and revenue of $52.94M significantly beat the $44.86M estimate — an ~18% revenue surprise. The August 2026 investor presentation (SEC 6-K filed today) reinforces the momentum narrative. Revenue growth is strong and the beat is material relative to the company's scale, though no explicit guidance raise was cited in the available text, keeping this from "game_changer" territory.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-08-05, items ] EX-99.1 2 exhibit_99-1.htm EXHIBIT 99.1 Exhibit 99.1 INVESTOR PRESENTATION - August 2026 1