12391|PRGO|2026-08-05|live|MODERATE|54.0|13.17|strong|MODERATE|judge|other|1.00|08:10|Perrigo filed an 8-K (Item 2.02) on August 5, 2026 reporting Q2 2026 earnings, but the press release contains no specific revenue figures, EPS numbers, or quantified guidance — only qualitative commentary about "continued execution" of their Three-S plan and market share gains. Crucially, the company merely reaffirmed its full-year 2026 outlook rather than raising guidance, and the CEO explicitly |Reaffirmed guidance with no quantified beat, no EPS/revenue specifics, and CEO acknowledgment of "category softness and macroeconomic headwinds" is routine in-line earnings commentary with no concrete metrics or upside surprise—pedestrian company news that does not meet the bar for sales_acceleratio|The only fresh, dated catalyst is a Q2 2026 earnings release (8-K Item 2.02, Aug 5) that contains no quantified revenue, EPS, or raised guidance — merely a REAFFIRMED full-year outlook alongside management's admission of "ongoing category softness and macroeconomic headwinds." On a no-growth consumer self-care name, share-gain commentary plus divestiture/portfolio-streamlining boilerplate is not the revenue acceleration or guidance raise the rubric requires for HIGH. No theme or narrative cohort link exists, so the gap+RVOL is the market's vote on an in-line print rather than evidence of a mat|Perrigo filed an 8-K (Item 2.02) on August 5, 2026 reporting Q2 2026 earnings, but the press release contains no specific revenue figures, EPS numbers, or quantified guidance — only qualitative commentary about "continued execution" of their Three-S plan and market share gains. Crucially, the company merely reaffirmed its full-year 2026 outlook rather than raising guidance, and the CEO explicitly acknowledged results were "impacted by ongoing category softness and macroeconomic headwinds." Without concrete beat metrics (actual vs. consensus EPS/revenue) or an upward guidance revision, this does not clear the bar for a strong or game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-05, items 2.02,9.01] prgo-20260805 0001585364 false 0001585364 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 0001585364 prgo:OrdinaryShares0001ParValueMember 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 0001585364 prgo:A4.900SeniorNotesDueJune152030Member 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 0001585364 prgo:A6.125SeniorNotesDue2032Member 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 0001585364 prgo:A5.375SeniorNotesDue2032Member 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 0001585364 prgo:A5.30UnsecuredSeniorNotesDueNovember152043Member 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 0001585364 prgo:A49SeniorLoanDue2024Member 2026-08-05 2026-08-05 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 _______________________________________________ FORM 8-K ______________________________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 5, 2026 __________________________________ ____________ Perrigo Company plc (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) _______________________________________________ Commission file number 001-36353 Ireland Not Applicable (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) The Sharp Building, Hogan Place, Dublin 2, Ireland D02 TY74 + 353 1 7094000 (Address, including zip code, and telephone number, including area code, of registrant&#8217;s principal executive offices) Not Applicable (Former name or former address, if changed since last report) ________________________________________ Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the