12400|INSM|2026-08-06|live|HIGH|96.0|16.14|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:25|Insmed reported Q2 2026 earnings with total revenues of $425.5M, headlined by BRINSUPRI revenues of $309.2M — a stunning 49% sequential quarter-over-quarter growth — alongside a meaningful guidance raise: 2026 BRINSUPRI revenue guidance lifted to $1.25B–$1.40B. Additionally, the company raised its peak revenue estimate for its three lead programs to more than $14B total (BRINSUPRI >$7B, TPIP >$6B,|INSM's 49% sequential QoQ revenue acceleration on BRINSUPRI (flagship launch drug) with full-year guidance raise and substantially elevated peak revenue estimates ($14B total) represents a company-specific multi-quarter earnings inflection and beat-and-raise—idiosyncratic outperformance of its own p|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: an 8-K/EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-06 reporting Q2 revenue of $425.5M with BRINSUPRI at $309.2M (+49% sequential) plus a raised 2026 guidance range ($1.25B–$1.40B) and peak revenue estimates lifted to >$14B — exactly the revenue-acceleration-with-guidance-raise signal the rubric treats as load-bearing for growth names. Relative to a $21.5B biopharma, a flagship launch compounding ~50% Q/Q with guidance raised twice over is transformative, not a rounding error. No active theme or narrative cohort match (biopharma launch, not AI/defense/semis), so the grade rests entire|Insmed reported Q2 2026 earnings with total revenues of $425.5M, headlined by BRINSUPRI revenues of $309.2M — a stunning 49% sequential quarter-over-quarter growth — alongside a meaningful guidance raise: 2026 BRINSUPRI revenue guidance lifted to $1.25B–$1.40B. Additionally, the company raised its peak revenue estimate for its three lead programs to more than $14B total (BRINSUPRI >$7B, TPIP >$6B, ARIKAYCE >$1B), a significant upward revision that signals long-term conviction in the pipeline. For a $21.5B market cap biopharma, 49% QoQ revenue acceleration on its flagship launch drug combined w