12401|LFST|2026-08-06|live|HIGH|96.0|18.80|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:50|LifeStance reported Q2 2026 results with revenue of $435.4M (+26% YoY), Adjusted EBITDA of $66.0M (nearly doubling from $34.0M), and a swing to net income of $23.6M from a net loss of $3.8M — a compelling turnaround inflection. The company simultaneously raised full-year 2026 guidance, lifting revenue expectations to $1.685B–$1.725B and Adjusted EBITDA to $215M–$235M, and announced a fresh $100M s|LifeStance exhibits a multi-quarter revenue and profitability inflection—26% YoY growth, EBITDA near-doubling, a swing from net loss to profit, and raised full-year guidance—all idiosyncratic operational execution with no sector-wide theme, policy driver, or supply constraint evident.|Fresh, primary-source 8-K/EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-06 shows revenue +26% YoY to $435.4M with a raised FY26 revenue and EBITDA outlook — the load-bearing growth signal — plus adjusted EBITDA nearly doubling and a loss-to-profit flip confirmed by demand (visit volumes +19%, clinicians +11%), so the turnaround is structural rather than a one-time item. The simultaneous $100M buyback on a $4.0B cap is supportive but secondary. No active theme/narrative match, but revenue acceleration + guidance raise on a growth name is sufficient for HIGH/game_changer on its own.|LifeStance reported Q2 2026 results with revenue of $435.4M (+26% YoY), Adjusted EBITDA of $66.0M (nearly doubling from $34.0M), and a swing to net income of $23.6M from a net loss of $3.8M — a compelling turnaround inflection. The company simultaneously raised full-year 2026 guidance, lifting revenue expectations to $1.685B–$1.725B and Adjusted EBITDA to $215M–$235M, and announced a fresh $100M share repurchase program. The combination of accelerating 26% revenue growth, a structural loss-to-profit flip, a material guidance raise, and a buyback on a $4.0B market cap company clears the bar for a game-changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-06,