12421|MTW|2026-08-07|live|HIGH|50.4|33.08|routine|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|09:50|Manitowoc reported Q2 2026 results with orders up 56.1% YoY to $708.7M, backlog surging to over $1.0B, net sales up 10.3%, and Adjusted EBITDA up 85.9% YoY with 330bps margin expansion. Crucially, the company raised full-year 2026 guidance on both net sales ($2.3-2.4B vs prior $2.25-2.35B) and Adjusted EBITDA ($150-170M vs prior $125-150M) — a substantial upward revision. This combination of stron|Manitowoc delivered a multi-quarter revenue/earnings inflection (orders +56% YoY, Adjusted EBITDA +85.9% YoY with margin expansion) and raised full-year guidance substantially—a company-specific beat-and-raise with no sector theme, policy, or shortage driver; this is pure operational outperformance |Fresh, primary-source catalyst: an 8-K/EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-06 with Q2 results showing orders +56.1% YoY, backlog crossing $1.0B, sales +10.3%, adjusted EBITDA +85.9% with 330bps margin expansion, and a raised FY26 guide on BOTH revenue and EBITDA — the load-bearing combination of revenue/order acceleration plus a guidance raise. Relative to a $667M market cap, a $1.05B backlog and a $25M+ EBITDA guidance lift is transformative operating leverage, justifying promotion above the routine floor. Held at strong rather than game_changer because the name sits in no active theme or narrative cohort |Manitowoc reported Q2 2026 results with orders up 56.1% YoY to $708.7M, backlog surging to over $1.0B, net sales up 10.3%, and Adjusted EBITDA up 85.9% YoY with 330bps margin expansion. Crucially, the company raised full-year 2026 guidance on both net sales ($2.3-2.4B vs prior $2.25-2.35B) and Adjusted EBITDA ($150-170M vs prior $125-150M) — a substantial upward revision. This combination of strong revenue/order growth acceleration plus a meaningful guidance raise on a $510M market cap company is a textbook game_changer catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-06, items 2.02,9.01] 8-K false 0000061986 00000