12425|SLN|2026-08-10|live|MODERATE|84.0|18.83|strong|MODERATE|judge|pre_catalyst_anticipation|1.00|07:00|SLN gapped up on anticipation of its Phase 2 SANRECO topline readout for divesiran in polycythemia vera, with the company announcing a conference call to discuss the results on Monday, August 10, 2026. That near-term binary event is the clearest catalyst in the latest news flow.[1][3] The move also fits a broader rerating theme: investors are bidding the stock on optimism around Silence Therapeuti|The gap is driven by investor positioning ahead of an imminent but not-yet-released Phase 2 SANRECO topline readout for divesiran (with conference call scheduled for Aug 10, 2026), not a reaction to already-disclosed results—a textbook pre-announcement binary clinical catalyst.|The attributed driver is ANTICIPATION of a Phase 2 SANRECO readout, not a disclosed result — no actual data, no direct primary source, so there is no fresh material event, only a scheduled conference call. Anticipation of a binary event is not a Pradeep-class catalyst (no theme, policy, shortage, or sales acceleration), and the pipeline rerating/partner-search optionality is stale background. Verifiable content supports MODERATE at best; a confirmed positive topline would be re-graded much higher.|The gap is driven by anticipation of Silence Therapeutics' Phase 2 SANRECO topline readout for divesiran in polycythemia vera, with a conference call scheduled today (Aug 10, 2026) to discuss results. This is a binary clinical-data catalyst on the company's lead pipeline asset, which is highly material for a $564M biotech with no approved products — a positive readout could be transformative, though actual data details aren't yet confirmed in the summary, keeping it just shy of game_changer pending confirmed results. The prior ATM sales agreement (May 2026) and past earnings filing are stale background and not today's driver.|[Web summary] SLN gapped up on anticipation of its Phase 2 SANRECO topline readout for divesiran in polycythemia vera, with the company announcing a conference call to discuss the results on Monday, August 10, 2026. That near-term binary event is the clearest catalyst in the latest news flow.[1][3] The move also fits a broader rerating theme: investors are bidding the stock on optimism around Silence Therapeutics’ siRNA pipeline, especially divesiran, plus optionality from a strategic partner search for zerlasiran and the return of global rights to SLN312 after AstraZeneca discontinued that program.[1] In short, the gap was driven by a major clinical-data catalyst, not a macro move or general market factor.[1][3]
12426|ABCL|2026-08-10|live|HIGH|96.0|17.60|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:20|Fresh, concrete catalyst dated today (2026-08-10): AbCellera announced positive top-line Phase 2 results for ABCL635, a first-in-class non-hormonal NK3R antibody for moderate-to-severe menopausal vasomotor symptoms, showing "significant symptom reduction, improved sleep, and favorable tolerability." This is a clinical proof-of-concept win in a large, high-value indication (VMS/menopause market) fo|ABCL635 Phase 2 proof-of-concept in a large TAM (menopausal vasomotor symptoms) de-risks the company's lead asset and sets up a multi-quarter commercial inflection; this is an idiosyncratic clinical/pipeline catalyst for AbCellera, not shared by biotech peers generically, and not a new product launc|Fresh, date-confirmed binary catalyst: positive top-line Phase 2 data for ABCL635 released pre-market 2026-08-10, pre-announced by an 8-K/EX-99.1 on 8/7 — freshness and primary-source lineage are both established. For a $2.1B clinical-stage biotech, de-risking its lead internally-owned asset in the large non-hormonal VMS/menopause market is transformative relative to company size, and a 17.6% gap on 12.7x pre-market RVOL confirms the market is repricing the pipeline. No active theme or narrative cohort applies (the AI-chip cohort is unrelated), so the catalyst axis alone carries the HIGH/game_|Fresh, concrete catalyst dated today (2026-08-10): AbCellera announced positive top-line Phase 2 results for ABCL635, a first-in-class non-hormonal NK3R antibody for moderate-to-severe menopausal vasomotor symptoms, showing "significant symptom reduction, improved sleep, and favorable tolerability." This is a clinical proof-of-concept win in a large, high-value indication (VMS/menopause market) for a clinical-stage biotech with a $2.1B market cap, meaningfully de-risking the company's most advanced internally-owned pipeline asset. Positive Phase 2 data of this nature is a classic binary biotech catalyst that can re-rate the stock significantly, warranting game_changer classification.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-07, items 8.01,9.01] abcl-20260807 0001703057 false Vancouver BC 0001703057 2026-08-07 2026-08-07 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION WASHINGTON, D.C. 20549 __________________________________________ FORM 8-K __________________________________________ CURRENT REPORT PURSUANT TO SECTION 13 OR 15(d) OF THE SECURITIES EXCHANGE ACT OF 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 7, 2026 __________________________________________ AbCellera Biologics Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) __________________________________________ British Columbia 001-39781 Not Applicable (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification Number) 150 W 4th Avenue Vancouver , BC V5Y 1G6 (Address of registrant&#8217;s principal executive office) (Zip code) (604) 559-9005 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) (Former name or former address, if changed since last report) __________________________________________ Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: o Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) o Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) o Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) o Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common shares ABCL The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities