12430|BW|2026-08-11|live|HIGH|96.0|34.91|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:00|BW reported Q2 2026 results beating consensus on all key metrics: revenue of $319.7M (+130% YoY, ahead of street), net income of $14.3M vs a loss of $58.5M a year ago, EPS of $0.07 vs -$0.63, and adjusted EBITDA up 57%. This is a genuine loss-to-profit turnaround accompanied by strong revenue growth/acceleration (not just an EPS beat on flat revenue), backed by a 533% surge in backlog to $2.6B, a |BW exhibits a multi-quarter idiosyncratic revenue and earnings inflection (130% YoY revenue growth, loss-to-profit turnaround, 57% EBITDA growth) driven by company-specific backlog expansion and data-center-tied demand, not a shared industry theme or policy driver.|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: today's 8-K (items 2.02/7.01, dated 2026-08-10) with the Q2 press release showing revenue +130% YoY to $319.7M, loss-to-profit inflection ($14.3M net income vs -$58.5M), adjusted EBITDA +57%, and a raise — revenue-led, structural, not a one-time item. Backlog +533% to $2.6B versus a $1.3B market cap plus a $14B pipeline is transformative relative to company size and makes the earnings durable rather than a single-quarter anomaly. The incremental 1GW of Siemens Energy steam turbines explicitly "in anticipation of our next data center project" plugs BW into the li|BW reported Q2 2026 results beating consensus on all key metrics: revenue of $319.7M (+130% YoY, ahead of street), net income of $14.3M vs a loss of $58.5M a year ago, EPS of $0.07 vs -$0.63, and adjusted EBITDA up 57%. This is a genuine loss-to-profit turnaround accompanied by strong revenue growth/acceleration (not just an EPS beat on flat revenue), backed by a 533% surge in backlog to $2.6B, a $14B pipeline, new Siemens turbine orders tied to data center demand, a new $50M buyback authorization, and debt reduction (repurchase of remaining 2026 notes). The combination of explosive revenue growth, structural EPS inflection, guidance raise, and massive backlog/pipeline expansion relative to the $1.3B market cap makes this a game-changer catalyst, not a one-time anomaly.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-10, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] bw-20260810 0001630805 FALSE 0001630805 2026-08-10 2026-08-10 0001630805 us-gaap:CommonStockMember 2026-08-10 2026-08-10 0001630805 bw:SeniorNotes650Due2026Member 2026-08-10 2026-08-10 0001630805 us-gaap:SeriesAPreferredStockMember 2026-08-10 2026-08-10 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15 (d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 10, 2026 BABCOCK & WILCOX ENTERPRISES, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-36876 47-2783641 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 1200 East Market Street Suite 650 Akron, Ohio 44305 (Address of Principal Executive Offices) (Zip Code) Registrant&#8217;s Telephone Number, including Area Code: ( 330 ) 753-4511 Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of Each Class Trading Symbol Name of Each Exchange on which Registered Common stock, $0.01 par value per share BW New York Stock Exchange 6.50% Senior Notes due 2026 BWNB New York Stock Exchange 7.75% Series A Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock BW PRA New York St