12436|GLBE|2026-08-12|live|HIGH|72.0|10.67|game_changer|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|07:05|Fresh, concrete catalyst dated today (2026-08-12): GLBE beat Q2 estimates on both lines (adj. EPS $0.37 vs $0.22 est, revenue $299M vs $283.1M est) and, critically for this growth name, raised FY2026 revenue guidance meaningfully from $1.220B-$1.280B to $1.305B-$1.355B (vs $1.276B est), plus issued strong Q3 sales guidance of $308.5M-$315.5M vs $294.9M est. This is a genuine revenue acceleration w|Company-specific multi-quarter earnings inflection: GLBE beat Q2 EPS and revenue materially, raised full-year revenue guidance +$0.085B midpoint, and guided Q3 revenue +4.6% above consensus—a genuine idiosyncratic acceleration with no sector theme, policy, or shortage driver involved.|Fresh, dated (2026-08-12) earnings catalyst with the load-bearing signal for a growth name: revenue beat ($299M vs $283.1M) plus a meaningful FY2026 revenue guidance RAISE ($1.305-1.355B from $1.220-1.280B, above the $1.276B consensus) and above-consensus Q3 sales guide — not merely an EPS beat. That qualifies as a real, material HIGH catalyst on a $6.9B name. I trim from game_changer to strong because it is a clean beat-and-raise rather than a business-model-changing event, no theme/narrative cohort is joined, no direct primary source is present, and the web backdrop shows part of the move wa|Fresh, concrete catalyst dated today (2026-08-12): GLBE beat Q2 estimates on both lines (adj. EPS $0.37 vs $0.22 est, revenue $299M vs $283.1M est) and, critically for this growth name, raised FY2026 revenue guidance meaningfully from $1.220B-$1.280B to $1.305B-$1.355B (vs $1.276B est), plus issued strong Q3 sales guidance of $308.5M-$315.5M vs $294.9M est. This is a genuine revenue acceleration with a material guidance raise on a growth stock, not just an EPS beat, which is the strongest possible combination for a growth name's EP gap.|[Benzinga 2026-08-12] Global E Online Sees Q3 Sales $308.500M-$315.500M vs $294.861M Est. [Benzinga 2026-08-12] Global E Online Raises FY2026 Sales Guidance from $1.220B-$1.280B to $1.305B-$1.355B vs $1.276B Est. [Benzinga 2026-08-12] Global E Online Q2 Adj. EPS $0.37 Beats $0.22 Estimate, Sales $299.000M Beat $283.097M Estimate. [Web summary] GLBE’s gap-up appears to be driven mainly by positive analyst action and earnings anticipation, not a single fresh company-specific shock. The clearest immediate catalyst is Piper Sandler reiterating an Overweight rating with a $48 target on August 11, alongside broader analyst optimism into the upcoming Q2 print. [10][7] The stock was already building momentum before that: MarketBeat noted GLBE hit a new 1-year high on an analyst upgrade on August 5, and recent coverage has emphasized expectations for Q2 EPS of $0.22 on revenue of about $282.3 million, with cross-border GMV and fulfillment growth as the key metrics investors are watching. [14][7][1] Other supportive news in the backdrop includes Morgan Stanley’s earlier target raise to $44 even while downgrading the rating on valuation, plus the previously announced $500 million buyback and completion of the Passport acquisition, both of which reinforce the bullish long-term narrative. [6][5] If you want, I can also break down whether this looks like a true catalyst-driven gap or just a continuation move from analyst upgrades and pre-earnings positioning.
12437|WYFI|2026-08-12|live|MODERATE|84.0|17.34|strong|MODERATE|judge|management_change|1.00|07:20|Today's fresh filing is an 8-K disclosing a CFO transition — Erke Huang resigning as CFO/Director (moving to Senior Advisor) and Justin Zhu being appointed as new CFO effective August 1, 2026. This is a routine executive personnel change, not a financial or operational catalyst — no earnings figures, guidance, contract value, or approval is disclosed. The prior bridge facility (May 2026) and Q4/FY|A CFO transition (Erke Huang resigning, Justin Zhu appointed effective August 1, 2026) is a management-change event; however, this is a routine executive personnel shuffle with no indication of strategic repositioning, activist intervention, or leadership quality signal—lacking the "high-profile" di|The only fresh, dated item is the 8/12 Q2 print: revenue $28.8M vs $19.3M expected — a ~49% top-line beat on a $935M name, which is the load-bearing signal for a growth/AI-infrastructure story, though it comes with an EPS loss, no explicit guidance raise, and no direct primary source in evidence. The $160M contract and July 30 CFO/board reshuffle are stale, pre-gap background and cannot be the attributed driver; the 8-K is a routine personnel change. Revenue-driven beat plus an adjacent (not member) AI data-center narrative supports a solid catalyst, but the absence of a direct source and guid|Today's fresh filing is an 8-K disclosing a CFO transition — Erke Huang resigning as CFO/Director (moving to Senior Advisor) and Justin Zhu being appointed as new CFO effective August 1, 2026. This is a routine executive personnel change, not a financial or operational catalyst — no earnings figures, guidance, contract value, or approval is disclosed. The prior bridge facility (May 2026) and Q4/FY2025 preliminary revenue figures (Jan 2026) are stale background items, not today's catalyst. There is no concrete, material, fresh business catalyst here to justify a momentum gap-up.|[Benzinga 2026-08-12] Whitefiber Q2 EPS $(0.39) Beats $(0.41) Estimate, Sales $28.839M Beat $19.336M Estimate. [Web summary] WYFI’s latest gap-up appears to be tied to a fresh wave of investor attention on WhiteFiber’s AI/data-center growth story, with the most concrete recent catalyst being the company’s June announcement of a $160M+ computing infrastructure contract and the market’s continuing focus on that deal as a growth driver.[4][2] The immediate stock-specific headline before the current move was WhiteFiber’s July 30 management and board reshuffle, which markets generally read as a governance and execution reset rather than a negative event.[15] That said, the broader setup has been building for weeks around: WhiteFiber’s AI infrastructure contract momentum, especially the $160M+ deal[4] Progress on NC-1 capacity coming online and turning contracted demand into revenue[6] Expectations for Q2 results and commentary on billing ramp, cloud revenue, and additional capacity monetization[6][9] The stock had already been acting strongly into this period, with MarketWatch noting a prior August 3 move after the leadership transition and WhiteFiber up more than 50% year-to-date in MarketBeat’s tracking.[4][3] If you want, I can also break down whether today’s gap looks more like earnings speculation, analyst/flow-driven momentum, or a news catalyst tied to BTBT/WhiteFiber ownership.
12438|NBIS|2026-08-12|live|MODERATE|54.7|12.20|strong|MODERATE|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|08:00|Fresh catalyst today is Nebius' Q2 2026 print: revenue of $582.3M beat estimates ($572.7M), continuing the company's rapid AI-infrastructure growth trajectory, even though adjusted EPS loss of $(0.68) missed the $(0.62) estimate. Per the stated rule, on a growth name like NBIS revenue beat/acceleration matters more than the EPS miss (which reflects ongoing capex-heavy scaling, not a structural iss|NBIS delivered a Q2 revenue beat ($582.3M vs. $572.7M est.) within the context of sustained AI-infrastructure demand and multi-year compute deals, demonstrating company-specific earnings inflection rather than sector-wide theme participation—the beat validates idiosyncratic execution and capex-to-sc|The only fresh, dated driver is the Q2 print: a thin ~1.7% revenue beat ($582.3M vs $572.7M) paired with a WIDER-than-expected adjusted loss of $(0.68) vs $(0.62), and no disclosed guidance raise — that is a marginal top-line beat, not the revenue acceleration + raise combination that earns HIGH on a growth name. The genuinely transformative items cited (the >$1B Reflection AI compute deal, Nvidia's $2B warrant/9.3% stake) are undated prior-period news resurfacing in a web summary, and the Goldman pre-earnings note is sell-side opinion, not a company event; with no direct primary source, none |Fresh catalyst today is Nebius' Q2 2026 print: revenue of $582.3M beat estimates ($572.7M), continuing the company's rapid AI-infrastructure growth trajectory, even though adjusted EPS loss of $(0.68) missed the $(0.62) estimate. Per the stated rule, on a growth name like NBIS revenue beat/acceleration matters more than the EPS miss (which reflects ongoing capex-heavy scaling, not a structural issue). This is reinforced by strong sector positioning (large multi-year AI compute deals, Nvidia backing) that make the top-line beat particularly credible and material, though there's no explicit guidance raise disclosed here, so it falls short of game_changer.|[Benzinga 2026-08-12] Nebius Group N.V. - Class A Ordinary Shares Q2 Adj. EPS $(0.68) Misses $(0.62) Estimate, Sales $582.300M Beat $572.747M Estimate. [Benzinga 2026-08-10] Nebius Stock Trades 30% Above Its 200-Day Average Ahead of Wednesday's Earnings. Nebius Group shares are in the spotlight Monday ahead of the company&#39;s second-quarter earnings release scheduled for Wednesday. [Benzinga 2026-08-08] DA Davidson Maintains Neutral on Nebius Group, Lowers Price Target to $175. [Web summary] NBIS gapped up on a cluster of AI-infrastructure catalysts, with the biggest near-term driver being a bullish pre-earnings note from Goldman Sachs ahead of Nebius’s Q2 2026 report, which pushed the stock up about 5.4% in morning trading. The move was reinforced by sympathy buying in the neocloud group ahead of CoreWeave’s earnings and by elevated expectations for Nebius’s own results after very strong prior growth. [4][5] There are also bigger fundamental catalysts behind the stock’s recent strength: Nebius announced a multi-year deal to sell more than $1 billion of computing power to Reflection AI through 2029, and earlier reports noted NVIDIA-related support for Nebius, including a reported $2 billion pre-funded warrant investment and a disclosed 9.3% stake that previously sent the stock sharply higher. [1][2][13][14] So the latest gap-up was mainly an earnings/setup and sector momentum move, but the broader rally is being fueled by major AI demand, contract wins, and NVIDIA association. [1][4][5][10]
12439|BRUN|2026-08-12|live|none|60.0|12.04|strong|none|judge|other|1.00|08:55|Today's only fresh filing is an 8-K announcing the DATE of Boost Run's Q2 2026 earnings call (scheduled for Aug 14, 2026) — this is a mere scheduling announcement, not the actual results. There are no revenue, EPS, or guidance figures disclosed here, so no earnings beat/raise can be assessed yet. The prior MSA with Thinking Machines Lab (May 2026) and June investor presentation are stale backgroun|An 8-K announcing only the scheduling date of a future earnings call is a routine administrative disclosure with no concrete financial results, guidance, contract award, or material business update—classified as pedestrian company news with no measurable catalyst content.|The only fresh disclosure is an Item 7.01 8-K announcing the DATE of the Q2 call — a scheduling notice with zero revenue, EPS, or guidance content, so no earnings catalyst can be assessed. The Thinking Machines MSA and June deck predate the gap and cannot be the attributed driver; no direct source supports any new contract or theme entry. The 12% gap on 4.5x RVOL is therefore an UNIDENTIFIED driver — GPU-cloud/AI adjacency alone does not join the active power-infrastructure or chip-enablement cohorts, so it grades routine.|Today's only fresh filing is an 8-K announcing the DATE of Boost Run's Q2 2026 earnings call (scheduled for Aug 14, 2026) — this is a mere scheduling announcement, not the actual results. There are no revenue, EPS, or guidance figures disclosed here, so no earnings beat/raise can be assessed yet. The prior MSA with Thinking Machines Lab (May 2026) and June investor presentation are stale background, not today's catalyst. Without concrete new financial results or contract news dated today, this is classified as routine.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-10, items 7.01,9.01] false 0002090646 0002090646 2026-08-07 2026-08-07 0002090646 BRUN:ClassCommonStock0.0001ParValueMember 2026-08-07 2026-08-07 0002090646 BRUN:WarrantsE