12442|CRWV|2026-08-12|live|HIGH|51.6|19.51|routine|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.00|09:50|CoreWeave's fresh Q2 2026 8-K/press release (filed 8/11, ahead of today's gap) shows revenue more than doubling YoY to $2.575B from $1.212B, with Adjusted EBITDA up strongly to $1.51B (59% margin) from $753M. Most importantly, revenue backlog surged to ~$104B (plus >$25B of new customer commitments not yet included), signaling accelerating demand and a massive forward growth runway relative to the|CoreWeave delivered a multi-quarter revenue inflection—doubling YoY with $104B backlog and $25B+ new commitments—demonstrating company-specific demand acceleration and forward growth visibility idiosyncratic to CoreWeave's GPU infrastructure positioning, not a sector-wide theme or policy driver.|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: an 8-K/EX-99.1 dated 2026-08-11 reporting Q2 revenue of $2.575B, +112% Y/Y, with Adjusted EBITDA up ~2x and revenue backlog of ~$104B (plus >$25B not yet included) — revenue acceleration, the load-bearing signal for a growth name, not an EPS-only beat. Materiality is high even against a $58.4B cap since backlog approaches ~2x market cap, and the story joins the active AI data-center buildout narrative as the compute layer feeding it. Held at strong rather than game_changer because GAAP operating income and net income remain negative on heavy interest expense and|CoreWeave's fresh Q2 2026 8-K/press release (filed 8/11, ahead of today's gap) shows revenue more than doubling YoY to $2.575B from $1.212B, with Adjusted EBITDA up strongly to $1.51B (59% margin) from $753M. Most importantly, revenue backlog surged to ~$104B (plus >$25B of new customer commitments not yet included), signaling accelerating demand and a massive forward growth runway relative to the $49.3B market cap. Despite a GAAP net loss (driven by high interest expense on debt), the combination of explosive top-line growth and a backlog nearly 2x market cap is a genuine growth-stock catalyst — strong rather than game_changer since profitability metrics (operating margin, net loss) remain negative and there's no explicit guidance raise cited.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-11, items 2.02,9.01] crwv-20260811 FALSE 0001769628 0001769628 2026-08-11 2026-08-11 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 ___________________________________ FORM 8-K ___________________________________ CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (date of earliest event reported): August 11, 2026 ___________________________________ CoreWeave, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) ___________________________________ Delaware 001-42563 82-3060021 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification Number) 290 W Mt. Pleasant Ave. , Suite 4100 Livingston , NJ 07039 (Address of registrant's principal executive offices) (Zip Code) Registrant's telephone number, including area code: ( 973 ) 270-9737 ___________________________________ Not Applicable (Former name or former address, if changed since last report) ___________________________________ Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions (see General Instruction A.2. below): &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol Name of each exchange on which registered Class A Common Stock, $0.000005 par value