12450|BLSH|2026-08-13|live|MODERATE|54.0|12.40|routine|MODERATE|judge|other|1.00|09:55|Bullish's Q2 report shows a revenue beat ($92.6M vs $87.81M est) but an EPS miss ($0.09 vs $0.10 est), and the underlying financials show a net loss of $(280)M for the quarter (vs. a profit a year ago) driven by large non-cash swings in fair value of digital assets held — not a sustainable earnings inflection. Per the rules, an EPS miss/beat with no guidance raise and a company reporting a net los|Q2 revenue beat is offset by EPS miss and a $(280)M net loss driven by non-cash fair-value adjustments on digital assets—no earnings inflection or guidance raise; tokenized share launch is a novel product milestone but lacks disclosed revenue impact and is immaterial relative to $4.2B market cap, ma|The fresh, verifiable events are a Q2 print with a modest revenue beat but an EPS miss, no guidance raise, and a $(280)M quarterly net loss driven by non-cash digital-asset fair-value marks — the opposite of a sustainable inflection, and squarely disqualified as a HIGH earnings catalyst. The second driver, the first GFSC-regulated tokenized BLSH equity trades, is a genuinely novel product milestone but carries no disclosed volume or revenue and is immaterial against a $4.2B cap; no direct primary source is attached. It shares no story with the active AI data-center/power cohorts, so no theme o|Bullish's Q2 report shows a revenue beat ($92.6M vs $87.81M est) but an EPS miss ($0.09 vs $0.10 est), and the underlying financials show a net loss of $(280)M for the quarter (vs. a profit a year ago) driven by large non-cash swings in fair value of digital assets held — not a sustainable earnings inflection. Per the rules, an EPS miss/beat with no guidance raise and a company reporting a net loss due to crypto fair-value marks is not a game-changer; it's a routine print. The other cited catalyst — tokenized BLSH share trading launch on Bullish Exchange — is a novel product milestone but lacks disclose