12454|VERA|2026-08-14|live|HIGH|86.4|14.23|game_changer|HIGH|judge|policy|1.20|07:25|FDA granted accelerated approval of TRUTAKNA (atacicept) for adult IgA nephropathy patients at risk of progression, with alignment on an earlier ORIGIN 3 final efficacy analysis to support full approval and an sBLA planned for Q4 2026. This is a transformative regulatory event for a $2.1B clinical/commercial-stage biotech, converting VERA into a commercial company with the first and only dual BAFF|FDA accelerated approval of TRUTAKNA is a regulatory milestone (policy driver) that converts Vera into a commercial-stage company with a first-and-only dual BAFF/APRIL inhibitor in IgAN, positioning it for full approval via earlier ORIGIN 3 data and Q4 2026 sBLA.|Fresh, primary-source-verified 8-K/EX-99.1 dated Aug 10, 2026 discloses FDA accelerated approval and commercial launch of TRUTAKNA (first and only dual BAFF/APRIL inhibitor in IgAN), plus FDA alignment on an earlier ORIGIN 3 final efficacy readout in Q3 2026 and a Q4 sBLA — a company-defining conversion from clinical to commercial stage for a $2.1B biotech. This is regulatory/government-approval class, the strongest available catalyst for a pre-revenue biotech, and is fully transformative relative to market cap, so no demotion applies despite no theme/narrative cohort membership. The 14% gap o|FDA granted accelerated approval of TRUTAKNA (atacicept) for adult IgA nephropathy patients at risk of progression, with alignment on an earlier ORIGIN 3 final efficacy analysis to support full approval and an sBLA planned for Q4 2026. This is a transformative regulatory event for a $2.1B clinical/commercial-stage biotech, converting VERA into a commercial company with the first and only dual BAFF/APRIL inhibitor approved in IgAN — a clear game-changing, company-defining catalyst freshly disclosed in the Aug 10, 2026 8-K/press release.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-10, items 2.02,9.01] 8-K false 0001831828 0001831828 2026-08-10 2026-08-10 UNITED ST