12455|LPTH|2026-08-14|live|MODERATE|54.7|10.03|strong|MODERATE|judge|policy|1.20|09:10|Fresh, dated catalyst: Piper Sandler initiated coverage on LPTH on 2026-08-12 with an Overweight rating and $15 price target, a significant premium to trading levels, signaling strong institutional conviction. This is reinforced by a concurrent $11M follow-on order for infrared cameras tied to counter-UAS/defense demand, which is material relative to LPTH's scale (quarterly revenue ~$19M) and supp|An $11M counter-UAS/defense order from government or defense contractor is a policy-driven catalyst (federal defense contracting demand), reinforced by new analyst coverage validating the growing backlog in the defense IR optics space.|The only dated, verifiable event today is a Piper Sandler Overweight initiation — an analyst opinion, not a company event, which sits at the bottom of the Pradeep hierarchy and does not itself change the business. The $11M counter-UAS follow-on order would be meaningful for a ~$19M/quarter company, but it is undated and has no direct primary source, so it cannot be established as today's driver; the BlackDiamond/backlog storyline is a pre-existing narrative, not fresh news. No active theme or narrative cohort match (the live cohorts are AI data-center power, not defense IR optics), so I keep t|Fresh, dated catalyst: Piper Sandler initiated coverage on LPTH on 2026-08-12 with an Overweight rating and $15 price target, a significant premium to trading levels, signaling strong institutional conviction. This is reinforced by a concurrent $11M follow-on order for infrared cameras tied to counter-UAS/defense demand, which is material relative to LPTH's scale (quarterly revenue ~$19M) and supports the growing backlog narrative (backlog already at $110.6M per last earnings). The combination of a new bullish analyst initiation with a notable price target plus a fresh, sizable defense order is a credible, concrete, company-specific catalyst — not a game-changer (no earnings beat/guidance raise today), but strong enough to justify the gap given the analyst conviction and reinforcing order flow in the fast-growing defense IR optics business.|[Benzinga 2026-08-12] Piper Sandler Initiates Coverage On LightPath Technologies with Overweight Rating, Announces Price Target of $15. [Web summary] LPTH’s gap up appears to have been driven by a fresh defense-themed catalyst mix: Piper Sandler initiated coverage with an overweight rating, and the company also had a new $11 million follow-on order for infrared cameras tied to counter-UAS use, which reinforced the bull case around defense demand.[5][6] The stock’s move is also being supported by the broader LPTH story: analysts and market commentary have been highlighting its shift toward BlackDiamond, a germanium-free infrared optical material, along with improving operating momentum, growing backlog, and defense-related demand tied to supply-chain substitution in infrared systems.[1][2][12] In short, the latest gap-up catalyst was mainly the combination of new analyst coverage plus a defense order headline, while the longer-running narrative is LPTH’s transition into a higher-value defense IR optics supplier.[5][6][1]
12456|NMAX|2026-08-14|live|HIGH|100.8|16.75|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|09:50|Newsmax reported Q2 2026 record revenue of $54.1M (+16.5% YoY), broadcast revenue up 20.5% YoY, and its first profitable quarter as a public company (net income $2.9M, adj. EBITDA $5.7M). This combines revenue acceleration with a genuine profitability inflection, plus a new AI content licensing partnership with Meta and rapid growth in international licensing revenue (+344% YoY guided). Given the |Newsmax reported a multi-quarter revenue inflection (16.5% YoY top-line growth, 20.5% broadcast growth) combined with an idiosyncratic loss-to-profit turnaround driven by company-specific licensing revenue acceleration (+344% YoY) and a concrete Meta partnership, representing a structural earnings i|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: today's 8-K/EX-99.1 (2026-08-13) reports record Q2 revenue of $54.1M (+16.5% YoY, broadcast +20.5%) alongside the first profitable quarter as a public company — revenue growth plus a loss-to-profit inflection driven by structural licensing/broadcast demand, not one-time items. The new multi-year Meta AI content-licensing partnership and a guided +344% international licensing ramp add a credible AI-monetization angle, adjacent to (though not squarely inside) the active AI infrastructure cohorts. Material but not transformative for a $1.5B cap, so strong/HIGH hold|Newsmax reported Q2 2026 record revenue of $54.1M (+16.5% YoY), broadcast revenue up 20.5% YoY, and its first profitable quarter as a public company (net income $2.9M, adj. EBITDA $5.7M). This combines revenue acceleration with a genuine profitability inflection, plus a new AI content licensing partnership with Meta and rapid growth in international licensing revenue (+344% YoY guided). Given the concrete, freshly reported beat on both top-line growth and the loss-to-profit turnaround (with structural drivers like licensing growth, not one-time items), this qualifies as a strong catalyst for a name of this size ($1.5B market cap).|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-13, items 2.02,7.01,9.01] nmax-20260813 0002026478 false 0002026478 2026-08-13 2026-08-13 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 August 13, 2026 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported) NEWSMAX INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Florida 024-12567 99-2600308 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation or organization) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification Number) 750 Park of Commerce Drive , Suite 100 Boca Raton , Florida 33487 (Address of principal executive offices and zip code) ( 561 ) 686-1165 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligations of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Class B Common Stock, $0.001 par value per share NMAX New York Stock Exchange, LLC Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9746; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 2.02 - Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On August 13, 2026, Newsmax Inc. (the "Company") issued a press release announcing its results of operations for the three months and six months ended June 30, 2026. A copy of the press release is furnished as Exhibit 99.1 hereto and incorporated herein by reference. The information in Item 2.02 of this Form 8-K and in the press release attached as Exhibit 99.1 is being furnished and shall not be deemed "filed" for purposes of Section 18 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended (the "Exchange Act"), or otherwise subject to the liabilities of that Section. The information in each of Item 2.02 of this Form 8-K and Exhibit 99.1 shall not be incorporated by reference in any filing made by the Company or other document under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, or the Exchange Act, regardless of any general i
12457|STDN|2026-08-14|live|MODERATE|53.3|12.90|strong|MODERATE|judge|theme|1.20|09:55|STDN's gap-up is driven by a cluster of fresh, bullish analyst initiations on 2026-08-10: William Blair (Outperform), RBC Capital (Outperform, $11 PT), BofA Securities (Buy, $15 PT), and Stifel (Buy), all framing Standard Nuclear as the first-mover, scarcity-value play in U.S. TRISO fuel for the advanced/SMR reactor buildout. Multiple simultaneous initiations with price targets well above current |STDN's gap-up is driven by analyst recognition of its role as a first-mover, scarcity-value supplier of TRISO fuel within the sector-wide U.S. advanced/SMR reactor buildout—a structural tailwind shared across nuclear infrastructure and materials peers, not an idiosyncratic company-specific event.|The only concrete, dated events are a cluster of sell-side initiations (William Blair, RBC $11, BofA $15, Stifel) from 2026-08-10 — analyst opinion, not a company event, and stale relative to the gap; the fresh 8-K is a routine independent-director appointment, explicitly non-material. No contract, financing, guidance or revenue datapoint exists, so the true driver is effectively UNIDENTIFIED beyond broker sponsorship plus the live AI-data-center power/nuclear narrative cohort that STDN already belongs to, which lights the narrative axis only. Weak pre-market RVOL (1.11, 50th %ile) and no dire|STDN's gap-up is driven by a cluster of fresh, bullish analyst initiations on 2026-08-10: William Blair (Outperform), RBC Capital (Outperform, $11 PT), BofA Securities (Buy, $15 PT), and Stifel (Buy), all framing Standard Nuclear as the first-mover, scarcity-value play in U.S. TRISO fuel for the advanced/SMR reactor buildout. Multiple simultaneous initiations with price targets well above current levels from major banks is a legitimate, concrete catalyst (not a vague summary), though it's an initiation cluster rather than an earnings beat/guidance raise or transformative contract, so it fits "strong" rather than "game_changer." The 8-K board appointment (Seth Cohen) is routine governance news and not a price-moving catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-14, items 5.02,9.01] stdn-20260812 0002086716 0002086716 2026-08-12 2026-08-12 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 _________________ Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 12, 2026 STANDARD NUCLEAR, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 1-143400 99-3989746 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) 200 Europia Ave Oak Ridge , TN 37830 Registrant telephone number, including area code: ( 845 ) 258-0016 Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: o Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) o Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) o Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) o Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of Each Class Trading Symbol Name of Each Exchange on Which Registered Class A Common Stock, par value $0.00001 per share STDN The New York Stock Exchange Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging Growth Company &#9746; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. o Item 5.02 Departure of Directors or Certain Officers; Election of Directors; Appointment of Certain Officers; Compensatory Arrangements of Certain Officers. On August 12, 2026, the Board of Directors (the "Board") of Standard Nuclear, Inc. (the "Company") increased the size of the Board from four to five directors by increasing the number of Class II directors, and appointed Seth Cohen to serve in the resulting vacancy. He will also serve on the Company&#8217;s Compensation Committee. Mr. Cohen&#8217;s term expires at the 2028 annual meeting of stockholders, or until his successor is duly elected and qualified, or until his earlier death, resignation, disqualification or removal. The Board has determined that Mr. Cohen qualifies as an "independent director" under the listing standards of the New York Stock Exchange, including the additional independence requirements applicable to compensation committee members under Section 303A.02(a)(ii) and Rule 10C-1 under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as
12458|ARGX|2026-08-17|live|HIGH|86.4|10.53|game_changer|HIGH|judge|policy|1.20|07:20|Fresh, dated catalyst (2026-08-17): argenx's efgartigimod (Vyvgart) became the first Phase 3 therapy to show statistically significant, clinically meaningful improvement in IMNM (a myositis subtype with no approved treatments), from the ALKIVIA trial. This is a concrete, positive pivotal trial readout opening a first-in-class commercial opportunity in an indication with zero competition, meaningfu|Successful Phase 3 pivotal trial (ALKIVIA) demonstrating statistically significant efficacy in a previously untreated indication (IMNM) sets the regulatory pathway for FDA approval of efgartigimod in a first-in-class, zero-competition market, constituting a concrete policy/regulatory catalyst that m|Fresh, dated (2026-08-17) pivotal Phase 3 readout: efgartigimod is the first therapy to show statistically significant, clinically meaningful improvement in IMNM, an indication with no approved treatment — a concrete, verifiable, label-expanding clinical catalyst, the strongest class of biotech event. For a $53B biopharma this is not transformative in the way a micro-cap deal would be, but it materially widens Vyvgart's addressable market in its core franchise, so it stays material rather than merely minor. No active theme or narrative cohort join (rare-disease cohort is earnings-driven, not p|Fresh, dated catalyst (2026-08-17): argenx's efgartigimod (Vyvgart) became the first Phase 3 therapy to show statistically significant, clinically meaningful improvement in IMNM (a myositis subtype with no approved treatments), from the ALKIVIA trial. This is a concrete, positive pivotal trial readout opening a first-in-class commercial opportunity in an indication with zero competition, meaningfully expanding Vyvgart's addressable market for a $53B biopharma - a true game-changing clinical/regulatory catalyst, not a stale financing or M&A event.|[Benzinga 2026-08-17] Argenx's Efgartigimod Becomes First Phase 3 Therapy To Show Statistically Significant, Clinically Meaningful Improvement In IMNM, A Subtype With No Approved Treatment. [Benzinga 2026-08-10] Here’s How Much You Would Have Made Owning argenx Stock In The Last 5 Years. argenx (NASDAQ:ARGX) has outperformed the market over the past 5 years by 11.1% on an annualized basis producing an average annual return of 22.73%. Currently, argenx has a market capitalization of $54.18 billion. [Web summary] ARGX gapped up on a **positive Phase 3 readout for Vyvgart in autoimmune myositis**. The key catalyst was topline data from the **ALKIVIA** trial showing **statistically significant and clinically meaningful improvement** versus placebo, which the market is treating as a potential expansion of Vyvgart’s addressable market.[3][5] The move was amplified by the fact that autoimmune myositis currently has **no approved treatments** in that setting, so the data raised hopes for a *first-in-class* commercial opportunity.[3][5] There was also earlier support from a separate Argenx pipeline/valuation backdrop, including: - **Strong Q2 earnings** that beat expectations on both EPS and revenue.[9][10] - An announced **$2.2 billion acquisition of Forte Biosciences**, which added another immunology asset to the pipeline.[6][8] If you want, I can also break down whether the gap looks like a **one-day biotech reaction** or the start of a **multi-week re-rating** based on the data and valuation.
12459|CBRS|2026-08-17|live|none|60.0|12.78|strong|none|judge|pre_catalyst_anticipation|1.00|09:55|The gap-up appears driven by pre-earnings positioning, analyst commentary (UBS PT raise to $330, Wedbush reiteration citing speculative "next-gen chip" possibility), bullish options flow, and general AI-sector momentum/investor stake disclosures (Tiger Global, Ark Invest buying) — none of which are concrete company-specific catalysts with hard numbers. Critically, the actual Q2 2026 earnings print|The gap-up was driven by positioning and sentiment ahead of Q2 2026 earnings—analyst commentary, options flow, and investor stake disclosures—anticipating but not reacting to a concrete fundamental catalyst; the actual earnings print (revenue miss) later reversed the move, confirming the gap was spe|No fresh, company-specific driver exists: the move is pre-earnings positioning plus sell-side PT raises (UBS $330, Wedbush $280) and 13F-style stake disclosures (Tiger Global, Ark), none of which are concrete corporate events and all immaterial against a $59.3B cap. The only verifiable dated event — the Q2 2026 print — was mixed with a revenue miss and the stock reversed, so the driver is effectively UNIDENTIFIED/sentiment-based. AI-sector drift does not qualify as joining an active narrative cohort absent an actual deal or capacity/revenue disclosure, so demote from the MODERATE floor to rout|The gap-up appears driven by pre-earnings positioning, analyst commentary (UBS PT raise to $330, Wedbush reiteration citing speculative "next-gen chip" possibility), bullish options flow, and general AI-sector momentum/investor stake disclosures (Tiger Global, Ark Invest buying) — none of which are concrete company-specific catalysts with hard numbers. Critically, the actual Q2 2026 earnings print (the only fresh, verifiable event) reportedly showed mixed results with a revenue miss, and the stock reversed after reporting, confirming the pre-print rally was sentiment/positioning driven rather than a real fundamental catalyst. No dated, quantified guidance raise or contract materially large versus the $59.3B market cap is identified, so this is classified as routine.|[Benzinga 2026-08-14] Tiger Global Management Takes New Stake In Cerebras Systems Inc With 2,999,000 Shares. [Benzinga 2026-08-14] Cathie Wood Sells Palantir Stock After Blowout Earnings, Ark Invest Doubles Down on Cerebras Systems. Ark Invest sold roughly $7.9 million in Palantir shares on Thursday, Aug.13, 2026, while buying Cerebras stock. [Benzinga 2026-08-13] UBS Maintains Buy on Cerebras Systems, Raises Price Target to $330. [Web summary] CBRS gapped up mainly on a pre-earnings catalyst: traders were positioning ahead of Cerebras’s Q2 2026 results, with additional support from bullish analyst commentary, strong AI-infrastructure sentiment, and optimism around its growth pipeline.[4][8][14] The clearest latest news behind the move was Wedbush reiterating an Outperform rating and a $280 target, citing data-center capacity expansion, a widening partner roster, and the possibility of a next-generation chip announcement at an upcoming product event.[4][7] Market coverage also pointed to bullish options positioning and broad AI-sector strength as amplifiers of the rally.[4][7] If you mean the bigger follow-through catalyst after the gap, Cerebras later announced it was powering OpenAI’s “Ultrafast mode” for GPT-5.6 Sol, which reinforced the company’s inference story and likely helped sentiment around the stock.[20] One important caveat: the stock’s move was not driven by a single earnings release beat; the rally happened before the print, and subsequent reporting showed the stock reversed after the mixed Q2 results and revenue miss.[11][16][19]
12460|AMLX|2026-08-18|live|HIGH|96.0|21.33|game_changer|HIGH|judge|policy|1.00|07:20|Amylyx announced today (8/18/26) that its Phase 3 LUCIDITY trial of avexitide met its primary endpoint, with a 55% reduction in Level 2/3 hypoglycemic events vs. placebo in post-bariatric hypoglycemia — a concrete, positive, statistically-backed pivotal trial readout for a drug that already carries FDA Breakthrough Therapy designation. This is a transformative, de-risking event for a clinical-stag|A positive Phase 3 pivotal trial readout meeting its primary endpoint is a regulatory de-risking event that materially increases the probability of FDA approval (NDA filing pathway), constituting a government/regulatory milestone that transforms the risk profile of a clinical-stage biotech—this is a|Fresh, dated (8/18/26) pivotal Phase 3 LUCIDITY topline in post-bariatric hypoglycemia met its primary endpoint with a 55% reduction in Level 2/3 hypoglycemic events, confirmed by a pre-announced 8:00am readout and a news-pending trading halt — a binary, de-risking event for a clinical-stage biotech, not vague PR. For a $2.4B pre-revenue company with Breakthrough Therapy designation in an indication with no approved therapy, a successful pivotal readout is transformative relative to size and clears the path to an NDA. No active theme/narrative match (rare-disease cohort was earnings-beat drive|Amylyx announced today (8/18/26) that its Phase 3 LUCIDITY trial of avexitide met its primary endpoint, with a 55% reduction in Level 2/3 hypoglycemic events vs. placebo in post-bariatric hypoglycemia — a concrete, positive, statistically-backed pivotal trial readout for a drug that already carries FDA Breakthrough Therapy designation. This is a transformative, de-risking event for a clinical-stage biotech (market cap $2.4B) since it clears the primary hurdle toward a potential NDA filing/approval and commercialization, materially changing the risk/reward profile of the stock (trading halted pending the news, confirming its market-moving significance).|[Benzinga 2026-08-18] Trading Halt: Halted at 6:55:57 a.m. ET - Trading Halt: Halt News Pending. [Benzinga 2026-08-17] Amylyx Pharmaceuticals Stock Soars After the Close: Here's Why. Amylyx Pharmaceuticals shares are trading higher Monday after the company scheduled a Phase 3 trial results readout for this week. [Benzinga 2026-08-17] Amylyx Pharmaceuticals To Announce Phase 3 LUCIDITY Trial Topline Results For Avexitide In Post-Bariatric Hypoglycemia On August 18 At 8:00 a.m. ET. [Web summary] AMLX gapped up on a company-specific clinical catalyst: Amylyx said it would release top-line results from its Phase 3 LUCIDITY trial of avexitide on August 18, and the stock jumped on anticipation of that readout. The trial is for post-bariatric hypoglycemia, and avexitide already has FDA Breakthrough Therapy status for that use.[1][12] The move was also helped by broader bullish positioning into the data event, with analysts and recent commentary framing the LUCIDITY readout as the main near-term inflection point for the stock. Mizuho also lifted its price target to $30 ahead of the results, citing updated pricing assumptions for avexitide.[8][14] In plain terms: the gap-up was driven by traders bidding the stock higher into imminent Phase 3 avexitide data, not by a new earnings report or M&A headline.[1][8]
12461|MRNA|2026-08-19|live|HIGH|115.2|33.10|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:10|Today's fresh catalyst is the Phase 3 INTerpath-001 topline results (Merck/Moderna) showing intismeran autogene (individualized neoantigen therapy) plus KEYTRUDA achieved statistically significant and clinically meaningful improvements in RFS and DMFS vs KEYTRUDA alone in resected high-risk melanoma. This is a positive, concrete, company-specific Phase 3 readout for Moderna's lead oncology/persona|Positive Phase 3 topline readout on Moderna's lead oncology asset (intismeran autogene) is a company-specific clinical inflection validating the mRNA platform in a new therapeutic area, extending beyond vaccines into cancer therapeutics—not a theme/policy/shortage driver, and predates commercial rev|Fresh, dated (2026-08-19) wire release of Phase 3 INTerpath-001 topline showing statistically significant RFS/DMFS improvement for intismeran autogene + KEYTRUDA is a concrete, company-specific, platform-validating readout on Moderna's flagship oncology asset — clearly material for a $25B biotech whose valuation rests on mRNA beyond COVID, and consistent with the 33% gap on 14x pre-market RVOL. It stops short of game_changer because it is interim topline data with no approval, label, revenue or guidance impact yet, and no active theme/narrative cohort membership (the specialty-pharma earnings |Today's fresh catalyst is the Phase 3 INTerpath-001 topline results (Merck/Moderna) showing intismeran autogene (individualized neoantigen therapy) plus KEYTRUDA achieved statistically significant and clinically meaningful improvements in RFS and DMFS vs KEYTRUDA alone in resected high-risk melanoma. This is a positive, concrete, company-specific Phase 3 readout for Moderna's lead oncology/personalized cancer vaccine asset, a pipeline platform-validating event that extends mRNA beyond vaccines into oncology therapeutics - a major potential value driver for a $25B biotech. While not an approval or revenue event (still "topline" interim data, indication pending further steps), the magnitude of positive Phase 3 data on a flagship pipeline program is a strong catalyst; it doesn't reach game_changer status absent full data/approval or guidance impact, but qualifies as strong given the platform validation and market cap-relative significance. Note: the mFlusiva FDA approval and Ebola Phase 1 mentioned in the web summary are not dated today and are treated as background, not the fresh driver.|[Benzinga 2026-08-19] Merck And Moderna Announce Topline Results From The Phase 3 Interpath-001 Trial Evaluating Adjuvant Treatment With Intismeran Autogene In Combination With KEYTRUDA In Patients With Completely Resected Stage IIB-IV Melanoma; At A Pre-specified Interim Analysis, Intismeran In Combination With KEYTRUDA As Adjuvant Therapy Demonstrated Statistically Significant And Clinically Meaningful Improvements In RFS And DMFS Compared To KEYTRUDA Alone. [Web summary] MRNA’s latest gap up was driven by the FDA’s approval of Moderna’s first mRNA flu vaccine, mFlusiva, which gave the stock a fresh regulatory and commercial catalyst. Investors also reacted to FDA briefing materials ahead of the vaccine committee meeting that were interpreted as supportive of the benefit-risk profile, reinforcing the move. [3][4][6][20] The key near-term catalyst is not a new COVID revenue story; it is Moderna proving it can expand its mRNA platform into flu and other respiratory vaccines, which is why the approval mattered so much to the market. The stock had already been moving on the expectation of that regulatory milestone, and the gap reflected follow-through buying after the decision became public. [3][6][14] There was also secondary support from news that Moderna began Phase 1 work on an Ebola vaccine candidate, but that looks more like a pipeline-positive backdrop than the main driver of the gap. The flu-vaccine approval is the primary reason. [2][3][16]
12462|MRVL|2026-08-19|live|HIGH|69.1|11.38|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|08:50|The fresh catalyst is the 8-K/Benzinga disclosure of an expanded commercial agreement between Marvell and Google, under which Marvell will develop a broad suite of custom silicon (AI inference accelerators, storage controllers, NICs, memory interface controllers, near-memory compute) attaching to Google's TPU ecosystem. This is a major, multi-year hyperscaler design-win expansion with a top-tier A|Major, multi-year hyperscaler design-win expansion with Google for custom silicon across AI inference, storage, and memory domains—a company-specific revenue inflection driver idiosyncratic to Marvell, not a sector-wide theme or policy event.|Fresh, primary-source catalyst: an 8-K filed 2026-08-19 (event 8/18) disclosing an expanded Google commercial agreement across the TPU ecosystem, with a warrant vesting in 240 tranches per $500M of custom-silicon revenue — an implied ~$120B multi-year revenue umbrella against a ~$10B run-rate, transformative even for a $194B cap. This is a top-of-hierarchy AI-infrastructure/hyperscaler-capex theme catalyst (theme > policy > ...), company-specific and concrete rather than the pre-earnings/sector-rotation narrative in the web summary. Warrant dilution and absence of updated guidance are the only|The fresh catalyst is the 8-K/Benzinga disclosure of an expanded commercial agreement between Marvell and Google, under which Marvell will develop a broad suite of custom silicon (AI inference accelerators, storage controllers, NICs, memory interface controllers, near-memory compute) attaching to Google's TPU ecosystem. This is a major, multi-year hyperscaler design-win expansion with a top-tier AI customer, evidenced by Google receiving warrants tied to up to $120B of potential custom silicon revenue (240 tranches x $500M) — a very large figure relative to Marvell's ~$194B market cap and current ~$10B annual revenue run-rate, making this a materially bullish, company-specific catalyst rather than routine news. It falls short of game_changer because there are no updated financial guidance figures or immediate earnings beat attached, and the warrant issuance (dilutive, tied to revenue milestones) tempers the pure upside, but the strategic partnership expansion with Google is a strong, concrete, and highly material catalyst for a custom silicon/AI infrastructure name like MRVL.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-19, items 1.01,3.02,9.01] 8-K false 0001835632 0001835632 2026-08-18 2026-08-18 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report: August 18, 2026 (Date of earliest event reported) MARVELL TECHNOLOGY, INC. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) Delaware 001-40357 85-3971597 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 1000 N. West Street , Suite 1200 Wilmington , Delaware 19801 (Address of principal executive offices, including Zip Code) (302) 295-4840 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading Symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, par value $0.002 per share MRVL The Nasdaq Global Select Market Indicate by check mark