company-specific catalysts: Tempus AI raised its 2026 revenue guidance after a stronger Q2, and investors have been digesting the newly approved tumor-only xT companion diagnostic, which could lift pricing and add meaningful revenue starting in 2027.[2][9] The most immediate news flow also includes: Tempus announced the clinical launch of the ArteraAI Prostate Test for metastatic hormone-sensitive prostate cancer, expanding its oncology menu.[6] Tempus received FDA 510(k) clearance for its RNA-based xR IVD sequencing assay, which broadens its precision-oncology platform.[1] Tempus has also been in the headlines for the Personalis acquisition and other commercial/clinical updates, which have kept the stock active.[9][16] If you mean “what specifically caused today’s gap,” the highest-probability trigger is a bullish reaction to the combination of upgraded guidance plus the FDA-related pricing and product-expansion catalysts, rather than one single headline.[2][9][1]
