the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 8.01 Other Events. On August 19, 2026, Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc. (&#8220;Ultragenyx&#8221; or the &#8220;Company&#8221;) announced the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (the &#8220;FDA&#8221;) granted accelerated approval for GENGLYCOS&#153; (pariglasgene brecaparvovec-opnr), also known as DTX401, in adult and pediatric patients eight years and older with glycogen storage disease type Ia (GSDIa). Clinical Program and Post-Marketing Study Requirements Supporting Accelerated Approval of GENGLYCOS The approval of GENGLYCOS is based on positive data from the 48-week randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled Phase 3 GlucoGene study which treated 46 participants aged eight years and older with DTX401 (1.0 x 10&#x5E;13 GC/kg dose) or placebo, showing a reduction in the cornstarch requirements in the treated group (p&lt;0.001). There were 44 participants in the mod
12466|BULL|2026-08-20|live|HIGH|100.8|15.16|strong|HIGH|judge|sales_acceleration|1.20|07:10|Webull reported Q2 2026 results with a clear beat-and-turnaround: revenue of $198.8M (+51% YoY, +24% sequentially) beat estimates of $181.3M, and adjusted EPS of $0.12 beat the $0.03 estimate. Critically, this is a growth-plus-turnaround story — the company swung from a net loss of $28.3M a year ago to net income of $24.4M, with adjusted operating margin expanding to 31.5% from prior-year levels, |Webull delivered a company-specific multi-quarter revenue/earnings inflection (51% YoY, +24% QoQ growth, profit swing from -$28.3M to +$24.4M) with structured operating leverage (margin expansion to 31.5%), driven by idiosyncratic factors (PDT rule elimination benefiting this platform, international|Fresh, primary-sourced catalyst: an SEC 6-K dated 2026-08-19 with Q2 revenue of $198.8M, +51% Y/Y and +24% sequential — real revenue acceleration, the load-bearing signal for a growth name, not an EPS-only beat. The profitability inflection (net loss $28.3M → net income $24.4M, 31.5% adj. operating margin) is structurally driven by the June 4 PDT-rule elimination lifting active-trader volumes plus international/institutional expansion, not a one-time item, so it survives the CBRL test. No guidance raise and no active theme/narrative membership caps it at strong rather than game_changer; materi|Webull reported Q2 2026 results with a clear beat-and-turnaround: revenue of $198.8M (+51% YoY, +24% sequentially) beat estimates of $181.3M, and adjusted EPS of $0.12 beat the $0.03 estimate. Critically, this is a growth-plus-turnaround story — the company swung from a net loss of $28.3M a year ago to net income of $24.4M, with adjusted operating margin expanding to 31.5% from prior-year levels, driven by structural drivers (PDT rule elimination boosting active trader volumes, international expansion, new AI product Vega Analyst) rather than a one-time item. Stock is up ~9% pre-market on this earnings-driven, company-specific catalyst, meeting the bar for "strong" given the combination of accelerating revenue growth and a credible profitability inflection, though not quite "game changer" absent an explicit forward guidance raise.|[SEC 6-K filed 2026-08-19, items ] EX-99.1 2 ea030257601ex99-1.htm PRESS RELEASE DATED AUGUST 19, 2026 Exhibit 99.1 Webull Reports Second Quarter 2026 Financial Results Webull reports another strong quarter of growth, marked by record trading volumes, increased customer assets, and strong net deposits. Webull continues to invest in strategic priorities, including enhanced offerings for its active traders, international expansion, and building its institutional business. ST. PETERSBURG, Fla., August 19, 2026 /PRNewswire/ &ndash; Webull Corporation (NASDAQ: BULL) (&ldquo;Webull&rdquo; or the &ldquo;Company&rdquo;) today announced financial and operating results for the second quarter ended June 30, 2026. &ldquo;I&rsquo;m proud to report a record second quarter for Webull, highlighted by our successful implementation of updated active trader functionality following the June 4 elimination of the Pattern Day Trader Rule,&rdquo; said Anthony Denier, Group President and U.S. CEO. &ldquo;Webull&rsquo;s advanced technology platform enabled eligible customers to fully leverage the new trading environment from day one, contributing to record trading volumes and strong customer engagement. We also made significant progress in executing on our 2026 roadmap, including expanding our AI capabilities with the launch of Vega Analyst, extending our global footprint, and scaling our institutional business. We believe these investments are strengthening Webull&rsquo;s position as a leading platform for active traders seeking access to investment opportunities across global markets and asset classes.&rdquo; &ldquo;Q2 was the best quarter in Webull&rsquo;s history, with record revenue of $198.8 million, up 51% year-over-year and 24% sequentially,&rdquo; said H.C. Wang, Chief Financial Officer of Webull. &ldquo;Adjusted operating profit reached $62.6 million, representing a 31.5% operating margin, while adjusted net income was $43.2 million. These results demonstrate the operating leverage inherent in our platform and the potential for further margin expansion.&rdquo; Second Quarter Results Financial Results &#9679; Total revenues increased 51% year-over-year to $198.8 million. &#9679; Trading-related revenue increased 66% year-over-year to $147.7 million. &#9679; Total operating expenses increased 13% year-over-year, primarily driven by higher brokerage and transaction costs associated with rapid growth in trading volumes as well as product expansion, offset by lower share-based compensation expense. &#9679; Adjusted operating expenses increased 26% year-over-year to $136.2 million. &#9679; Income before income taxes totaled $34.7 million for the quarter, compared to a loss before taxes of $21.4 million for the prior year comparative quarter. The increase of $56.1 million in income was primarily due to total revenues growing 51%, which outpaced the 13% increase in total operating expenses. &#9679; Adjusted operating profit totaled $62.6 million for the quarter, compare
12467|SCSC|2026-08-20|live|none|96.0|20.58|strong|none|judge|unknown|1.00|09:25|The only fresh, dated filing today is an 8-K disclosing a single board member's retirement (Peter C. Browning) — a routine governance item with no financial or business impact. The other cited items (Pzena stake disclosure, Northcoast downgrade, prior credit agreement, prior earnings) are either not company-specific catalysts, are negative/neutral, or predate today's gap and are explicitly backgro|The only fresh filing is a routine board member retirement with no financial or business impact; no earnings beat, guidance raise, contract, approval, or sector-wide driver identified despite the gap-up move.|The only fresh, dated disclosure is an 8-K on a single director's retirement — routine governance with zero financial or business impact for a $1.0B distributor. Everything else cited (13F/Pzena stake, a Northcoast downgrade, prior earnings/credit agreement) is either non-company-specific, negative, or predates the gap, so the driver is UNIDENTIFIED. No theme or narrative-cohort story is joined, so the 20.6% gap plus 5x RVOL is only the market's vote and cannot carry HIGH on its own.|The only fresh, dated filing today is an 8-K disclosing a single board member's retirement (Peter C. Browning) — a routine governance item with no financial or business impact. The other cited items (Pzena stake disclosure, Northcoast downgrade, prior credit agreement, prior earnings) are either not company-specific catalysts, are negative/neutral, or predate today's gap and are explicitly background. No concrete fresh earnings beat, guidance raise, contract, or approval was identified, so this gap lacks a verifiable, material company-specific catalyst.|[SEC 8-K filed 2026-08-17, items 5.02,9.01] scsc-20260811 August 11, 2026 0000918965 false 0000918965 2026-08-11 2026-08-11 UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 Form 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 or 15(d) of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported): August 11, 2026 ScanSource, Inc. (Exact name of registrant as specified in its charter) SC 00-26926 57-0965380 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (IRS Employer Identification No.) 6 Logue Court , Greenville , SC 29615 (Address of principal executive offices, including zip code) 864 - 288-2432 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Title of Each Class Trading Symbol Name of Each Exchange on Which Registered Common Stock, no par value SCSC NASDAQ Global Select Market Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Indicate by check mark whether the registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934. Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 5.02. Departure of Directors or Certain Officers; Election of Directors; Appointment of Certain Officers; Compensatory Arrangements of Certain Officers. On August 11, 2026, Peter C. Browning, who has served on the Company's Board of Directors (the "Board") since 2014, notified the Board of his retirement from the Board as of August 12, 2026. Upon Mr. Browning&#8217;s retirement, the Board decreased in size to seven seats. This transition is not a result of any disagreement between Mr. Browning and the Company. The full text of the press release announcing Mr. Browning&#8217;s retirement is furnished as Exhibit 99.1 to this report and shall not be deemed "filed" for purposes of Section 18 of the Exchange Act or otherwise subject to the liabilities of that section, nor shall it be deemed incorporated by reference in any other filing under the Securities Act of 1933 or the Exchange Act. Item 9.01. Financial Statements and Exhibits. (d) Exhibits Exhibit Number Description 99.1 Press release 104 Cover Page Interactive Data File (embedded within the Inline XBR
12468|UUUU|2026-08-21|live|HIGH|51.6|9.28|strong|HIGH|judge|new_product|1.20|09:55|Concrete, fresh operational catalyst: Energy Fuels announced its terbium oxide from White Mesa Mill passed all qualifications for commercial use by one of the world's largest (Japan-based) rare earth permanent magnet makers outside China, meaning no further validation is needed. This de-risks the company's heavy rare earth "mine-to-magnet" strategy and represents a meaningful commercial milestone |Energy Fuels achieved commercial qualification of its terbium oxide product from White Mesa Mill by a major international rare earth magnet manufacturer, removing validation risk and de-risking a TAM-expanding heavy rare earth processing strategy that was previously uncertain.|Fresh, dated (2026-08-19) wire-confirmed operational catalyst: UUUU's terbium oxide passed all qualifications with a top non-China permanent-magnet maker, de-risking the heavy-rare-earth "mine-to-magnet" strategy for a $3.8B name whose REE segment is pre-revenue — a genuine commercial-validation inflection rather than boilerplate PR. This sits squarely in the hot rare-earth / China-supply-shortage + Western-supply-chain policy theme, which is Pradeep's second- and third-strongest catalyst class, and is reinforced by the ASM acquisition shareholder approval and a fresh BMO Outperform initiation|Concrete, fresh operational catalyst: Energy Fuels announced its terbium oxide from White Mesa Mill passed all qualifications for commercial use by one of the world's largest (Japan-based) rare earth permanent magnet makers outside China, meaning no further validation is needed. This de-risks the company's heavy rare earth "mine-to-magnet" strategy and represents a meaningful commercial milestone for its REE segment, reinforced by a fresh BMO Capital Outperform initiation ($18 PT) and progress on the ASM acquisition. While not a quantifiable revenue/earnings event, it's a material, verifiable strategic validation for a still-early-stage REE business, warranting a "strong" classification rather than routine.|[Benzinga 2026-08-19] Energy Fuels' Terbium Oxide Has Passed All Qualifications For Use By One Of The World's Largest Rare Earth Permanent Magnets Makers Outside Of China. [Benzinga 2026-08-14] BMO Capital Initiates Coverage On Energy Fuels with Outperform Rating, Announces Price Target of $18. [Web summary] UUUU gapped up on a fresh operational catalyst: Energy Fuels said its terbium oxide from White Mesa Mill passed all qualifications for use by one of the world’s largest Japan-based rare earth permanent magnet manufacturers, meaning it is now approved for commercial production with no further validation required. The stock also got a tailwind from the broader market interpretation that this de-risks Energy Fuels’ heavy rare earth “mine-to-magnet” strategy. [3][4][6] The move is consistent with the price action: shares were already up more than 5% on the session after the announcement and were tracking a larger August rebound. [3][6] A secondary positive headline came from the Australian Strategic Materials acquisition: ASM shareholders approved the deal, clearing another milestone toward closing, which supports Energy Fuels’ vertical integration plan. [5][2] There was also an analyst upgrade from BMO Capital Markets to “strong buy” around the same period, but the immediate gap-up catalyst was the terbium qualification news. [7]
